1
00:00:02,560 --> 00:00:03,392
Ho Bin to serve.

2
00:00:03,393 --> 00:00:04,333
(The match continues.)

3
00:00:04,587 --> 00:00:05,587
(Yoon Ha passes.)

4
00:00:05,733 --> 00:00:06,773
Yoon Ha with the pass!

5
00:00:06,798 --> 00:00:07,912
(Tsubaki sets it up.)

6
00:00:08,587 --> 00:00:10,021
(Yoon Ha hammers it down.)

7
00:00:13,287 --> 00:00:14,515
Nice!

8
00:00:14,540 --> 00:00:15,749
The youngest duo on the court,

9
00:00:15,774 --> 00:00:18,721
both born in 2007, combine for the point.

10
00:00:19,654 --> 00:00:20,853
Yeong Hye, you have to jump.

11
00:00:20,854 --> 00:00:22,320
Why are you coming up so far on defense?

12
00:00:22,321 --> 00:00:24,186
Ho Bin, the ball dropped.

13
00:00:24,187 --> 00:00:25,454
Why did you step up so far?

14
00:00:26,433 --> 00:00:27,394
That was a mistake.

15
00:00:29,017 --> 00:00:32,083
What did you think of that play
by the two players...

16
00:00:32,084 --> 00:00:32,983
born in 2007?

17
00:00:32,984 --> 00:00:35,102
Let's ask Hyo Jin, who went pro in 2007.

18
00:00:36,751 --> 00:00:38,251
When you put it like that...

19
00:00:38,617 --> 00:00:40,150
That makes me feel a little old.

20
00:00:40,151 --> 00:00:40,984
I'm sorry.

21
00:00:48,617 --> 00:00:49,751
- Chae Min.
- Yeah?

22
00:00:51,855 --> 00:00:53,603
(During the previous timeout)

23
00:00:53,628 --> 00:00:55,750
You need to hit right over Tsubaki.

24
00:00:55,751 --> 00:00:57,224
She can only reach this high.

25
00:00:58,715 --> 00:01:01,381
(Tsubaki has a relatively low block.)

26
00:01:02,081 --> 00:01:04,781
(They're targeting Tsubaki.)

27
00:01:05,428 --> 00:01:06,561
Let's try that again!

28
00:01:10,115 --> 00:01:11,615
(She calls for a short serve.)

29
00:01:12,115 --> 00:01:13,415
(Got it!)

30
00:01:14,148 --> 00:01:15,180
Serve.

31
00:01:15,181 --> 00:01:16,242
Yoon Ha serves.

32
00:01:18,915 --> 00:01:20,147
She disrupts their receive.

33
00:01:20,148 --> 00:01:20,915
(The ball goes to Chae Min.)

34
00:01:21,062 --> 00:01:22,428
Just hit it from up high!

35
00:01:22,453 --> 00:01:23,417
High contact!

36
00:01:24,515 --> 00:01:25,881
(It grazes her fingertips.)

37
00:01:26,575 --> 00:01:27,908
A spike!

38
00:01:28,001 --> 00:01:29,322
And it's off the block and out.

39
00:01:29,867 --> 00:01:31,625
That's it!

40
00:01:31,650 --> 00:01:33,515
(The strategy to target Tsubaki pays off.)

41
00:01:33,875 --> 00:01:34,708
No.

42
00:01:35,128 --> 00:01:36,096
It touched my hand.

43
00:01:37,281 --> 00:01:39,214
(So close.)

44
00:01:39,215 --> 00:01:43,136
Chae Min has a high contact point
and plenty of power,

45
00:01:43,247 --> 00:01:45,438
so she excels at hitting
over the block like that.

46
00:01:46,587 --> 00:01:49,398
(Chae Min subbed in early
in the third set.)

47
00:01:50,548 --> 00:01:52,548
(Contributing on both offense and defense)

48
00:01:53,915 --> 00:01:56,048
(She's been the spark
behind her team's scoring run.)

49
00:01:56,581 --> 00:02:00,815
(Pohang Sports Council's secret weapon)

50
00:02:01,448 --> 00:02:02,881
(Peeking)

51
00:02:03,515 --> 00:02:05,481
Serve deep to the left, toward Min Kyeong.

52
00:02:06,248 --> 00:02:10,081
(Min Kyeong is the next target.)

53
00:02:11,248 --> 00:02:13,015
The score is 17 to 15, a two-point lead.

54
00:02:15,281 --> 00:02:16,281
Tough pass.

55
00:02:17,594 --> 00:02:18,872
Young In chases it down.

56
00:02:19,848 --> 00:02:21,174
She just sends a free ball over.

57
00:02:22,815 --> 00:02:23,947
Cross-court.

58
00:02:23,948 --> 00:02:24,944
Go for the swing.

59
00:02:25,381 --> 00:02:26,414
The set goes to Hyeon Ju!

60
00:02:26,415 --> 00:02:27,414
And she puts it away.

61
00:02:27,948 --> 00:02:29,915
(A pinpoint cross-court shot)

62
00:02:30,115 --> 00:02:31,481
Nice.

63
00:02:32,594 --> 00:02:33,848
(The match continues.)

64
00:02:34,648 --> 00:02:35,622
Back C!

65
00:02:35,940 --> 00:02:38,015
(Chae Min on the right?)

66
00:02:40,415 --> 00:02:42,281
- Hit it! Just swing!
- Swing!

67
00:02:42,715 --> 00:02:44,948
Chae Min crushes it from the right side!

68
00:02:45,481 --> 00:02:46,281
No.

69
00:02:47,315 --> 00:02:48,334
Where was the block?

70
00:02:50,881 --> 00:02:52,980
(Chae Min keeps leading the charge.)

71
00:02:52,981 --> 00:02:55,747
Chae Min has been swinging...

72
00:02:55,748 --> 00:02:58,647
- aggressively from both pins.
- Yes.

73
00:02:58,648 --> 00:03:01,147
This is exactly what Coach Yun Hye
was hoping for, isn't it?

74
00:03:01,148 --> 00:03:03,515
Pohang Sports Council pulls within one.

75
00:03:04,948 --> 00:03:06,748
She used to play
for the Pink Spiders, right?

76
00:03:08,081 --> 00:03:11,080
(A formidable hitter with pro experience)

77
00:03:11,081 --> 00:03:12,915
How will Chae Min's serve play out?

78
00:03:14,615 --> 00:03:17,915
(They can't afford
to give up another point.)

79
00:03:18,048 --> 00:03:18,915
Serve.

80
00:03:22,848 --> 00:03:23,780
Yoon Ha passes.

81
00:03:23,781 --> 00:03:25,081
(The pass is off.)

82
00:03:25,835 --> 00:03:27,102
Tsubaki keeps it alive.

83
00:03:27,481 --> 00:03:28,508
Back-row off-speed hit.

84
00:03:29,315 --> 00:03:30,114
Chae Min with the dig.

85
00:03:30,115 --> 00:03:30,881
Yours.

86
00:03:31,948 --> 00:03:32,912
Gyeong Hyeon.

87
00:03:34,715 --> 00:03:35,581
It's sent back.

88
00:03:35,881 --> 00:03:37,315
Hyeon Ju with the tip!

89
00:03:37,757 --> 00:03:38,856
- Kept it alive!
- It's up.

90
00:03:38,881 --> 00:03:40,115
(They scramble to send it back over.)

91
00:03:40,815 --> 00:03:41,914
Where will the set go?

92
00:03:41,915 --> 00:03:43,280
She pushes it to the left.

93
00:03:43,281 --> 00:03:44,915
- Go in!
- Aim high!

94
00:03:45,715 --> 00:03:47,947
Gyeong Hyeon hammers it down!

95
00:03:47,948 --> 00:03:50,015
I told you to aim for the seam.

96
00:03:51,015 --> 00:03:53,048
And we're all tied up at 18 to 18.

97
00:03:56,215 --> 00:03:58,380
Gyeong Hyeon scores again,

98
00:03:58,381 --> 00:04:00,614
and Pohang's trio, Chae Min,
Hyeon Ju, and Gyeong Hyeon,

99
00:04:00,615 --> 00:04:03,315
have completely shifted the momentum.

100
00:04:05,381 --> 00:04:07,347
Yoon Ha, it's not that hard.

101
00:04:07,348 --> 00:04:09,115
Just take one more step
to get behind the ball.

102
00:04:10,048 --> 00:04:12,215
- Min Kyeong, hit it deep.
- Got it.

103
00:04:12,781 --> 00:04:14,748
(She immediately calls a play
for Min Kyeong.)

104
00:04:14,948 --> 00:04:15,815
Serve.

105
00:04:16,381 --> 00:04:17,714
All tied up.

106
00:04:17,715 --> 00:04:18,758
Chae Min serves.

107
00:04:21,317 --> 00:04:22,723
Tsubaki gets back for the pass.

108
00:04:22,748 --> 00:04:23,781
(The ball goes to Min Kyeong.)

109
00:04:24,548 --> 00:04:26,580
Min Kyeong with a massive spike!

110
00:04:26,605 --> 00:04:28,405
- Nice!
- Way to go!

111
00:04:29,192 --> 00:04:30,723
(They manage to side out.)

112
00:04:30,748 --> 00:04:31,881
Nice!

113
00:04:32,748 --> 00:04:34,348
Nice, Min Kyeong!

114
00:04:37,481 --> 00:04:39,348
(Scanning the court)

115
00:04:41,724 --> 00:04:42,956
(Coach calls to serve at number four.)

116
00:04:42,981 --> 00:04:44,548
(Got it.)

117
00:04:48,748 --> 00:04:50,123
There you go. Nice.

118
00:04:51,381 --> 00:04:52,280
Split the block!

119
00:04:52,281 --> 00:04:53,365
(In 1, 2.)

120
00:04:53,691 --> 00:04:54,614
A huge spike!

121
00:04:54,615 --> 00:04:55,947
(She breaks through.)

122
00:04:55,948 --> 00:04:57,548
(A face dig)

123
00:04:58,215 --> 00:04:59,448
And it drops in!

124
00:05:01,748 --> 00:05:04,481
(A costly error)

125
00:05:08,081 --> 00:05:10,048
No.

126
00:05:13,315 --> 00:05:16,347
We've been seeing miscommunications
like this every match.

127
00:05:16,348 --> 00:05:18,126
When you're hesitating
over whose ball it is,

128
00:05:18,151 --> 00:05:19,415
- you just have to go for it.
- Exactly.

129
00:05:20,981 --> 00:05:23,081
(Tied again after an unforced error.)

130
00:05:23,774 --> 00:05:25,608
(Could this be our chance?)

131
00:05:26,015 --> 00:05:27,047
Hyeon Ju, step back!

132
00:05:27,048 --> 00:05:27,981
Okay.

133
00:05:28,548 --> 00:05:30,248
Defense, hold your spots! Stay low!

134
00:05:31,781 --> 00:05:33,214
Get ready!

135
00:05:33,239 --> 00:05:34,767
(The bulldogs are looking
to take the lead.)

136
00:05:35,115 --> 00:05:36,148
Tied at 20 to 20!

137
00:05:39,015 --> 00:05:40,547
The pass is off. She bumps it up.

138
00:05:40,548 --> 00:05:41,480
The set goes to Gyeong Hyeon.

139
00:05:41,481 --> 00:05:42,647
Just swing!

140
00:05:42,648 --> 00:05:43,581
Hit it high.

141
00:05:44,948 --> 00:05:47,615
(Another shaky block)

142
00:05:51,215 --> 00:05:52,215
Ye Dam covers!

143
00:05:52,881 --> 00:05:54,981
(On the edge of their seats)

144
00:05:55,786 --> 00:05:56,980
Watch out for the tip!

145
00:05:56,981 --> 00:05:57,948
Yoon Ha.

146
00:05:59,757 --> 00:06:01,023
She back-sets to Hyeon Ju.

147
00:06:01,048 --> 00:06:02,648
Hyeon Ju is stuffed.

148
00:06:03,348 --> 00:06:04,714
- Hyeon Ju!
- Back to the right.

149
00:06:04,715 --> 00:06:05,580
Just hit it!

150
00:06:05,581 --> 00:06:06,547
(Will she break through?)

151
00:06:06,548 --> 00:06:07,715
(Or will they shut her down?)

152
00:06:14,548 --> 00:06:16,314
Hyeon Ju!

153
00:06:16,315 --> 00:06:17,481
Off the block and out.

154
00:06:22,415 --> 00:06:24,448
Pohang Sports Council takes the lead.

155
00:06:25,015 --> 00:06:26,814
The Wonder Dogs can't afford
to lose focus now.

156
00:06:26,815 --> 00:06:29,981
Now the Wonder Dogs are playing catch-up.

157
00:06:30,774 --> 00:06:33,108
Good! Well done!

158
00:06:34,215 --> 00:06:36,181
- No!
- Let's go again.

159
00:06:40,848 --> 00:06:41,615
Tsubaki.

160
00:06:42,481 --> 00:06:44,370
Set it more to Young In.

161
00:06:44,681 --> 00:06:45,448
Okay.

162
00:06:46,748 --> 00:06:47,781
(She spots Young In.)

163
00:06:49,748 --> 00:06:50,448
(Approaching)

164
00:06:52,081 --> 00:06:53,781
(Her secret buddy grabs her hand.)

165
00:06:54,481 --> 00:06:55,881
(She flashes a signal.)

166
00:06:57,048 --> 00:06:57,848
Young In.

167
00:06:58,715 --> 00:07:00,548
Try broad-jumping into your swing.

168
00:07:01,015 --> 00:07:01,815
Okay.

169
00:07:02,081 --> 00:07:04,848
Pohang has turned the tables
and leads by one.

170
00:07:05,948 --> 00:07:06,948
Hyeon Ju to serve.

171
00:07:07,948 --> 00:07:09,748
Stay locked in!

172
00:07:10,848 --> 00:07:12,115
It's 21 to 20.

173
00:07:13,991 --> 00:07:15,056
Great pass.

174
00:07:15,081 --> 00:07:16,648
- Tsubaki!
- Nice!

175
00:07:17,415 --> 00:07:18,680
Young In, let's go.

176
00:07:18,947 --> 00:07:19,714
Swing!

177
00:07:19,715 --> 00:07:20,580
(She leaps forward and crushes it!)

178
00:07:20,581 --> 00:07:21,348
Young In.

179
00:07:21,815 --> 00:07:23,280
Off the block and out.

180
00:07:23,281 --> 00:07:24,080
Nice.

181
00:07:24,081 --> 00:07:24,980
(In awe)

182
00:07:24,981 --> 00:07:26,010
(Oh, no.)

183
00:07:26,511 --> 00:07:28,344
- Nice.
- Nice set.

184
00:07:28,345 --> 00:07:30,045
- Good.
- All right.

185
00:07:31,245 --> 00:07:33,445
Nice set. Great work.

186
00:07:33,778 --> 00:07:35,710
Despite the double block,

187
00:07:35,711 --> 00:07:38,710
Young In doesn't hesitate
and goes for the swing.

188
00:07:38,711 --> 00:07:39,878
- Right.
- That's bold.

189
00:07:40,578 --> 00:07:41,645
Good one, Young In.

190
00:07:43,178 --> 00:07:44,564
Nice bounce.

191
00:07:45,311 --> 00:07:46,311
Hyeon Ju.

192
00:07:46,845 --> 00:07:48,845
I told you to cover deep together.

193
00:07:49,011 --> 00:07:50,211
Got it. Sorry.

194
00:07:50,711 --> 00:07:51,744
Let's get one.

195
00:07:51,745 --> 00:07:53,210
They can't let the gap widen.

196
00:07:53,211 --> 00:07:55,078
They need to pull ahead instead.

197
00:07:55,378 --> 00:07:56,378
Watch the tip!

198
00:07:57,245 --> 00:07:58,577
It's 21 to 21, all tied up.

199
00:07:58,578 --> 00:07:59,279
Seon Ah!

200
00:07:59,578 --> 00:08:00,878
- Mine!
- Seon Ah digs it up.

201
00:08:01,311 --> 00:08:02,678
Push!

202
00:08:02,978 --> 00:08:04,217
It's kept alive.

203
00:08:05,145 --> 00:08:06,219
She sends a free ball over.

204
00:08:06,411 --> 00:08:07,445
Run. Give it.

205
00:08:07,578 --> 00:08:09,577
- Go!
- A back set. A slide attack.

206
00:08:09,578 --> 00:08:10,810
Okay.

207
00:08:10,811 --> 00:08:12,110
- Tsubaki digs it up.
- Cover!

208
00:08:12,111 --> 00:08:13,478
- C!
- Young In.

209
00:08:13,845 --> 00:08:14,845
There.

210
00:08:15,545 --> 00:08:16,745
Spike!

211
00:08:16,878 --> 00:08:17,878
Hyeon Ju digs it up.

212
00:08:18,111 --> 00:08:19,110
Hit it now!

213
00:08:19,111 --> 00:08:20,111
Gyeong Hyeon!

214
00:08:24,645 --> 00:08:25,645
It's saved.

215
00:08:25,878 --> 00:08:27,941
- Tsubaki!
- She's so good.

216
00:08:28,678 --> 00:08:30,244
(She dived to save the ball.)

217
00:08:30,245 --> 00:08:31,245
She sends it back over.

218
00:08:31,445 --> 00:08:33,077
Another chance for Pohang Sports Council.

219
00:08:33,078 --> 00:08:34,078
Quick, hit it!

220
00:08:34,511 --> 00:08:36,678
Gyeong Hyeon with the quick attack.

221
00:08:37,778 --> 00:08:38,811
She scores.

222
00:08:39,078 --> 00:08:40,810
(Pohang Sports Council pulls ahead again.)

223
00:08:40,811 --> 00:08:43,177
- All right.
- Well done, Gyeong Hyeon.

224
00:08:43,178 --> 00:08:45,645
- Yeong Hye, nice set.
- Nice set.

225
00:08:46,578 --> 00:08:47,745
Once again,

226
00:08:48,245 --> 00:08:50,030
Pohang Sports Council takes the lead.

227
00:08:50,945 --> 00:08:52,978
- Is the block too open?
- It's fine.

228
00:08:55,011 --> 00:08:56,610
She was way too far inside, right?

229
00:08:56,611 --> 00:08:58,178
(But Coach Kim isn't fine.)

230
00:08:58,578 --> 00:09:00,978
The ball was here.
Why were you blocking over there?

231
00:09:01,845 --> 00:09:03,678
Square up to the ball.

232
00:09:04,845 --> 00:09:05,878
(Leaning forward)

233
00:09:07,511 --> 00:09:08,645
(Remembering her notes)

234
00:09:10,178 --> 00:09:11,211
Chae Min!

235
00:09:11,778 --> 00:09:13,010
Don't jump on Young In too early.

236
00:09:13,011 --> 00:09:14,445
- Press over and wait.
- Yes, Coach.

237
00:09:16,245 --> 00:09:17,910
They're down by one again.

238
00:09:17,911 --> 00:09:19,844
Yes. They need to answer right away.

239
00:09:19,845 --> 00:09:20,845
Exactly.

240
00:09:21,545 --> 00:09:22,610
Gyeong Hyeon to serve.

241
00:09:22,611 --> 00:09:23,711
(Gyeong Hyeon serves.)

242
00:09:23,945 --> 00:09:24,945
Go, Min Kyeong!

243
00:09:25,111 --> 00:09:26,110
Now.

244
00:09:26,111 --> 00:09:27,110
(Set to Young In)

245
00:09:27,111 --> 00:09:28,111
Tsubaki.

246
00:09:28,911 --> 00:09:30,078
Press over!

247
00:09:33,445 --> 00:09:35,478
Young In gets stuffed.

248
00:09:40,045 --> 00:09:42,678
(Chae Min scores with a solo block.)

249
00:09:43,745 --> 00:09:46,344
Pohang Sports Council is
coming alive right now.

250
00:09:46,345 --> 00:09:48,345
Right. They're finishing strong,

251
00:09:48,545 --> 00:09:50,644
and as expected, we're starting
to see their true colors.

252
00:09:50,645 --> 00:09:53,310
(Their bulldog grit is waking up.)

253
00:09:53,311 --> 00:09:55,610
At this point, anything could happen...

254
00:09:55,611 --> 00:09:57,664
- Tsubaki, I was too far out.
- until the final point.

255
00:09:58,311 --> 00:10:00,245
Guys, no. Please.

256
00:10:00,845 --> 00:10:02,711
Come on, push through!

257
00:10:03,411 --> 00:10:04,977
- We've got this.
- Tsubaki.

258
00:10:04,978 --> 00:10:06,377
Let's go.

259
00:10:06,378 --> 00:10:07,378
- A to C.
- Okay.

260
00:10:07,678 --> 00:10:09,244
They can't afford
to give up any more points.

261
00:10:09,245 --> 00:10:10,810
They need to turn things around.

262
00:10:12,011 --> 00:10:13,280
Gyeong Hyeon serves again.

263
00:10:14,411 --> 00:10:15,545
Tsubaki, set it.

264
00:10:15,845 --> 00:10:17,110
Tsubaki sets it again.

265
00:10:17,111 --> 00:10:18,145
Young In tips it over.

266
00:10:18,311 --> 00:10:19,378
It comes tight to the net.

267
00:10:19,411 --> 00:10:21,411
A dump. Tsubaki keeps it alive.

268
00:10:21,878 --> 00:10:22,911
Yu Kyung.

269
00:10:23,445 --> 00:10:26,145
Young In. It goes off the block,
and Seon Ah saves it.

270
00:10:27,478 --> 00:10:28,478
Hit it!

271
00:10:28,604 --> 00:10:30,138
Hyeon Ju from the back row.

272
00:10:30,545 --> 00:10:32,145
- C! Okay.
- Tsubaki digs it up.

273
00:10:32,778 --> 00:10:33,944
Hit it!

274
00:10:33,945 --> 00:10:34,945
Young In again!

275
00:10:35,145 --> 00:10:36,569
Hyeon Ju keeps it alive.

276
00:10:36,911 --> 00:10:37,911
Get it over!

277
00:10:38,045 --> 00:10:39,045
It goes over.

278
00:10:39,278 --> 00:10:40,677
- B!
- Free ball for the Wonder Dogs.

279
00:10:40,678 --> 00:10:42,178
- Tsubaki sets it to the left.
- C!

280
00:10:42,345 --> 00:10:43,064
There.

281
00:10:43,088 --> 00:10:44,511
- Yoon Ha!
- Hit it!

282
00:10:45,445 --> 00:10:46,844
Yoon Ha!

283
00:10:46,845 --> 00:10:47,547
Yes!

284
00:10:47,730 --> 00:10:48,877
In!

285
00:10:48,878 --> 00:10:49,878
In!

286
00:10:50,111 --> 00:10:52,010
No, it's out!

287
00:10:52,011 --> 00:10:53,145
It's out!

288
00:10:54,478 --> 00:10:55,944
Is it out?

289
00:10:55,945 --> 00:10:57,311
(It's out?)

290
00:10:58,445 --> 00:10:59,478
(Nodding)

291
00:11:02,145 --> 00:11:05,111
(She challenges the call.)

292
00:11:06,078 --> 00:11:08,111
Wasn't that in?

293
00:11:08,278 --> 00:11:10,345
It's in, I swear.

294
00:11:11,211 --> 00:11:12,245
No worries.

295
00:11:17,511 --> 00:11:18,910
(In)

296
00:11:18,911 --> 00:11:20,544
See? It was in.

297
00:11:20,545 --> 00:11:21,214
In!

298
00:11:21,239 --> 00:11:22,811
(Finally smiling)

299
00:11:24,045 --> 00:11:25,845
Great swing, kid.

300
00:11:26,111 --> 00:11:29,044
Could Coach Kim really see that
from all the way over there?

301
00:11:29,045 --> 00:11:30,857
How did she even spot that?

302
00:11:33,345 --> 00:11:34,945
(She sees everything.)

303
00:11:35,178 --> 00:11:36,945
(Eyes full of confidence)

304
00:11:37,745 --> 00:11:39,810
- Incredible. Talk about eagle eyes.
- You're right.

305
00:11:39,811 --> 00:11:40,945
(The true eagle coach)

306
00:11:42,545 --> 00:11:44,445
- Good job, Yoon Ha.
- Nice.

307
00:11:44,678 --> 00:11:45,711
Yoon Ha, nice.

308
00:11:45,911 --> 00:11:48,010
Swinging like that at this score...

309
00:11:48,011 --> 00:11:50,578
shows how fearless she is.

310
00:11:51,345 --> 00:11:53,877
If they tie it up,
they could steal the momentum.

311
00:11:53,878 --> 00:11:54,878
Exactly.

312
00:11:54,945 --> 00:11:56,277
(A tight third set)

313
00:11:56,278 --> 00:11:59,610
They're neck and neck late in the set.

314
00:11:59,611 --> 00:12:02,445
(Third set, Pohang Sports Council 23
: Wonder Dogs 22)

315
00:12:02,711 --> 00:12:03,911
Just one more.

316
00:12:04,211 --> 00:12:05,444
You can catch up.

317
00:12:05,445 --> 00:12:06,445
(Three more points for a sweep)

318
00:12:06,578 --> 00:12:08,978
Every single point matters now.

319
00:12:09,011 --> 00:12:10,711
Okay, dig it up.

320
00:12:15,145 --> 00:12:16,669
Ho Bin, press deep over the net.

321
00:12:17,111 --> 00:12:19,444
Just get your hands over and wait.
Focus on the block.

322
00:12:19,445 --> 00:12:20,240
On it.

323
00:12:24,311 --> 00:12:25,178
Tsubaki.

324
00:12:25,511 --> 00:12:26,511
(Startled)

325
00:12:27,811 --> 00:12:28,715
Don't...

326
00:12:29,178 --> 00:12:30,177
(Chuckling)

327
00:12:30,178 --> 00:12:32,110
- Don't force the set to the right.
- Okay.

328
00:12:32,111 --> 00:12:33,445
- We can use the pipe too.
- Got it.

329
00:12:33,978 --> 00:12:35,544
(Directing with body language)

330
00:12:35,545 --> 00:12:37,345
- Stay deep.
- Yes, Coach.

331
00:12:37,378 --> 00:12:39,311
(Rushing back)

332
00:12:40,078 --> 00:12:41,078
Min Kyeong, space.

333
00:12:41,478 --> 00:12:42,745
(Nodding)

334
00:12:43,845 --> 00:12:44,911
One-point game.

335
00:12:46,611 --> 00:12:48,045
(Watching)

336
00:12:50,511 --> 00:12:51,877
(Targeting...)

337
00:12:51,878 --> 00:12:53,645
(Zone 4, close to the line)

338
00:12:55,211 --> 00:12:57,344
(The target zone)

339
00:12:57,345 --> 00:12:59,546
The Wonder Dogs need to start
with a tough serve.

340
00:13:00,778 --> 00:13:01,945
- Cover!
- C!

341
00:13:02,345 --> 00:13:03,377
(Right at Zone 4)

342
00:13:03,378 --> 00:13:04,711
That's it. Nice serve.

343
00:13:04,945 --> 00:13:06,052
- Run.
- Yeong Hye.

344
00:13:06,545 --> 00:13:07,578
A slide attack.

345
00:13:07,745 --> 00:13:08,910
She kept it up!

346
00:13:08,911 --> 00:13:10,745
- Yoon Ha!
- Yoon Ha spikes!

347
00:13:11,811 --> 00:13:12,910
Get out!

348
00:13:12,911 --> 00:13:14,245
Chae Min on the left.

349
00:13:15,178 --> 00:13:16,178
It got through.

350
00:13:17,211 --> 00:13:18,277
Yu Kyung digs it up.

351
00:13:18,278 --> 00:13:19,277
(A high ball)

352
00:13:19,278 --> 00:13:20,278
The middle!

353
00:13:20,621 --> 00:13:21,653
Hit it.

354
00:13:21,678 --> 00:13:23,610
A jump set! A pipe!

355
00:13:23,611 --> 00:13:24,678
Swing!

356
00:13:27,545 --> 00:13:28,878
It's blocked.

357
00:13:31,545 --> 00:13:32,545
Ho Bin!

358
00:13:34,311 --> 00:13:35,311
That was so close.

359
00:13:35,704 --> 00:13:38,371
Ho Bin shuts down the shot, of all people.

360
00:13:40,245 --> 00:13:41,678
At this crucial moment,

361
00:13:42,778 --> 00:13:44,711
I'm sorry.

362
00:13:45,211 --> 00:13:47,645
she stuffs Min Kyeong's attack.

363
00:13:48,511 --> 00:13:49,545
So close.

364
00:13:49,678 --> 00:13:51,910
Pohang Sports Council has really
found their rhythm.

365
00:13:51,911 --> 00:13:52,732
Yes.

366
00:13:52,945 --> 00:13:54,377
Nice, okay.

367
00:13:54,378 --> 00:13:55,945
(Pohang Sports Council's set point)

368
00:13:56,244 --> 00:13:57,844
Way to go.

369
00:13:58,477 --> 00:13:59,305
Chae Min.

370
00:14:00,011 --> 00:14:01,891
Get up to your contact point
and swing fast.

371
00:14:01,915 --> 00:14:02,475
Okay.

372
00:14:04,611 --> 00:14:07,444
(Reviewing the previous rally)

373
00:14:07,944 --> 00:14:08,944
Tsubaki!

374
00:14:09,077 --> 00:14:10,543
You left the middle open.

375
00:14:10,544 --> 00:14:12,943
The ball was over there,
but you jumped here instead.

376
00:14:12,944 --> 00:14:14,544
(Stressing blocking discipline again)

377
00:14:14,677 --> 00:14:16,810
For the Wonder Dogs,
if this goes to a fourth set,

378
00:14:16,811 --> 00:14:18,343
it's anyone's game.

379
00:14:18,344 --> 00:14:21,743
Yes. And Pohang Sports Council is
a team of fifth-set specialists.

380
00:14:21,744 --> 00:14:24,011
- That's right.
- They can't let their guard down.

381
00:14:25,211 --> 00:14:27,811
Gyeong Hyeon, go for it.
You can hit it high.

382
00:14:28,311 --> 00:14:30,577
Keep pushing. We can do this.
Just two more!

383
00:14:31,277 --> 00:14:33,111
Pohang Sports Council's set point.

384
00:14:35,477 --> 00:14:36,476
Ho Bin to serve.

385
00:14:36,477 --> 00:14:37,544
(Ho Bin serves.)

386
00:14:37,911 --> 00:14:38,711
Mine!

387
00:14:39,177 --> 00:14:40,776
It goes over after a shaky pass.

388
00:14:40,777 --> 00:14:42,377
Use C!

389
00:14:43,877 --> 00:14:44,876
(It's right.)

390
00:14:44,877 --> 00:14:45,943
Hit it fast!

391
00:14:45,944 --> 00:14:47,444
You need to go!

392
00:14:48,911 --> 00:14:52,311
- Chae Min scores.
- All right.

393
00:14:54,904 --> 00:14:56,937
- My bad.
- Sorry.

394
00:14:56,969 --> 00:14:57,964
I jumped too fast.

395
00:14:58,177 --> 00:15:00,043
It ends 22 to 25.

396
00:15:00,044 --> 00:15:02,802
Pohang Sports Council fights back
to take the third set.

397
00:15:04,044 --> 00:15:06,377
We keep fighting and never give in.

398
00:15:06,677 --> 00:15:08,177
We'll push through to the end.

399
00:15:09,711 --> 00:15:12,144
I thought the tide had turned again,

400
00:15:12,844 --> 00:15:16,444
and we were in for a tough battle today.

401
00:15:18,344 --> 00:15:20,911
(Fourth-set timeout)

402
00:15:21,344 --> 00:15:22,377
Let's go.

403
00:15:23,251 --> 00:15:25,417
How many times is this?

404
00:15:27,944 --> 00:15:29,176
It went through the seam again.

405
00:15:29,177 --> 00:15:30,396
What did I tell you about the high ball?

406
00:15:30,477 --> 00:15:33,343
- Stay tighter and close the block.
- Yes.

407
00:15:33,344 --> 00:15:36,044
The other team has come up
with a lot of big blocks.

408
00:15:36,944 --> 00:15:40,577
(The opponents' block has tightened up.)

409
00:15:41,611 --> 00:15:42,743
(While ours fell apart.)

410
00:15:42,744 --> 00:15:45,644
And we've been making too many errors.

411
00:15:46,544 --> 00:15:48,976
I think our blocking alignment
will be critical...

412
00:15:48,977 --> 00:15:50,311
in the fourth set.

413
00:15:50,577 --> 00:15:51,676
Where should you be lining up your block?

414
00:15:51,677 --> 00:15:53,543
- At zero.
- Right, straight on the ball.

415
00:15:53,544 --> 00:15:55,110
Line up the block at zero.

416
00:15:55,111 --> 00:15:56,143
- Yes, Coach.
- Yes, Coach.

417
00:15:56,144 --> 00:15:57,143
(The middle)

418
00:15:57,144 --> 00:15:59,477
- And hit through the seam.
- Okay.

419
00:16:00,377 --> 00:16:02,611
(She's been urging them
to hit the seam from the start.)

420
00:16:04,177 --> 00:16:06,010
(Right through the seam)

421
00:16:06,011 --> 00:16:07,544
- Okay.
- Sorry about the block.

422
00:16:08,077 --> 00:16:09,110
Let's get a block first.

423
00:16:09,111 --> 00:16:11,911
- Doing great, Hyeon Ju.
- That's what I'm talking about.

424
00:16:12,244 --> 00:16:13,476
Yeong Hye, nice.

425
00:16:13,477 --> 00:16:14,776
- Good one.
- Nice.

426
00:16:14,777 --> 00:16:17,843
- Great work.
- Don't shift the block for now.

427
00:16:17,844 --> 00:16:18,843
- Got it.
- Hold your spot.

428
00:16:18,844 --> 00:16:20,310
Once you get a good dig, swing fast.

429
00:16:20,311 --> 00:16:22,476
- You can't score with soft shots.
- Understood.

430
00:16:22,477 --> 00:16:24,143
Either go cross-court or hit it deep.

431
00:16:24,144 --> 00:16:25,577
- Make something happen.
- Yes, Coach.

432
00:16:25,603 --> 00:16:27,368
Go ahead and swing. You're good.

433
00:16:27,369 --> 00:16:29,368
- Cover Gyeong Hyeon on her swing.
- Let's go.

434
00:16:29,369 --> 00:16:30,302
Come on. One more.

435
00:16:30,303 --> 00:16:31,736
- Let's push this to a fifth set.
- Yes.

436
00:16:32,436 --> 00:16:33,469
Now, let's turn it up.

437
00:16:33,698 --> 00:16:35,258
- Lock it in!
- Yes, Coach!

438
00:16:36,069 --> 00:16:38,835
I knew we had to close it out
in the fourth set...

439
00:16:38,836 --> 00:16:39,732
no matter what.

440
00:16:39,903 --> 00:16:41,368
We're forcing a fifth set,

441
00:16:41,369 --> 00:16:42,869
and we're taking it there.

442
00:16:44,136 --> 00:16:45,468
Yeong Hye's serve...

443
00:16:45,469 --> 00:16:46,903
gets the fourth set underway.

444
00:16:48,169 --> 00:16:48,968
Go for it!

445
00:16:48,969 --> 00:16:49,976
Min Kyeong with the pass.

446
00:16:51,503 --> 00:16:52,303
A slide!

447
00:16:52,736 --> 00:16:54,235
- Back set.
- Hit it quick!

448
00:16:54,236 --> 00:16:55,135
Go ahead and swing.

449
00:16:55,136 --> 00:16:56,369
Just hit it!

450
00:16:58,969 --> 00:17:00,435
Hyeon Ju hammers it through.

451
00:17:00,436 --> 00:17:02,068
All right!

452
00:17:02,069 --> 00:17:04,203
(Splitting the block for the first point)

453
00:17:04,336 --> 00:17:05,703
Good.

454
00:17:06,442 --> 00:17:07,245
(Hyeon Ju broke the block.)

455
00:17:07,269 --> 00:17:08,336
Come on, no!

456
00:17:09,336 --> 00:17:10,669
Put it through the seams.

457
00:17:11,785 --> 00:17:12,811
(Nodding)

458
00:17:12,836 --> 00:17:13,669
Yes.

459
00:17:14,836 --> 00:17:15,669
It's 1 to 0.

460
00:17:17,845 --> 00:17:18,911
(A solid dig)

461
00:17:18,936 --> 00:17:19,736
- Good.
- Cover!

462
00:17:21,036 --> 00:17:22,103
(A chance for Min Kyeong)

463
00:17:22,636 --> 00:17:23,735
(Right through the seam)

464
00:17:23,736 --> 00:17:24,602
Go!

465
00:17:24,603 --> 00:17:26,236
(She puts it away.)

466
00:17:28,503 --> 00:17:29,902
Thank you!

467
00:17:29,903 --> 00:17:31,468
Looking sharp, Min Kyeong.

468
00:17:31,469 --> 00:17:32,336
Nice.

469
00:17:32,803 --> 00:17:34,236
Nice shot, Min Kyeong.

470
00:17:35,336 --> 00:17:39,368
Min Kyeong got there early,
got right behind the ball,

471
00:17:39,369 --> 00:17:41,568
- and took a clean swing.
- Exactly.

472
00:17:41,569 --> 00:17:43,736
Min Kyeong split the seam
between the blockers.

473
00:17:45,203 --> 00:17:46,335
You're fine. Good job.

474
00:17:46,336 --> 00:17:47,968
Stay ready to swing.

475
00:17:47,969 --> 00:17:48,935
Hyeon Ju!

476
00:17:48,936 --> 00:17:50,270
You have to contact it higher.

477
00:17:51,703 --> 00:17:55,036
(A chess match at the net)

478
00:17:57,603 --> 00:17:58,469
All tied at 1 to 1.

479
00:18:00,469 --> 00:18:01,835
Just hit it deep!

480
00:18:01,836 --> 00:18:02,669
Hyeon Ju.

481
00:18:02,969 --> 00:18:04,836
- They score off the block and out.
- So close.

482
00:18:06,803 --> 00:18:08,069
Good.

483
00:18:09,469 --> 00:18:10,835
That sailed out of bounds.

484
00:18:10,836 --> 00:18:12,091
- Get ready, Min Kyeong.
- Yes.

485
00:18:14,003 --> 00:18:15,103
That's it.

486
00:18:17,269 --> 00:18:18,103
Swing!

487
00:18:18,969 --> 00:18:20,502
Min Kyeong scores.

488
00:18:20,503 --> 00:18:21,636
(They keep finding the seam.)

489
00:18:22,236 --> 00:18:24,002
Min Kyeong is in rhythm today.

490
00:18:24,003 --> 00:18:24,868
Se Yeon,

491
00:18:24,869 --> 00:18:26,568
get up for the quick.

492
00:18:26,569 --> 00:18:27,607
Push one through!

493
00:18:30,969 --> 00:18:32,736
Quick attack down the middle.

494
00:18:33,555 --> 00:18:34,740
Ye Dam!

495
00:18:34,870 --> 00:18:36,135
Ye Dam.

496
00:18:36,136 --> 00:18:37,984
Watch the seams in the block.

497
00:18:38,496 --> 00:18:39,696
That's it.

498
00:18:40,469 --> 00:18:41,569
(Using the footwork she drilled)

499
00:18:42,336 --> 00:18:43,268
Swing!

500
00:18:43,269 --> 00:18:44,769
Young In from the right side.

501
00:18:45,069 --> 00:18:46,035
She scores.

502
00:18:46,036 --> 00:18:47,435
Nice.

503
00:18:47,436 --> 00:18:48,436
This is our chance.

504
00:18:49,269 --> 00:18:51,002
- There we go.
- Nice.

505
00:18:51,003 --> 00:18:52,736
- Nice.
- Great job, Young In.

506
00:18:54,803 --> 00:18:55,603
Back set.

507
00:18:56,103 --> 00:18:57,569
- Hyeon Ju.
- Hit it quick!

508
00:18:59,069 --> 00:19:00,306
Another point off the block.

509
00:19:00,869 --> 00:19:02,703
- Hyeon Ju is back in form.
- She is.

510
00:19:03,336 --> 00:19:05,068
- My bad.
- Get ready, quick!

511
00:19:05,093 --> 00:19:06,556
Get the timing right.

512
00:19:06,556 --> 00:19:08,236
(Pohang leads again by 1 point.)

513
00:19:10,003 --> 00:19:12,869
(They keep scoring through the seams.)

514
00:19:14,103 --> 00:19:16,003
- Off the block and out.
- Get in position.

515
00:19:16,869 --> 00:19:17,835
Another point off the block.

516
00:19:17,836 --> 00:19:19,336
(Their blocks keep coming up short.)

517
00:19:20,969 --> 00:19:23,703
(The early momentum slips away.)

518
00:19:24,069 --> 00:19:26,568
Young In, line up your block.

519
00:19:26,569 --> 00:19:27,336
Yes, Coach.

520
00:19:27,636 --> 00:19:28,935
I'll take that spot.

521
00:19:28,936 --> 00:19:30,469
- Slow it down a touch.
- Okay.

522
00:19:31,069 --> 00:19:32,769
It's 5 to 6, down by just one.

523
00:19:34,236 --> 00:19:35,069
Serve.

524
00:19:37,536 --> 00:19:38,603
Seon Ah passes.

525
00:19:39,169 --> 00:19:40,235
Push it out!

526
00:19:40,236 --> 00:19:41,102
One, two...

527
00:19:41,103 --> 00:19:41,836
(Three!)

528
00:19:42,836 --> 00:19:43,968
The Wonder Dogs stuff it!

529
00:19:43,969 --> 00:19:45,051
That's what we need.

530
00:19:46,821 --> 00:19:48,588
- They couldn't get a swing off.
- Mine!

531
00:19:48,969 --> 00:19:49,835
She sets it up.

532
00:19:49,836 --> 00:19:51,269
Tsubaki with the quick.

533
00:19:51,869 --> 00:19:53,135
Hit it right away!

534
00:19:53,136 --> 00:19:53,936
C!

535
00:19:54,736 --> 00:19:55,535
(The ball goes back...)

536
00:19:55,536 --> 00:19:56,569
Hit it cross-court!

537
00:19:56,869 --> 00:19:57,803
(to Gyeong Hyeon.)

538
00:19:58,945 --> 00:20:00,154
Gyeong Hyeon swings.

539
00:20:00,178 --> 00:20:01,712
Dug up by Ye Dam!

540
00:20:01,736 --> 00:20:02,336
C!

541
00:20:03,236 --> 00:20:04,469
(Great defense meets...)

542
00:20:05,636 --> 00:20:07,540
Yoon Ha puts it away!

543
00:20:07,540 --> 00:20:08,860
(great offense.)

544
00:20:10,403 --> 00:20:12,269
Coach Kim applauds.

545
00:20:13,303 --> 00:20:14,835
And that deserves applause.

546
00:20:14,836 --> 00:20:17,302
They finally land a block.

547
00:20:17,303 --> 00:20:18,568
(They shut down the attack.)

548
00:20:18,569 --> 00:20:19,802
Just as Coach Kim instructed,

549
00:20:19,803 --> 00:20:22,288
they're exploiting the seams in the block.

550
00:20:24,069 --> 00:20:25,068
Set to the right.

551
00:20:25,069 --> 00:20:28,303
- Great job, Yoon Ha.
- Nice one, Yoon Ha.

552
00:20:28,603 --> 00:20:30,169
It's okay. Get the next one.

553
00:20:31,369 --> 00:20:33,435
Yeong Hye.

554
00:20:33,436 --> 00:20:34,536
Hyeon Ju is right there.

555
00:20:35,036 --> 00:20:36,202
You have to take a swing.

556
00:20:36,203 --> 00:20:37,135
Let's get one.

557
00:20:37,136 --> 00:20:38,269
(Calling for a right-side attack)

558
00:20:39,203 --> 00:20:40,635
Ye Dam serves again.

559
00:20:40,636 --> 00:20:41,503
Serve.

560
00:20:42,303 --> 00:20:43,169
Dig it up.

561
00:20:43,769 --> 00:20:44,535
C!

562
00:20:44,536 --> 00:20:45,635
Number seven!

563
00:20:45,636 --> 00:20:46,436
Set me!

564
00:20:48,136 --> 00:20:49,102
Cover!

565
00:20:49,103 --> 00:20:51,335
- Only one blocker up.
- Defense!

566
00:20:51,336 --> 00:20:52,236
Swing!

567
00:20:52,436 --> 00:20:53,535
There we go.

568
00:20:53,536 --> 00:20:54,836
(And of all people, Hyeon Ju)

569
00:20:56,203 --> 00:20:57,202
Hyeon Ju from the back row.

570
00:20:57,203 --> 00:20:58,203
It's out!

571
00:20:58,803 --> 00:20:59,735
Nice.

572
00:20:59,736 --> 00:21:01,402
- There you go.
- Nice.

573
00:21:01,403 --> 00:21:02,603
Touch!

574
00:21:03,103 --> 00:21:04,935
- It didn't touch my hand.
- It didn't?

575
00:21:04,936 --> 00:21:06,435
Called out.

576
00:21:06,436 --> 00:21:07,369
It touched her!

577
00:21:08,669 --> 00:21:09,802
It touched her.

578
00:21:09,803 --> 00:21:11,669
- It touched her!
- Touch!

579
00:21:13,003 --> 00:21:13,936
Let's challenge the call.

580
00:21:15,669 --> 00:21:18,303
Yoon Ha said it was out, but...

581
00:21:20,136 --> 00:21:21,335
Yeah, that clearly grazed her fingers.

582
00:21:21,336 --> 00:21:22,603
- It sure did.
- Right.

583
00:21:23,303 --> 00:21:25,535
Still, in a moment like that,

584
00:21:25,536 --> 00:21:27,703
players will always swear
they didn't touch it.

585
00:21:29,169 --> 00:21:30,336
It's okay. Good effort.

586
00:21:32,103 --> 00:21:35,068
Look at where that ball was set.

587
00:21:35,069 --> 00:21:35,936
Where was it set?

588
00:21:36,503 --> 00:21:37,436
Way off to the pin.

589
00:21:39,436 --> 00:21:41,102
(Poor positioning)

590
00:21:41,103 --> 00:21:42,669
She's on the left. Where should you be?

591
00:21:43,036 --> 00:21:44,235
You need to be lined up in the middle.

592
00:21:44,260 --> 00:21:45,060
- Zero.
- Yes, Coach.

593
00:21:46,103 --> 00:21:49,768
If we get our blocking alignment
right today,

594
00:21:49,769 --> 00:21:51,203
we can really build momentum.

595
00:21:52,403 --> 00:21:54,402
- Serve.
- Ye Eun has a tough serve.

596
00:21:54,403 --> 00:21:55,236
That's right.

597
00:21:56,936 --> 00:21:58,303
- Off Hyeon Ju.
- C!

598
00:21:58,707 --> 00:21:59,427
Put it away!

599
00:21:59,836 --> 00:22:00,769
One, two.

600
00:22:01,436 --> 00:22:02,369
Chae Min with the tip.

601
00:22:02,661 --> 00:22:03,495
That's it.

602
00:22:03,617 --> 00:22:04,223
Set it.

603
00:22:04,468 --> 00:22:05,595
- A bump set.
- Cover!

604
00:22:06,303 --> 00:22:07,069
Min Kyeong!

605
00:22:07,569 --> 00:22:09,269
- Middle!
- They keep it alive. Tsubaki.

606
00:22:10,336 --> 00:22:11,703
A soft pipe shot.

607
00:22:12,136 --> 00:22:13,136
(Hyeon Ju dives for the dig.)

608
00:22:13,403 --> 00:22:14,536
Front quick!

609
00:22:15,369 --> 00:22:16,569
Timing!

610
00:22:18,136 --> 00:22:19,935
- They shut down the middle attack.
- That's it.

611
00:22:19,936 --> 00:22:21,035
Okay.

612
00:22:21,036 --> 00:22:21,936
C!

613
00:22:23,269 --> 00:22:24,703
Back to Chae Min.

614
00:22:25,169 --> 00:22:26,335
Tip it!

615
00:22:26,336 --> 00:22:27,336
Watch the timing!

616
00:22:27,803 --> 00:22:28,736
One more!

617
00:22:30,936 --> 00:22:32,802
It hits the antenna!

618
00:22:32,803 --> 00:22:34,053
The error puts the Wonder Dogs in front.

619
00:22:34,569 --> 00:22:35,403
There we go.

620
00:22:36,969 --> 00:22:38,435
(Solid blocking)

621
00:22:38,436 --> 00:22:41,003
- Good job.
- Nice, Tsubaki.

622
00:22:42,269 --> 00:22:45,503
(She left the right side wide open
and gave up a point earlier.)

623
00:22:46,836 --> 00:22:48,936
(This time,
she sealed off the right side,)

624
00:22:50,003 --> 00:22:52,169
(forcing the error.)

625
00:22:53,103 --> 00:22:55,435
(Their blocking is finally clicking.)

626
00:22:55,436 --> 00:22:56,836
(Fourth set, Pohang Sports Council 9
: Wonder Dogs 9)

627
00:22:59,736 --> 00:23:00,703
Get it up!

628
00:23:01,269 --> 00:23:02,435
Shaky pass.

629
00:23:02,436 --> 00:23:03,203
Hey!

630
00:23:04,469 --> 00:23:06,203
- Hit it!
- You have to swing at that!

631
00:23:08,603 --> 00:23:09,536
They keep it alive!

632
00:23:10,503 --> 00:23:11,336
C!

633
00:23:12,145 --> 00:23:13,011
You have to take a swing!

634
00:23:13,036 --> 00:23:13,902
(A chance to redeem herself)

635
00:23:13,903 --> 00:23:15,069
Good.

636
00:23:16,036 --> 00:23:17,102
Min Kyeong with the backstep.

637
00:23:17,103 --> 00:23:17,936
Down the line.

638
00:23:18,503 --> 00:23:20,236
- Sorry about that.
- Min Kyeong was...

639
00:23:21,303 --> 00:23:22,435
about to get an earful.

640
00:23:22,436 --> 00:23:24,135
Focus!

641
00:23:24,136 --> 00:23:25,803
Take a breath.

642
00:23:26,236 --> 00:23:27,069
(Feeling self-conscious)

643
00:23:28,236 --> 00:23:29,636
Min Kyeong has been hot and cold today.

644
00:23:30,736 --> 00:23:33,669
She owes Bo Been for covering for her.

645
00:23:34,703 --> 00:23:37,803
(A momentary passing error)

646
00:23:38,469 --> 00:23:40,468
- Nice recovery.
- Right.

647
00:23:40,469 --> 00:23:43,469
Min Kyeong makes up for it
right away with a kill.

648
00:23:43,936 --> 00:23:44,868
Nice cover.

649
00:23:44,869 --> 00:23:47,935
- Clear your head.
- Yes.

650
00:23:47,936 --> 00:23:49,228
What's got you so rattled?

651
00:23:49,436 --> 00:23:50,535
Get your head straight.

652
00:23:50,536 --> 00:23:52,369
(No more ups and downs)

653
00:23:53,603 --> 00:23:55,636
- Pass it, then run a pipe. Be ready.
- Yes.

654
00:23:55,928 --> 00:23:56,602
Tsubaki.

655
00:23:56,627 --> 00:23:57,547
(Signaling a pipe attack)

656
00:23:58,803 --> 00:24:00,168
- Let's go.
- The Wonder Dogs lead 10 to 9,

657
00:24:00,169 --> 00:24:01,769
up by a single point.

658
00:24:04,036 --> 00:24:05,136
Now!

659
00:24:05,828 --> 00:24:07,528
Watch the timing.

660
00:24:08,193 --> 00:24:08,754
Swing!

661
00:24:08,778 --> 00:24:09,868
A soft shot from Hyeon Ju.

662
00:24:09,869 --> 00:24:11,102
They keep it alive with a diving dig.

663
00:24:11,103 --> 00:24:12,836
Tsubaki to Min Kyeong.

664
00:24:13,403 --> 00:24:14,720
Hyeon Ju charges in again.

665
00:24:15,503 --> 00:24:17,103
Pipe attack. Off the net!

666
00:24:17,436 --> 00:24:18,268
Dug up.

667
00:24:18,293 --> 00:24:19,360
(Min Kyeong regroups and makes the dig.)

668
00:24:21,736 --> 00:24:23,702
Tsubaki sends it over.

669
00:24:23,703 --> 00:24:24,869
Yeong Hye, set me!

670
00:24:25,669 --> 00:24:26,902
Yeong Hye pushes it left.

671
00:24:26,903 --> 00:24:27,803
One, two.

672
00:24:28,636 --> 00:24:29,602
(This time, it gets through.)

673
00:24:29,603 --> 00:24:31,002
Hyeon Ju.

674
00:24:31,003 --> 00:24:32,435
- Middle!
- Ye Eun digs it.

675
00:24:32,436 --> 00:24:33,268
Tsubaki.

676
00:24:33,269 --> 00:24:34,110
That's it.

677
00:24:35,169 --> 00:24:36,036
A tip from the back row!

678
00:24:37,069 --> 00:24:38,503
And they score.

679
00:24:38,528 --> 00:24:39,839
(Scoring with a pipe attack)

680
00:24:40,103 --> 00:24:41,636
(Clenching her fist)

681
00:24:44,636 --> 00:24:46,203
Nice one, Tsubaki.

682
00:24:46,469 --> 00:24:48,835
Since Tsubaki subbed in,

683
00:24:48,836 --> 00:24:51,503
- they've been running a lot more pipes.
- You're right.

684
00:24:52,236 --> 00:24:53,768
(Since Tsubaki subbed in,)

685
00:24:53,769 --> 00:24:58,336
(back-row attacks have picked up.)

686
00:24:59,703 --> 00:25:01,002
Great placement.

687
00:25:01,003 --> 00:25:02,336
(Their first two-point lead in Set Four)

688
00:25:04,536 --> 00:25:05,469
Right away.

689
00:25:06,303 --> 00:25:09,069
Coach Kim had told them to mix in
more back-row attacks.

690
00:25:11,169 --> 00:25:14,236
You can tell
they really drilled it in practice.

691
00:25:15,136 --> 00:25:16,536
Ho Bin, watch short.

692
00:25:20,336 --> 00:25:21,921
I knew I had to get at least one block.

693
00:25:22,436 --> 00:25:25,136
(Fourth set, Pohang Sports Council 11
: Wonder Dogs 13)

694
00:25:27,303 --> 00:25:28,236
Make it count.

695
00:25:28,631 --> 00:25:29,131
Cover.

696
00:25:29,269 --> 00:25:30,769
Yeong Hye sets left to Gyeong Hyeon.

697
00:25:31,703 --> 00:25:32,536
Off the block.

698
00:25:32,903 --> 00:25:34,068
Young In keeps it alive.

699
00:25:34,069 --> 00:25:34,936
Good, that's it.

700
00:25:35,303 --> 00:25:36,135
Mine!

701
00:25:36,493 --> 00:25:37,778
Do it!

702
00:25:37,803 --> 00:25:39,803
(A pipe attack attempt)

703
00:25:43,569 --> 00:25:44,403
Min Kyeong.

704
00:25:46,336 --> 00:25:48,603
(Ho Bin goes up for another solo block.)

705
00:25:50,303 --> 00:25:51,336
Good.

706
00:25:53,769 --> 00:25:54,936
Why didn't you put that away?

707
00:25:59,436 --> 00:26:01,861
They're hitting toward Gyeong Hyeon,
so I'll shift over to cover that side.

708
00:26:02,636 --> 00:26:03,702
Just cover the short ones.

709
00:26:03,703 --> 00:26:05,136
(Nodding)

710
00:26:05,336 --> 00:26:07,066
I'll cover the right side.

711
00:26:07,088 --> 00:26:07,711
(Got it.)

712
00:26:07,736 --> 00:26:08,936
Lock in!

713
00:26:10,769 --> 00:26:12,036
- Hey!
- Mine!

714
00:26:13,269 --> 00:26:14,140
- Go for it!
- There it goes. Good.

715
00:26:14,168 --> 00:26:14,906
Young In!

716
00:26:15,436 --> 00:26:16,236
(The ball goes high.)

717
00:26:16,336 --> 00:26:17,402
Swing now!

718
00:26:17,427 --> 00:26:18,760
You take it.

719
00:26:18,969 --> 00:26:19,979
Gyeong Hyeon.

720
00:26:20,503 --> 00:26:22,369
It lands in.

721
00:26:23,369 --> 00:26:24,869
- Nice.
- Good one.

722
00:26:26,381 --> 00:26:28,449
Nice dig.

723
00:26:29,563 --> 00:26:32,865
Pohang Sports Council
not only plays great defense,

724
00:26:32,890 --> 00:26:35,792
but also knows
how to play to its strengths.

725
00:26:35,793 --> 00:26:36,626
Right.

726
00:26:37,728 --> 00:26:38,795
Well done.

727
00:26:39,063 --> 00:26:40,263
(Fourth set, Pohang Sports Council 14
: Wonder Dogs 14)

728
00:26:40,264 --> 00:26:42,666
Seon Ah and Ho Bin know our game
inside out.

729
00:26:42,667 --> 00:26:45,602
They know our strengths and weaknesses.

730
00:26:45,870 --> 00:26:48,105
(The veteran coach's response)

731
00:26:48,539 --> 00:26:50,006
- Young In.
- Got it.

732
00:26:50,541 --> 00:26:51,374
What's our play?

733
00:26:52,744 --> 00:26:53,744
Got it.

734
00:26:53,745 --> 00:26:55,479
(Going with Tsubaki and Young In's combo)

735
00:26:55,480 --> 00:26:56,680
Let's go right away.

736
00:26:56,681 --> 00:26:58,017
- Let's go.
- Right away.

737
00:27:00,880 --> 00:27:02,421
Focus!

738
00:27:02,854 --> 00:27:03,787
Gyeong Hyeon to serve.

739
00:27:04,690 --> 00:27:05,598
(Min Kyeong with the dig)

740
00:27:05,623 --> 00:27:06,590
Set me.

741
00:27:07,158 --> 00:27:08,358
One-on-one!

742
00:27:09,596 --> 00:27:10,576
(Hyeon Ju with the dig)

743
00:27:11,529 --> 00:27:12,729
They're crowding the ball.

744
00:27:13,315 --> 00:27:14,518
It goes back over the net.

745
00:27:14,550 --> 00:27:15,489
(Here comes a free ball.)

746
00:27:15,523 --> 00:27:16,387
Again!

747
00:27:16,412 --> 00:27:17,278
Free ball!

748
00:27:17,601 --> 00:27:18,534
Tsubaki sets.

749
00:27:20,037 --> 00:27:21,137
It goes back over.

750
00:27:21,138 --> 00:27:23,305
Young In puts it away.

751
00:27:23,808 --> 00:27:25,541
(Fourth set, Pohang Sports Council 14
: Wonder Dogs 15)

752
00:27:25,542 --> 00:27:26,943
Nice.

753
00:27:26,944 --> 00:27:28,044
(The Wonder Dogs retake the lead by one.)

754
00:27:28,145 --> 00:27:29,112
That's it.

755
00:27:29,980 --> 00:27:31,580
Let's go, Young In.

756
00:27:32,149 --> 00:27:33,416
(The target is...)

757
00:27:33,417 --> 00:27:34,284
(Hyeon Ju.)

758
00:27:34,285 --> 00:27:35,151
Nice serve.

759
00:27:35,152 --> 00:27:36,786
Hyeon Ju passes it, and then a back set.

760
00:27:36,854 --> 00:27:38,021
(Ho Bin's shot)

761
00:27:38,022 --> 00:27:39,522
It's out!

762
00:27:39,757 --> 00:27:40,623
It sailed out!

763
00:27:44,161 --> 00:27:45,328
That was a tough serve.

764
00:27:45,529 --> 00:27:48,198
This is driving me crazy.

765
00:27:48,199 --> 00:27:49,165
Ho Bin,

766
00:27:49,400 --> 00:27:51,070
they're not going to bite on the jump.

767
00:27:52,169 --> 00:27:56,005
As the match wore on,
Young In got more aggressive.

768
00:27:56,006 --> 00:27:58,741
She's calling for the ball
and putting points away.

769
00:27:59,009 --> 00:28:04,180
You can really feel her fire
and her hunger to win.

770
00:28:06,784 --> 00:28:07,951
That's it.

771
00:28:08,285 --> 00:28:11,221
Sparked by Young In's hustle,
the team now leads by three.

772
00:28:12,056 --> 00:28:14,190
(Ye Eun serves.)

773
00:28:14,450 --> 00:28:15,884
(The target is...)

774
00:28:16,060 --> 00:28:17,229
Serve wherever you want.

775
00:28:21,198 --> 00:28:23,566
(Baby Eagle takes flight.)

776
00:28:24,868 --> 00:28:27,236
(Locking onto the target)

777
00:28:32,042 --> 00:28:32,942
Serve.

778
00:28:40,585 --> 00:28:43,319
- Ye Eun scores an ace!
- My fault.

779
00:28:43,887 --> 00:28:44,920
(Baby Eagle's hunt succeeds.)

780
00:28:44,921 --> 00:28:46,689
- That's it.
- Ye Eun!

781
00:28:48,626 --> 00:28:49,759
What a serve.

782
00:28:50,427 --> 00:28:53,729
That was a much-needed point
right when they needed it.

783
00:28:54,164 --> 00:28:55,998
And she went right at Seon Ah.

784
00:28:57,268 --> 00:28:58,201
It's okay.

785
00:28:58,202 --> 00:28:59,369
My bad.

786
00:29:00,271 --> 00:29:01,171
I'll cover it.

787
00:29:01,338 --> 00:29:03,373
Seon Ah, you have to call out
your signs early.

788
00:29:03,374 --> 00:29:05,508
I've got it.

789
00:29:06,877 --> 00:29:09,245
(Fourth set, Pohang Sports Council 15
: Wonder Dogs 19)

790
00:29:09,246 --> 00:29:10,546
Let's go right away.

791
00:29:10,547 --> 00:29:11,614
Let's go.

792
00:29:12,082 --> 00:29:14,920
Even though we know the Wonder Dogs well,
it's still a tough match.

793
00:29:15,453 --> 00:29:17,387
Still, as Pohang's captain,
I have to step up.

794
00:29:18,322 --> 00:29:19,722
We have to win this.

795
00:29:20,257 --> 00:29:22,225
Let's lock in.

796
00:29:22,426 --> 00:29:23,896
I'll cover the deep serves.

797
00:29:24,328 --> 00:29:26,562
Let's chip away at the lead.

798
00:29:26,563 --> 00:29:27,930
(Captain Seon Ah rallies her team.)

799
00:29:28,199 --> 00:29:31,234
- We have to bounce back.
- Let's do it!

800
00:29:32,569 --> 00:29:34,069
Chae Min, contact it high and swing fast.

801
00:29:34,238 --> 00:29:35,104
Let's go.

802
00:29:38,542 --> 00:29:39,509
Serve.

803
00:29:39,510 --> 00:29:40,543
(Ye Eun serves again.)

804
00:29:41,712 --> 00:29:42,612
(Rattled)

805
00:29:42,613 --> 00:29:43,613
Hit it.

806
00:29:43,614 --> 00:29:44,817
Shaky pass.

807
00:29:44,840 --> 00:29:45,450
Hurry.

808
00:29:45,516 --> 00:29:47,216
Just swing already!

809
00:29:47,217 --> 00:29:48,051
It's a high ball.

810
00:29:48,052 --> 00:29:49,252
Swing!

811
00:29:50,021 --> 00:29:51,987
Chae Min with the open spike.

812
00:29:52,222 --> 00:29:53,422
(Oh no.)

813
00:29:54,291 --> 00:29:55,157
Nice job.

814
00:29:57,561 --> 00:30:00,396
Chae Min has great placement...

815
00:30:00,397 --> 00:30:01,765
and plenty of power.

816
00:30:01,766 --> 00:30:04,567
She's tough to dig
when she swings like that.

817
00:30:04,702 --> 00:30:06,202
Nice.

818
00:30:07,171 --> 00:30:09,105
Chae Min to serve.

819
00:30:09,106 --> 00:30:10,140
Serve.

820
00:30:10,407 --> 00:30:12,474
They need to watch out
for this late surge.

821
00:30:14,545 --> 00:30:16,315
Dang it. Ye Eun, go!

822
00:30:16,647 --> 00:30:18,314
That's an ace.

823
00:30:18,649 --> 00:30:20,016
Nice.

824
00:30:22,120 --> 00:30:26,523
Pohang Sports Council is steadily
closing the gap.

825
00:30:26,524 --> 00:30:29,692
We might actually see a fifth set.

826
00:30:29,693 --> 00:30:30,930
Please, don't jinx it.

827
00:30:31,028 --> 00:30:31,894
Right.

828
00:30:32,296 --> 00:30:34,029
(Led by Captain Seon Ah,)

829
00:30:34,030 --> 00:30:36,165
(Pohang Sports Council closes in.)

830
00:30:36,166 --> 00:30:37,300
Just focus on getting the next point.

831
00:30:37,301 --> 00:30:38,868
- Stay calm.
- You've got this.

832
00:30:38,869 --> 00:30:40,937
Let's go.

833
00:30:41,197 --> 00:30:42,831
The score is 20 to 18.

834
00:30:42,973 --> 00:30:44,440
- C!
- Back-row attack.

835
00:30:44,641 --> 00:30:45,474
Clean pass.

836
00:30:45,909 --> 00:30:46,776
Young In from the back row.

837
00:30:46,777 --> 00:30:48,244
- You go.
- Chae Min with the dig.

838
00:30:48,846 --> 00:30:49,779
It's a high ball.

839
00:30:49,780 --> 00:30:50,680
Spread out!

840
00:30:50,681 --> 00:30:51,848
To Hyeon Gyeong.

841
00:30:52,316 --> 00:30:53,383
Stuffed.

842
00:30:55,385 --> 00:30:56,920
(Hyeon Ju's turn)

843
00:30:56,921 --> 00:30:58,555
- Swing!
- Put it away!

844
00:30:58,949 --> 00:31:01,250
Hyeon Ju scores off the block.

845
00:31:02,292 --> 00:31:03,626
(Cheering)

846
00:31:03,827 --> 00:31:06,095
Nice.

847
00:31:06,689 --> 00:31:08,156
- Tsubaki.
- To the center.

848
00:31:08,432 --> 00:31:09,332
Cover!

849
00:31:09,600 --> 00:31:10,833
Back set to Hyeon Ju.

850
00:31:10,858 --> 00:31:11,758
(Hyeon Ju again)

851
00:31:13,604 --> 00:31:14,470
A tip.

852
00:31:14,471 --> 00:31:16,205
- Nice.
- Good shot!

853
00:31:16,874 --> 00:31:19,409
(Fourth set, Pohang Sports Council 20
: Wonder Dogs 21)

854
00:31:19,410 --> 00:31:20,844
That was sharp.

855
00:31:22,412 --> 00:31:27,116
(Down to a one-point game again)

856
00:31:28,652 --> 00:31:29,819
That was so close.

857
00:31:30,587 --> 00:31:35,024
Pohang Sports Council is determined
to force a fifth set today.

858
00:31:35,025 --> 00:31:38,027
Right. They've got
a lot of gritty players.

859
00:31:38,028 --> 00:31:40,996
And Coach Yun Hye isn't...

860
00:31:41,398 --> 00:31:43,265
one to back down either.

861
00:31:45,869 --> 00:31:46,735
Tsubaki!

862
00:31:49,673 --> 00:31:51,707
Run A and C.

863
00:31:51,708 --> 00:31:54,810
(A and C: decoys to draw the blockers)

864
00:31:55,279 --> 00:31:59,549
(This time, it goes to Min Kyeong
instead of Young In.)

865
00:32:00,150 --> 00:32:01,984
(Se Yeon serves.)

866
00:32:02,311 --> 00:32:03,520
- Ye Eun.
- Cover!

867
00:32:03,553 --> 00:32:04,420
Tsubaki.

868
00:32:05,823 --> 00:32:07,123
(The decoy works.)

869
00:32:07,491 --> 00:32:08,324
Give me C!

870
00:32:08,626 --> 00:32:10,926
They're running C. Time your jumps!

871
00:32:12,496 --> 00:32:13,663
(A single-block opportunity!)

872
00:32:13,831 --> 00:32:15,267
Min Kyeong has been hot and cold today.

873
00:32:16,667 --> 00:32:17,567
Cross-court.

874
00:32:18,168 --> 00:32:19,034
She scores.

875
00:32:19,035 --> 00:32:21,637
(A clean kill this time)

876
00:32:22,039 --> 00:32:23,640
(Cheering)

877
00:32:24,308 --> 00:32:25,809
(Beaming with pride)

878
00:32:27,177 --> 00:32:28,144
(Nice job)

879
00:32:28,145 --> 00:32:29,779
That was huge, Min Kyeong.

880
00:32:32,249 --> 00:32:33,149
Hey!

881
00:32:34,017 --> 00:32:36,151
Why did you jump with Ye Dam?

882
00:32:36,453 --> 00:32:38,020
(Sighing)

883
00:32:38,322 --> 00:32:40,356
(The decoy play regains control.)

884
00:32:40,924 --> 00:32:43,426
(Time to close out the win)

885
00:32:44,094 --> 00:32:45,561
(Subbing in Chae Rim for Min Kyeong)

886
00:32:45,562 --> 00:32:47,229
Chae Rim checks in.

887
00:32:47,664 --> 00:32:50,699
(Substitution to shore up
back-row defense)

888
00:32:51,735 --> 00:32:53,737
She looks pretty pleased with herself.

889
00:32:53,738 --> 00:32:56,005
You can't help smiling...

890
00:32:56,006 --> 00:32:57,907
- after coming through like that.
- Definitely.

891
00:32:58,475 --> 00:32:59,708
Let's stay locked in.

892
00:33:00,144 --> 00:33:01,744
Let's go, Chae Rim.

893
00:33:02,613 --> 00:33:03,779
Chae Rim serves.

894
00:33:03,804 --> 00:33:04,940
(Chae Rim to serve.)

895
00:33:05,816 --> 00:33:06,682
Go!

896
00:33:07,117 --> 00:33:09,385
(Shaky pass)

897
00:33:09,386 --> 00:33:10,219
Give me B!

898
00:33:10,587 --> 00:33:11,788
(A hurried tip)

899
00:33:11,789 --> 00:33:13,556
- Watch the middle.
- Tsubaki!

900
00:33:13,557 --> 00:33:14,690
Tsubaki.

901
00:33:15,058 --> 00:33:15,924
Young In!

902
00:33:17,027 --> 00:33:18,364
Mine!

903
00:33:18,762 --> 00:33:20,363
- Hyeon Ju!
- Swing!

904
00:33:21,064 --> 00:33:22,631
Tip, watch the tip!

905
00:33:24,544 --> 00:33:25,277
(Yu Kyung gets a touch on the block.)

906
00:33:25,302 --> 00:33:26,169
Yu Kyung passes it.

907
00:33:26,170 --> 00:33:27,870
You have to swing!

908
00:33:28,238 --> 00:33:29,174
Dug up.

909
00:33:29,174 --> 00:33:30,075
Left!

910
00:33:30,332 --> 00:33:31,933
(Ye Eun steps in to swing.)

911
00:33:32,075 --> 00:33:32,908
Hit it!

912
00:33:34,011 --> 00:33:35,445
Ye Eun!

913
00:33:36,246 --> 00:33:37,145
(Out?)

914
00:33:37,146 --> 00:33:38,848
No touch!

915
00:33:38,849 --> 00:33:39,715
No.

916
00:33:41,485 --> 00:33:44,053
- Net touch!
- Net violation!

917
00:33:44,288 --> 00:33:46,256
(Did she touch the net?)

918
00:33:46,323 --> 00:33:47,790
No, she didn't touch it.

919
00:33:48,025 --> 00:33:49,292
Was there a net violation?

920
00:33:53,864 --> 00:33:56,032
She brushed the net on the way down.

921
00:33:56,033 --> 00:33:57,317
(Net touch on the landing)

922
00:33:58,635 --> 00:34:01,237
(Point to the Wonder Dogs)

923
00:34:01,872 --> 00:34:04,173
(Grateful for the break)

924
00:34:04,174 --> 00:34:06,642
She touched the net
while the ball was still in play.

925
00:34:08,612 --> 00:34:10,713
Oh, come on.

926
00:34:11,114 --> 00:34:11,947
Sorry.

927
00:34:12,616 --> 00:34:14,016
Let's go right away.

928
00:34:14,251 --> 00:34:15,885
Let's lock in.

929
00:34:15,886 --> 00:34:17,353
The score is 23 to 20.

930
00:34:17,554 --> 00:34:18,921
Let's get one.

931
00:34:18,922 --> 00:34:19,956
Let's go.

932
00:34:19,957 --> 00:34:22,091
(One point away from match point)

933
00:34:22,893 --> 00:34:24,260
(The game continues.)

934
00:34:24,604 --> 00:34:25,437
(Rattled)

935
00:34:25,462 --> 00:34:26,295
Hit it!

936
00:34:26,296 --> 00:34:27,463
(Scrambling to dig a tip)

937
00:34:27,464 --> 00:34:28,297
Hit it!

938
00:34:29,142 --> 00:34:30,042
(Bump set to Gyeong Hyeon)

939
00:34:30,067 --> 00:34:30,967
To Gyeong Hyeon.

940
00:34:30,968 --> 00:34:31,934
Swing!

941
00:34:32,203 --> 00:34:33,135
Hit it deep!

942
00:34:34,004 --> 00:34:34,784
That's right!

943
00:34:36,840 --> 00:34:37,906
Dug up in the back row.

944
00:34:38,145 --> 00:34:39,171
(A chance to turn the tide)

945
00:34:39,843 --> 00:34:40,810
Tsubaki with the bump set.

946
00:34:40,811 --> 00:34:42,411
Time your jumps!

947
00:34:43,139 --> 00:34:43,939
Ye Eun's shot.

948
00:34:44,767 --> 00:34:46,267
Hyeon Ju keeps it alive.

949
00:34:46,383 --> 00:34:47,416
(Relentless defense)

950
00:34:47,417 --> 00:34:48,387
Hit it!

951
00:34:48,785 --> 00:34:49,618
To the middle.

952
00:34:50,454 --> 00:34:51,654
Tsubaki digs it up.

953
00:34:52,055 --> 00:34:52,988
Mine!

954
00:34:53,157 --> 00:34:54,090
I'm covering.

955
00:34:54,316 --> 00:34:55,193
Swing!

956
00:34:55,218 --> 00:34:56,628
A spike from Young In!

957
00:34:57,928 --> 00:35:00,062
(Dangerous transition)

958
00:35:00,697 --> 00:35:03,032
(The set goes to Gyeong Hyeon.)

959
00:35:03,267 --> 00:35:04,703
Hit it deep!

960
00:35:07,404 --> 00:35:10,840
Ye Dam stuffs it!

961
00:35:10,841 --> 00:35:11,774
That's it.

962
00:35:11,799 --> 00:35:14,200
(A brick wall by Ye Dam)

963
00:35:14,503 --> 00:35:16,371
(Cheering)

964
00:35:16,913 --> 00:35:18,280
(Sighing)

965
00:35:18,305 --> 00:35:18,983
My bad.

966
00:35:19,050 --> 00:35:20,872
Ho Bin, you have to put it away!

967
00:35:23,121 --> 00:35:25,221
A huge block at the most critical moment!

968
00:35:25,367 --> 00:35:29,325
Just one more. Stay focused.

969
00:35:29,326 --> 00:35:30,226
(Pohang Sports Council 21
: Wonder Dogs 24)

970
00:35:30,227 --> 00:35:31,763
The score is 24 to 21.

971
00:35:32,663 --> 00:35:34,998
Match point for the Wonder Dogs.

972
00:35:35,032 --> 00:35:36,712
(The Wonder Dogs' match point)

973
00:35:37,334 --> 00:35:38,567
Just one more.

974
00:35:38,568 --> 00:35:40,903
(One point away from victory)

975
00:35:41,972 --> 00:35:43,505
This is the final push.

976
00:35:43,530 --> 00:35:45,577
Someone has to step up and lead the way.

977
00:35:46,676 --> 00:35:48,443
(Someone has to seal the win.)

978
00:35:48,612 --> 00:35:50,148
Set Young In one more time.

979
00:35:52,349 --> 00:35:55,584
(Young In holds the final key.)

980
00:35:56,153 --> 00:36:00,956
Coach chose to give me another shot.

981
00:36:02,259 --> 00:36:05,595
Just getting that opportunity...

982
00:36:05,862 --> 00:36:07,930
makes me want to work even harder.

983
00:36:08,832 --> 00:36:11,100
(Coach Kim's unwavering trust)

984
00:36:13,236 --> 00:36:14,937
(Serve Zone 4.)

985
00:36:15,659 --> 00:36:17,216
Make sure to catch it!

986
00:36:17,242 --> 00:36:18,020
(The target is Zone 4.)

987
00:36:20,477 --> 00:36:21,477
Get it.

988
00:36:21,478 --> 00:36:22,478
Shaky pass.

989
00:36:22,479 --> 00:36:23,345
Nice serve.

990
00:36:23,346 --> 00:36:24,780
- Here's our chance!
- Do it.

991
00:36:24,781 --> 00:36:25,898
Swing!

992
00:36:25,899 --> 00:36:27,627
(They just sent a free ball over.)

993
00:36:27,879 --> 00:36:28,846
(Our chance)

994
00:36:29,046 --> 00:36:29,846
Left.

995
00:36:30,146 --> 00:36:30,946
Go for B.

996
00:36:31,412 --> 00:36:32,979
(Where's the set going?)

997
00:36:33,679 --> 00:36:35,146
Key! Right away!

998
00:36:36,346 --> 00:36:38,046
(The key goes to Young In.)

999
00:36:39,579 --> 00:36:40,746
Watch the line!

1000
00:36:40,746 --> 00:36:42,379
We've got this.

1001
00:36:42,379 --> 00:36:43,646
Let's go.

1002
00:36:45,179 --> 00:36:46,712
I'll keep improving.

1003
00:36:49,779 --> 00:36:51,046
Spike!

1004
00:36:51,046 --> 00:36:52,712
(Young In puts it away.)

1005
00:36:52,713 --> 00:36:55,099
(Cheering)

1006
00:36:55,212 --> 00:36:56,746
Spike!

1007
00:36:56,746 --> 00:36:58,212
Yoon Young In!

1008
00:37:03,446 --> 00:37:05,112
(Smiling)

1009
00:37:05,212 --> 00:37:07,012
- Young In.
- Young In.

1010
00:37:08,979 --> 00:37:10,312
Thank you, Tsubaki.

1011
00:37:11,312 --> 00:37:14,246
(We won!)

1012
00:37:14,247 --> 00:37:15,425
(Yay!)

1013
00:37:16,712 --> 00:37:19,246
Against Pohang Sports Council,

1014
00:37:19,246 --> 00:37:21,212
the Wonder Dogs have won three straight.

1015
00:37:24,046 --> 00:37:26,612
Good game, Coach. Thank you.

1016
00:37:26,846 --> 00:37:29,642
The Wonder Dogs have now won...

1017
00:37:30,156 --> 00:37:31,546
three games in a row,

1018
00:37:32,446 --> 00:37:34,212
which is an incredible feat.

1019
00:37:34,879 --> 00:37:39,979
We saw much better chemistry
between them today,

1020
00:37:39,979 --> 00:37:42,512
so I'm even more excited
for their next match.

1021
00:37:42,512 --> 00:37:45,112
If you had to pick today's MVP,
who would it be?

1022
00:37:45,812 --> 00:37:50,012
I'd say Tsubaki and Young In.

1023
00:37:50,012 --> 00:37:51,812
Those two were completely in sync.

1024
00:37:51,812 --> 00:37:54,679
Right, they clicked so well today.

1025
00:37:55,812 --> 00:37:58,646
More than anything,
I think Young In must have regained...

1026
00:37:58,646 --> 00:38:00,478
a lot of confidence through today's match.

1027
00:38:02,446 --> 00:38:04,079
(During the pre-game warm-up)

1028
00:38:04,079 --> 00:38:05,678
Young In, are you feeling the pressure?

1029
00:38:06,079 --> 00:38:07,879
No, I'm not.

1030
00:38:07,879 --> 00:38:10,512
I'm just worried about my hitting.

1031
00:38:10,846 --> 00:38:12,912
- Are you starting today?
- Yes.

1032
00:38:14,312 --> 00:38:15,179
You can do it.

1033
00:38:16,212 --> 00:38:17,146
(The people rallying behind Young In)

1034
00:38:17,146 --> 00:38:18,446
Young In is in a crisis.

1035
00:38:19,312 --> 00:38:20,595
But you'll overcome it.

1036
00:38:22,779 --> 00:38:24,379
(Behind Young In's points...)

1037
00:38:25,179 --> 00:38:29,146
(The staff who gave her courage)

1038
00:38:29,646 --> 00:38:32,912
(Her teammate cheering her on
from the sidelines)

1039
00:38:32,912 --> 00:38:34,212
I have to push through.

1040
00:38:34,212 --> 00:38:36,546
I might get cut at this rate.

1041
00:38:36,546 --> 00:38:38,879
Yeon Joo, what if I get cut?

1042
00:38:40,212 --> 00:38:41,612
That's not going to happen.

1043
00:38:41,612 --> 00:38:44,312
No matter what, just believe
that you're the one who can pull it off.

1044
00:38:44,312 --> 00:38:46,512
- Play with confidence. Got it?
- Got it.

1045
00:38:48,012 --> 00:38:51,912
(And another teammate)

1046
00:38:53,479 --> 00:38:55,046
Why are you staring at me?

1047
00:38:55,746 --> 00:38:56,912
I have something to tell you.

1048
00:38:58,812 --> 00:38:59,712
Today,

1049
00:39:00,612 --> 00:39:02,179
let's forget about everything else,

1050
00:39:02,479 --> 00:39:04,246
and just focus on each other.

1051
00:39:04,246 --> 00:39:05,679
- You know what I mean?
- Okay.

1052
00:39:06,646 --> 00:39:07,646
I'm nervous too.

1053
00:39:10,046 --> 00:39:12,179
But let's not worry about anything else.

1054
00:39:12,646 --> 00:39:13,746
If you score a point,

1055
00:39:13,746 --> 00:39:15,212
I'll cheer louder than anyone.

1056
00:39:15,912 --> 00:39:17,046
And if I score a point,

1057
00:39:17,046 --> 00:39:18,446
you cheer louder than anyone.

1058
00:39:18,446 --> 00:39:20,012
I'm getting choked up.

1059
00:39:20,012 --> 00:39:21,412
That's how we move forward.

1060
00:39:21,746 --> 00:39:23,279
- Are we playing the finals today?
- You know what I mean.

1061
00:39:23,279 --> 00:39:24,646
Let's play like it's the finals.

1062
00:39:27,446 --> 00:39:31,412
(There was also a friend who celebrated
as if it were her own win.)

1063
00:39:32,646 --> 00:39:35,346
(And one more person)

1064
00:39:35,946 --> 00:39:38,912
I could clearly see
that they were improving.

1065
00:39:38,912 --> 00:39:41,146
I believed in our players.

1066
00:39:41,146 --> 00:39:42,712
I believed in them,

1067
00:39:42,712 --> 00:39:45,079
and they delivered
just as I thought they would.

1068
00:39:45,079 --> 00:39:46,112
Just as expected.

1069
00:39:46,546 --> 00:39:48,079
I knew it.

1070
00:39:48,679 --> 00:39:52,739
(And their coach,
who believed in them until the very end)

1071
00:39:53,812 --> 00:39:56,046
(Helping one player get back
on her feet...)

1072
00:39:56,479 --> 00:39:59,879
(takes the support of so many people.)

1073
00:39:59,879 --> 00:40:01,612
That's one team.

1074
00:40:01,612 --> 00:40:03,212
Doing it for the team.

1075
00:40:05,412 --> 00:40:08,112
(Teamwork saved Young In.)

1076
00:40:08,112 --> 00:40:09,879
(Smiling)

1077
00:40:10,612 --> 00:40:12,546
(Current record: 3 wins in 3 games)

1078
00:40:13,379 --> 00:40:15,879
(Undefeated win rate)

1079
00:40:17,779 --> 00:40:19,479
With three straight wins...

1080
00:40:19,979 --> 00:40:20,979
My chest is swelling...

1081
00:40:22,579 --> 00:40:23,846
I can't stop beaming with pride.

1082
00:40:23,846 --> 00:40:25,146
Even when I should be humbler.

1083
00:40:25,646 --> 00:40:27,246
Well, that's not really true.

1084
00:40:27,679 --> 00:40:32,412
It feels like the pieces of the puzzle are
finally falling into place, one by one.

1085
00:40:32,412 --> 00:40:34,512
We're getting stronger.

1086
00:40:34,512 --> 00:40:37,746
I can feel our team coming together.

1087
00:40:38,079 --> 00:40:40,179
(Until survival,)

1088
00:40:40,179 --> 00:40:44,612
(just one more win)

1089
00:40:44,612 --> 00:40:48,446
I think our biggest challenge is
keeping this team together.

1090
00:40:48,746 --> 00:40:51,279
We need to stay mentally tough,

1091
00:40:51,279 --> 00:40:52,412
and make sure we win.

1092
00:40:53,112 --> 00:40:55,346
We've made it this far.

1093
00:40:55,346 --> 00:40:57,012
If we want to reach the next level,

1094
00:40:57,012 --> 00:40:59,679
we need to face stronger opponents.

1095
00:41:00,512 --> 00:41:04,012
(Here comes their next opponent.)

1096
00:41:09,246 --> 00:41:12,646
(An overseas away game in Vietnam)

1097
00:41:15,846 --> 00:41:20,279
We knew nothing at all
about our opponents, so...

1098
00:41:21,912 --> 00:41:23,412
I was a little caught off guard.

1099
00:41:28,412 --> 00:41:30,612
(The 2022 Hangzhou Asian Games)

1100
00:41:31,679 --> 00:41:36,546
(South Korea vs. Vietnam)

1101
00:41:38,946 --> 00:41:42,212
(The shocking reverse-sweep loss
that left everyone speechless)

1102
00:41:43,212 --> 00:41:44,746
This is bad.

1103
00:41:46,079 --> 00:41:47,946
How did it come to this?

1104
00:41:48,512 --> 00:41:49,379
(The 2022 AVC Cup)

1105
00:41:49,379 --> 00:41:50,179
(The 2023 Asian Championships)

1106
00:41:50,179 --> 00:41:51,812
(The 2023 Asian Games)

1107
00:41:51,812 --> 00:41:53,712
(Vietnam wins.)

1108
00:41:53,712 --> 00:41:56,579
The Korean national team failed
to contain Vietnam's offense,

1109
00:41:56,579 --> 00:41:58,979
losing the match 3 to 2.

1110
00:41:59,279 --> 00:42:02,079
(In Vietnam's pro league,)

1111
00:42:02,079 --> 00:42:03,779
(one of the top teams)

1112
00:42:07,512 --> 00:42:08,879
(Lao Cai)

1113
00:42:09,512 --> 00:42:10,479
Lao Cai.

1114
00:42:14,812 --> 00:42:16,512
(Since its founding in 2016,)

1115
00:42:16,512 --> 00:42:18,212
(just four years later...)

1116
00:42:18,212 --> 00:42:19,246
(Runner-up in 2020)

1117
00:42:19,246 --> 00:42:20,179
(Runner-up in 2021)

1118
00:42:20,179 --> 00:42:21,079
(Runner-up in 2022)

1119
00:42:21,079 --> 00:42:21,912
(Runner-up in 2023)

1120
00:42:21,912 --> 00:42:23,112
(Runner-up in 2024)

1121
00:42:25,212 --> 00:42:26,846
(And,)

1122
00:42:27,879 --> 00:42:31,479
(they won
the 2026 Vietnam Pro Regular Season.)

1123
00:42:36,979 --> 00:42:39,812
(At the heart of Vietnam's top team,
Lao Cai,)

1124
00:42:40,446 --> 00:42:43,046
(stands a national team middle blocker...)

1125
00:42:43,646 --> 00:42:46,412
(towering at 195 cm,)

1126
00:42:47,546 --> 00:42:50,779
(who dismantled Korea,)

1127
00:42:57,412 --> 00:43:00,246
(backed by main attackers...)

1128
00:43:01,312 --> 00:43:04,079
(averaging 180 cm in height.)

1129
00:43:09,779 --> 00:43:11,379
(And another key figure...)

1130
00:43:11,379 --> 00:43:13,612
(behind Lao Cai)

1131
00:43:14,079 --> 00:43:16,512
Hello. I'm Nguyen Huu Ha,
head coach of Lao Cai.

1132
00:43:16,512 --> 00:43:21,546
(Coach Nguyen Huu Ha)

1133
00:43:22,946 --> 00:43:25,946
(A former national team star
who spent 10 years as a leading hitter)

1134
00:43:26,746 --> 00:43:29,879
(A legend of Vietnamese volleyball)

1135
00:43:29,879 --> 00:43:31,246
(After retiring,)

1136
00:43:31,246 --> 00:43:33,812
(he personally began scouting
promising young talent.)

1137
00:43:35,012 --> 00:43:36,979
(In 2019, he took over
bottom-dwelling Lao Cai.)

1138
00:43:36,979 --> 00:43:39,379
(And just one year later,)

1139
00:43:39,379 --> 00:43:43,579
(he led them to the finals...)

1140
00:43:43,579 --> 00:43:45,979
(for five straight years.)

1141
00:43:47,612 --> 00:43:51,546
(An underdog specialist)

1142
00:43:52,312 --> 00:43:54,846
(A national team captain)

1143
00:43:55,312 --> 00:43:58,046
(A pro league MVP)

1144
00:43:58,412 --> 00:44:01,479
(Two legends who have walked
a similar path)

1145
00:44:03,146 --> 00:44:06,345
If I could offer one piece of advice
to Coach Kim...

1146
00:44:08,112 --> 00:44:12,546
Rather than just criticizing players
on the court,

1147
00:44:12,546 --> 00:44:17,279
you need to help them feel comfortable
when they play.

1148
00:44:17,279 --> 00:44:21,279
That way, they can compete
with a positive mindset.

1149
00:44:21,279 --> 00:44:25,679
I'll let the results speak
for themselves on the court.

1150
00:44:28,279 --> 00:44:31,079
(The steady type)

1151
00:44:31,079 --> 00:44:34,779
(vs. the passionate type)

1152
00:44:34,979 --> 00:44:36,979
(A showdown between two legends)

1153
00:44:37,646 --> 00:44:39,412
(Uncharted volleyball territory)

1154
00:44:40,879 --> 00:44:42,812
(Their first overseas away game)

1155
00:44:46,746 --> 00:44:49,279
(Facing the ultimate test for survival)

1156
00:44:51,179 --> 00:44:55,146
(Episode 7: The Wall)

1157
00:44:55,579 --> 00:44:59,146
This might be a tough match.

1158
00:44:59,479 --> 00:45:01,046
I'm worried about...

1159
00:45:01,046 --> 00:45:04,279
how quickly our players will adapt
to a new environment,

1160
00:45:04,279 --> 00:45:05,479
and perform at their best.

1161
00:45:05,479 --> 00:45:07,346
That's what I'm worried about.

1162
00:45:07,912 --> 00:45:09,579
No matter who we face...

1163
00:45:09,946 --> 00:45:11,012
we have to win, of course.

1164
00:45:11,512 --> 00:45:14,479
We'll do our best to make it
four wins in a row.

1165
00:45:15,579 --> 00:45:17,912
I think we're at a clear disadvantage.

1166
00:45:18,546 --> 00:45:20,246
I'm a little worried,

1167
00:45:20,246 --> 00:45:22,312
but I still think we have a shot.

1168
00:45:22,746 --> 00:45:24,546
I really want to win.

1169
00:45:26,046 --> 00:45:30,112
(Just one more win until survival.)

1170
00:45:30,646 --> 00:45:32,479
(They must overcome...)

1171
00:45:32,479 --> 00:45:34,579
(the wall that is Vietnam.)

1172
00:45:34,979 --> 00:45:37,612
(Intense physical training)

1173
00:45:38,746 --> 00:45:39,746
Have some of this.

1174
00:45:40,146 --> 00:45:41,779
Vietnam is really hot.

1175
00:45:41,779 --> 00:45:42,679
Really?

1176
00:45:42,679 --> 00:45:44,412
You need to stay hydrated,

1177
00:45:44,412 --> 00:45:46,812
so you can give it your all
when it matters most.

1178
00:45:47,079 --> 00:45:49,012
(Everyone takes
a refreshing drink together.)

1179
00:45:49,012 --> 00:45:52,146
- Let's train hard!
- Let's go.

1180
00:45:54,079 --> 00:45:55,046
Good job.

1181
00:45:57,312 --> 00:45:59,346
Your hands are a little too high
right now.

1182
00:45:59,346 --> 00:46:00,212
Understood?

1183
00:46:02,646 --> 00:46:03,612
(Tapping)

1184
00:46:04,112 --> 00:46:05,546
Sorry to interrupt, but...

1185
00:46:05,546 --> 00:46:06,346
Bo Been is...

1186
00:46:07,179 --> 00:46:08,278
She's hurting right now.

1187
00:46:08,446 --> 00:46:11,446
(An urgent message
from the training staff)

1188
00:46:12,179 --> 00:46:14,146
(A call is made immediately.)

1189
00:46:14,146 --> 00:46:16,146
- Sang Hwa, it's me.
- Yes.

1190
00:46:16,512 --> 00:46:19,146
Bo Been says she's in pain.

1191
00:46:19,146 --> 00:46:22,946
Even if she only does half the session,
she'll still be in pain.

1192
00:46:24,379 --> 00:46:28,106
(Did Bo Been get injured?)

1193
00:46:28,421 --> 00:46:30,555
I mean, how can we make her train?

1194
00:46:31,291 --> 00:46:32,091
In that condition?

1195
00:46:32,092 --> 00:46:33,125
(The phone call drags on.)

1196
00:46:33,693 --> 00:46:37,763
(Bo Been missed all of today's training.)

1197
00:46:37,764 --> 00:46:41,833
She's been dealing with a string
of muscle injuries lately.

1198
00:46:42,068 --> 00:46:45,337
Every time I think she's finally ready
to step up in a match, she gets hurt.

1199
00:46:46,206 --> 00:46:47,239
This side.

1200
00:46:47,240 --> 00:46:50,442
(She heads straight
to the hospital for an exam.)

1201
00:46:50,810 --> 00:46:54,279
(Waiting for the test results)

1202
00:46:54,814 --> 00:46:56,281
I'm back.

1203
00:46:57,383 --> 00:47:02,187
She was diagnosed
with a grade one abdominal strain.

1204
00:47:02,188 --> 00:47:05,791
They say it's mild, but apparently
she's been in pain since yesterday.

1205
00:47:06,259 --> 00:47:08,128
I don't think we can keep
pushing her to train...

1206
00:47:08,129 --> 00:47:09,261
- in that condition...
- Exactly.

1207
00:47:09,863 --> 00:47:12,164
- It's going to be tough.
- I don't think it'll be easy.

1208
00:47:12,985 --> 00:47:17,860
(Is her injury serious enough
to keep her out of the lineup?)

1209
00:47:18,277 --> 00:47:20,378
A lot of people find it surprising.

1210
00:47:20,379 --> 00:47:21,646
(What makes an abdominal injury
so serious?)

1211
00:47:21,647 --> 00:47:23,181
When volleyball players swing,

1212
00:47:23,182 --> 00:47:26,784
they arch their backs quite a bit.

1213
00:47:26,785 --> 00:47:31,022
That puts a lot of strain
on the core muscles being stretched here.

1214
00:47:31,023 --> 00:47:33,124
And when that strain builds up,

1215
00:47:33,125 --> 00:47:35,693
it can lead to serious injuries.

1216
00:47:35,694 --> 00:47:36,928
I've been through it myself.

1217
00:47:36,929 --> 00:47:38,897
(Coach Yeon Koung suffered the same injury
during her playing career.)

1218
00:47:39,298 --> 00:47:41,599
It's a particularly tricky injury.

1219
00:47:41,834 --> 00:47:44,569
That's because you engage your abs
and back muscles...

1220
00:47:44,570 --> 00:47:47,672
for practically everything.

1221
00:47:47,940 --> 00:47:51,542
Even when you're just sitting like this,
you're using your core.

1222
00:47:51,543 --> 00:47:53,744
So it can hurt
even when you're just sitting still.

1223
00:47:54,213 --> 00:47:56,314
It's very hard to manage,

1224
00:47:56,682 --> 00:47:58,183
and even after you recover
and return to the court,

1225
00:47:58,184 --> 00:48:01,753
there's a high risk of reinjury.

1226
00:48:01,754 --> 00:48:04,555
The doctors said we'd need to monitor...

1227
00:48:04,556 --> 00:48:06,557
her condition for about a week.

1228
00:48:07,293 --> 00:48:10,529
(With less than five days
until the next match)

1229
00:48:10,964 --> 00:48:11,963
It hurts.

1230
00:48:11,964 --> 00:48:14,299
(Bo Been's chances of recovering
in time remain uncertain.)

1231
00:48:14,300 --> 00:48:17,168
- If her condition gets worse...
- That would be a serious problem.

1232
00:48:17,169 --> 00:48:20,305
It's a risk we'd have to weigh.

1233
00:48:20,306 --> 00:48:22,607
We're already down two players.
This is a disaster.

1234
00:48:22,775 --> 00:48:24,776
What are we going to do?
Her season could be over.

1235
00:48:25,111 --> 00:48:29,114
(For now, they decide to let her rest
and monitor her recovery.)

1236
00:48:29,115 --> 00:48:32,718
Yeah, I don't think she'll be able to play
in the next match.

1237
00:48:32,719 --> 00:48:33,719
(Bo Been will miss the match
against Lao Cai.)

1238
00:48:33,720 --> 00:48:36,055
As you all know,

1239
00:48:36,056 --> 00:48:38,390
we're flying out to Vietnam on Thursday.

1240
00:48:38,524 --> 00:48:40,792
(Bo Been's spot remains empty.)

1241
00:48:41,027 --> 00:48:44,562
It looks like two more players won't be
able to make the trip with us.

1242
00:48:44,797 --> 00:48:46,865
Bo Been isn't doing well either.

1243
00:48:46,866 --> 00:48:48,166
(Two more players missing?)

1244
00:48:48,167 --> 00:48:50,635
Enkhsoyol can't come
because she has a college tournament.

1245
00:48:53,239 --> 00:48:54,306
And Tsubaki too.

1246
00:48:54,640 --> 00:48:56,507
It looks like neither of them
will be able to join us.

1247
00:48:57,376 --> 00:48:59,877
Not having our full roster together...

1248
00:48:59,878 --> 00:49:01,379
could make things tough.

1249
00:49:03,516 --> 00:49:05,917
But I heard Enkhsoyol has to play
in a tournament.

1250
00:49:05,918 --> 00:49:08,487
Apparently,
her tournament starts on the 16th.

1251
00:49:08,488 --> 00:49:11,189
So she won't be able to join us
starting on the 14th.

1252
00:49:11,190 --> 00:49:12,090
(Enkhsoyol has to compete
in a college tournament.)

1253
00:49:12,580 --> 00:49:16,149
(Unfortunately,
it clashes with the Vietnam trip.)

1254
00:49:16,384 --> 00:49:17,284
What are we going to do?

1255
00:49:18,786 --> 00:49:20,787
Coach,
did you know Tsubaki couldn't go either?

1256
00:49:21,522 --> 00:49:24,057
I'd heard something about it,
but is it final?

1257
00:49:24,058 --> 00:49:25,425
Yeah, she can't. Because of her visa.

1258
00:49:26,727 --> 00:49:30,797
(Tsubaki is on a visa
for her activities in Korea.)

1259
00:49:31,599 --> 00:49:35,168
(Traveling in and out of the country
is complicated.)

1260
00:49:36,003 --> 00:49:39,706
(Three key players who helped lead
the team to victory in previous matches)

1261
00:49:41,942 --> 00:49:44,644
(All three are unavailable.)

1262
00:49:44,912 --> 00:49:47,881
Then 11... 12. So we're heading
to Vietnam with 12 players.

1263
00:49:48,416 --> 00:49:49,983
I heard the Vietnamese team...

1264
00:49:50,551 --> 00:49:53,887
will have a middle blocker
who's even taller than Thuy.

1265
00:49:54,088 --> 00:49:56,756
And apparently, a player who's been...

1266
00:49:56,757 --> 00:49:59,325
on the Vietnamese national team
will be playing too.

1267
00:49:59,326 --> 00:50:00,727
Her name is Tran Tu Linh.

1268
00:50:00,728 --> 00:50:03,463
Their roster keeps changing.

1269
00:50:03,864 --> 00:50:07,266
I'll get the updated list and report back
once everything is confirmed.

1270
00:50:08,269 --> 00:50:09,903
It's a pretty serious situation.

1271
00:50:10,271 --> 00:50:12,806
It feels like things keep piling up
as we go,

1272
00:50:13,074 --> 00:50:17,210
with one obstacle after another...

1273
00:50:17,912 --> 00:50:20,146
Yeah,
it's definitely not an easy situation.

1274
00:50:20,649 --> 00:50:23,550
But... I... Well...

1275
00:50:23,812 --> 00:50:25,111
I don't think we'll have a problem.

1276
00:50:25,152 --> 00:50:26,019
Why?

1277
00:50:26,087 --> 00:50:27,420
It's not that I'm overconfident.

1278
00:50:28,522 --> 00:50:30,256
I just think we've prepared well.

1279
00:50:31,092 --> 00:50:34,494
(On the day of the match
against Pohang Sports Council)

1280
00:50:34,696 --> 00:50:38,031
(The performance analyst keeps
checking something.)

1281
00:50:41,669 --> 00:50:44,504
(Footage of their next opponent, Lao Cai)

1282
00:50:44,939 --> 00:50:48,341
(Scouting Match 4
before they've even played Match 3?)

1283
00:50:48,342 --> 00:50:52,078
We've already done our homework,

1284
00:50:53,147 --> 00:50:54,514
so I have a feeling things will be fine...

1285
00:50:55,082 --> 00:50:56,783
Have you finished cutting
the Vietnam footage yet?

1286
00:50:56,784 --> 00:50:57,817
- Yes.
- Already?

1287
00:50:57,818 --> 00:51:00,586
(1. Requests video analysis
right after Matches 1 and 2.)

1288
00:51:00,587 --> 00:51:03,890
(2. Then requests opponent analysis
from coaching staff.)

1289
00:51:04,225 --> 00:51:06,526
When should we finish reviewing them?

1290
00:51:07,094 --> 00:51:08,361
Let's say...

1291
00:51:09,530 --> 00:51:10,463
- The day after tomorrow?
- Okay.

1292
00:51:10,464 --> 00:51:11,898
All right, the day after tomorrow, then.
By Saturday.

1293
00:51:11,899 --> 00:51:12,866
That's right.

1294
00:51:13,801 --> 00:51:16,870
(Alongside the video analysis)

1295
00:51:17,071 --> 00:51:18,505
Are you working on the attack charts?

1296
00:51:18,506 --> 00:51:20,240
(3. Dives right into preparing
the scouting report.)

1297
00:51:20,241 --> 00:51:21,107
Send me what you have.

1298
00:51:21,675 --> 00:51:23,042
This... Okay.

1299
00:51:24,545 --> 00:51:26,779
(An urgent request)

1300
00:51:27,042 --> 00:51:28,608
Make some training plans.

1301
00:51:28,609 --> 00:51:30,424
(3. Develops a training plan
for the Lao Cai match based on the data)

1302
00:51:30,425 --> 00:51:31,393
We need to pinpoint...

1303
00:51:31,418 --> 00:51:33,753
exactly what to drill against Vietnam.

1304
00:51:33,754 --> 00:51:36,088
(Coach Kim has prepared
for every possible scenario.)

1305
00:51:36,089 --> 00:51:37,957
We have a group chat with all the staff,

1306
00:51:37,958 --> 00:51:39,892
and we're messaging every night,
even at midnight or 1 a.m.

1307
00:51:39,893 --> 00:51:42,361
"Are the videos done yet? Why aren't
they up? What's taking so long?"

1308
00:51:42,362 --> 00:51:44,964
When we finish the tasks
she assigns us and upload them,

1309
00:51:45,433 --> 00:51:47,834
she replies almost immediately,
even in the middle of the night.

1310
00:51:47,835 --> 00:51:49,169
I heard she even texts you
on your days off.

1311
00:51:49,170 --> 00:51:51,705
Have we ever had a day off?

1312
00:51:53,407 --> 00:51:54,374
Coach Tae Young?

1313
00:51:54,375 --> 00:51:55,575
(Of course not.)

1314
00:51:56,911 --> 00:51:58,111
What's this down here?

1315
00:51:58,112 --> 00:52:01,181
This is for when they pass and attack...

1316
00:52:01,615 --> 00:52:07,186
(Through countless meetings,)

1317
00:52:08,422 --> 00:52:14,227
(they fine-tune every last detail.)

1318
00:52:14,695 --> 00:52:19,866
(Game plans built
on the staff's blood, sweat, and tears)

1319
00:52:20,401 --> 00:52:25,338
(Prepared for every possible scenario)

1320
00:52:25,339 --> 00:52:26,706
We need to keep them...

1321
00:52:26,707 --> 00:52:28,408
(Blocking strategy)

1322
00:52:28,409 --> 00:52:29,810
(Counterattack and speed strategy)

1323
00:52:29,811 --> 00:52:30,741
(Attack strategy)

1324
00:52:30,742 --> 00:52:32,746
We need to disrupt them
so they can't run a fast offense.

1325
00:52:32,880 --> 00:52:35,015
Goodness. Would you even get it...

1326
00:52:35,016 --> 00:52:36,449
if I broke down all the details?

1327
00:52:37,985 --> 00:52:40,720
(She's all-in on preparing
for the Vietnam match.)

1328
00:52:40,721 --> 00:52:44,324
Once I feel like we've covered everything
from A to Z,

1329
00:52:44,325 --> 00:52:45,792
I feel confident.

1330
00:52:46,061 --> 00:52:47,727
I think we'll be fine,

1331
00:52:47,728 --> 00:52:49,529
(After all those preparations,
she can say this.)

1332
00:52:50,397 --> 00:52:51,879
I don't foresee any issues.

1333
00:52:54,068 --> 00:52:57,504
(Training for the match against Lao Cai)

1334
00:52:58,672 --> 00:52:59,872
(Glancing)

1335
00:52:59,974 --> 00:53:02,676
(A 2-meter blocker from Team Korea
makes an appearance.)

1336
00:53:03,444 --> 00:53:05,045
That's it. Nice shot.

1337
00:53:05,046 --> 00:53:06,179
(They hit around the block.)

1338
00:53:06,180 --> 00:53:07,113
Okay.

1339
00:53:09,483 --> 00:53:10,283
Hey!

1340
00:53:10,284 --> 00:53:11,117
(Everyone is swinging
around the blockers?)

1341
00:53:11,118 --> 00:53:12,151
Okay.

1342
00:53:12,687 --> 00:53:15,722
After scouting Vietnam's matches,

1343
00:53:15,923 --> 00:53:19,192
I think our top priority is raising...

1344
00:53:19,193 --> 00:53:20,860
our hitting efficiency.

1345
00:53:21,227 --> 00:53:25,431
Their middle blockers are definitely tall,

1346
00:53:25,432 --> 00:53:27,867
so the key is to use that height
against them.

1347
00:53:27,868 --> 00:53:29,401
The Vietnamese players have serious size,

1348
00:53:29,637 --> 00:53:32,406
so there's no point trying to power
straight through them.

1349
00:53:32,407 --> 00:53:34,174
You know how we hit those sharp cut shots?

1350
00:53:34,175 --> 00:53:35,976
Those are a great option this time.

1351
00:53:35,977 --> 00:53:38,478
If you have the angle, take it.

1352
00:53:38,579 --> 00:53:41,114
And mix in tips too.

1353
00:53:41,181 --> 00:53:43,616
When you swing deep, the ball often
gets stuffed or rebounds off the block.

1354
00:53:43,617 --> 00:53:44,717
So swing deep,

1355
00:53:45,019 --> 00:53:47,020
push it to the middle, or tip into Zone 3.

1356
00:53:47,021 --> 00:53:48,521
Always keep those options in mind.

1357
00:53:48,889 --> 00:53:53,926
(A game plan to beat the block
with placement rather than power)

1358
00:53:55,162 --> 00:53:55,995
(The shots fly past the blockers.)

1359
00:53:55,996 --> 00:53:57,230
That's it. Nice.

1360
00:53:59,366 --> 00:54:00,433
That's it.

1361
00:54:01,669 --> 00:54:04,004
Right on, Min Kyeong. Good read.

1362
00:54:04,005 --> 00:54:05,839
Even in our final practice,

1363
00:54:05,840 --> 00:54:09,442
so many players kept showing growth.

1364
00:54:10,010 --> 00:54:12,177
It gives me confidence that we can hold...

1365
00:54:12,178 --> 00:54:14,246
our own against any team.

1366
00:54:15,783 --> 00:54:18,151
(The day of the Vietnam trip)

1367
00:54:18,855 --> 00:54:19,587
(Bo Been flies out with the team too.)

1368
00:54:19,588 --> 00:54:22,590
The cabin is so clean and nice.
It's really comfortable.

1369
00:54:22,591 --> 00:54:23,758
Seriously, so comfortable.

1370
00:54:24,060 --> 00:54:25,827
Let's go out there and play well.
And stay injury-free.

1371
00:54:26,028 --> 00:54:27,729
- We can win, right?
- We've got this.

1372
00:54:31,495 --> 00:54:34,063
(Vietnam)

1373
00:54:34,732 --> 00:54:36,933
It was really hot.
The sun was blazing too.

1374
00:54:37,768 --> 00:54:38,935
Gosh, it's so hot.

1375
00:54:38,936 --> 00:54:41,871
It was hot, humid, and sticky.

1376
00:54:43,040 --> 00:54:45,408
I knew our players were going
to have a tough time.

1377
00:54:45,643 --> 00:54:47,811
Everyone says this is a must-have.

1378
00:54:47,912 --> 00:54:49,112
I feel totally bare without it too.

1379
00:54:49,113 --> 00:54:50,113
(Coach Kim's routine
when traveling abroad)

1380
00:54:50,414 --> 00:54:52,949
It soothes and firms up your skin
when you put it on.

1381
00:54:53,884 --> 00:54:58,554
(She keeps her skin protected
even in the heat.)

1382
00:54:59,691 --> 00:55:02,191
We're not really passing through downtown,
are we?

1383
00:55:02,626 --> 00:55:05,695
This is the main road
from Da Nang to Hoi An.

1384
00:55:06,398 --> 00:55:08,365
The ocean is right over there on the left.

1385
00:55:08,366 --> 00:55:10,800
(Heading from Da Nang to Hoi An)

1386
00:55:10,801 --> 00:55:14,304
We're going to Hoi An because
there's apparently a festival happening.

1387
00:55:14,705 --> 00:55:15,538
Hoi An.

1388
00:55:16,006 --> 00:55:19,046
There's a local festival,
and we heard there's going to be...

1389
00:55:19,047 --> 00:55:20,176
a volleyball match there.

1390
00:55:20,611 --> 00:55:23,179
(After the matchup
against Vietnam was confirmed)

1391
00:55:23,648 --> 00:55:26,914
("A Chance to Meet Coach Kim
and Watch Wonder Dogs vs. Lao Cai")

1392
00:55:26,915 --> 00:55:28,745
(Da Nang City Volleyball Federation
actively promoted the match.)

1393
00:55:28,895 --> 00:55:33,029
They're hosting a major event,

1394
00:55:33,029 --> 00:55:35,062
where pros and amateurs play together.

1395
00:55:35,062 --> 00:55:37,329
Lao Cai is the pro team competing there.

1396
00:55:38,162 --> 00:55:40,495
Four of their players are taking part
in the tournament.

1397
00:55:40,795 --> 00:55:42,962
So I thought it'd be fun to go...

1398
00:55:43,462 --> 00:55:44,729
and check out the match.

1399
00:55:46,595 --> 00:55:49,595
(The sun soon sets.)

1400
00:55:50,162 --> 00:55:52,029
- Can they even play? It's dark.
- Aren't they done already?

1401
00:55:52,029 --> 00:55:53,329
Yeah, it's dark outside.

1402
00:55:53,329 --> 00:55:55,295
Are they really playing
this late at night?

1403
00:55:56,762 --> 00:55:57,795
(The car pulls up at the market.)

1404
00:55:57,795 --> 00:55:59,462
Okay, we're here.

1405
00:56:01,462 --> 00:56:02,595
That looks good.

1406
00:56:04,495 --> 00:56:05,529
Looks delicious.

1407
00:56:06,062 --> 00:56:09,429
(A vibrant night market)

1408
00:56:10,029 --> 00:56:11,795
- So this is Hoi An?
- Yes.

1409
00:56:12,062 --> 00:56:13,062
Car.

1410
00:56:13,595 --> 00:56:15,062
The traffic doesn't stop.

1411
00:56:15,062 --> 00:56:16,462
(Scooters pack the street.)

1412
00:56:16,462 --> 00:56:17,795
Look at all those scooters.

1413
00:56:20,595 --> 00:56:23,662
- I can't picture them playing here.
- I know.

1414
00:56:24,429 --> 00:56:25,962
- It's dark out.
- Right.

1415
00:56:26,595 --> 00:56:27,995
I wonder if the court has lights.

1416
00:56:27,995 --> 00:56:31,062
- The lights...
- Yeah, there should be lights.

1417
00:56:31,062 --> 00:56:33,462
(No sign of a volleyball court
in the alley)

1418
00:56:33,795 --> 00:56:34,929
Oh, what's this?

1419
00:56:34,929 --> 00:56:35,962
It's our poster.

1420
00:56:37,962 --> 00:56:40,162
There's a poster of us in Vietnam.

1421
00:56:40,395 --> 00:56:41,395
This is so cool.

1422
00:56:41,395 --> 00:56:42,429
Our poster in Da Nang.

1423
00:56:42,429 --> 00:56:43,429
It looks great.

1424
00:56:44,695 --> 00:56:45,762
This must be the festival.

1425
00:56:46,495 --> 00:56:47,495
Is this it?

1426
00:56:47,495 --> 00:56:48,595
I see a ball bouncing.

1427
00:56:49,429 --> 00:56:51,462
- Is it here?
- Could they be playing over there?

1428
00:56:53,029 --> 00:56:55,262
I think there's a game going on
over there.

1429
00:56:56,329 --> 00:56:58,129
They're actually playing volleyball.

1430
00:56:58,129 --> 00:56:59,341
(Walking across the grass)

1431
00:56:59,829 --> 00:57:00,862
Both teams, please take the court.

1432
00:57:01,662 --> 00:57:02,929
Let's give them a round of applause.

1433
00:57:02,929 --> 00:57:04,895
Which team will take the win?

1434
00:57:06,262 --> 00:57:07,762
Get in!

1435
00:57:07,762 --> 00:57:08,762
Right here!

1436
00:57:18,878 --> 00:57:22,011
(All the locals have gathered.)

1437
00:57:22,578 --> 00:57:25,678
The 2026 Women's Volleyball Tournament...

1438
00:57:25,678 --> 00:57:27,878
- is officially underway.
- Is she an emcee?

1439
00:57:27,878 --> 00:57:30,144
I've never seen a tournament
with an emcee before.

1440
00:57:30,144 --> 00:57:31,144
Cool.

1441
00:57:32,278 --> 00:57:34,711
The way they run the event is fascinating,

1442
00:57:35,111 --> 00:57:36,311
and the crowd is massive.

1443
00:57:36,311 --> 00:57:37,844
- Everyone's here.
- Yes, the whole town turned out.

1444
00:57:38,311 --> 00:57:40,911
I couldn't believe there was
a volleyball match happening there.

1445
00:57:41,178 --> 00:57:42,378
I was genuinely stunned.

1446
00:57:43,278 --> 00:57:44,311
Here?

1447
00:57:44,778 --> 00:57:45,811
In a spot like this?

1448
00:57:46,085 --> 00:57:48,118
(In the middle of town,)

1449
00:57:50,211 --> 00:57:53,244
(there's a court surrounded by grass.)

1450
00:57:54,578 --> 00:57:56,344
It felt like a public square,

1451
00:57:56,344 --> 00:57:57,978
with just a net put up.

1452
00:57:59,211 --> 00:58:01,044
Wait, that's concrete!

1453
00:58:01,711 --> 00:58:05,644
(They're playing on concrete?)

1454
00:58:05,878 --> 00:58:06,944
Have you ever played on concrete?

1455
00:58:06,944 --> 00:58:08,611
(Shaking her head)

1456
00:58:09,311 --> 00:58:10,311
Are they okay?

1457
00:58:10,311 --> 00:58:11,511
It hurts just watching.

1458
00:58:12,078 --> 00:58:13,544
Gosh, that looks painful.

1459
00:58:14,411 --> 00:58:15,411
(A diving dig)

1460
00:58:15,411 --> 00:58:16,411
That's got to hurt.

1461
00:58:16,678 --> 00:58:17,678
(Throwing themselves onto the ground)

1462
00:58:17,678 --> 00:58:18,678
I felt that.

1463
00:58:19,944 --> 00:58:21,511
The girl who went down earlier
must be sore.

1464
00:58:22,178 --> 00:58:23,311
I've never seen anything like it.

1465
00:58:23,311 --> 00:58:26,078
They were jumping
and diving straight onto concrete.

1466
00:58:26,444 --> 00:58:28,744
And I wondered what was happening...

1467
00:58:30,244 --> 00:58:31,311
around the court.

1468
00:58:31,611 --> 00:58:33,411
(There's even traditional Vietnamese
martial arts.)

1469
00:58:34,611 --> 00:58:37,144
It was a whole new world.

1470
00:58:37,144 --> 00:58:38,244
(The fighting spirit runs
deep in Vietnam.)

1471
00:58:39,011 --> 00:58:40,644
I've watched plenty of volleyball matches,

1472
00:58:40,644 --> 00:58:41,744
but never one like this.

1473
00:58:41,744 --> 00:58:43,478
Seriously, it's no joke.

1474
00:58:43,478 --> 00:58:44,844
In cities with lots of tournaments
like this,

1475
00:58:44,844 --> 00:58:47,078
some even have 100 courts.

1476
00:58:47,744 --> 00:58:50,144
- That's hard to imagine back home.
- Exactly.

1477
00:58:50,578 --> 00:58:52,544
I'm fascinated and a little envious
at the same time.

1478
00:58:57,011 --> 00:58:59,011
- Aren't those Lao Cai players?
- They are.

1479
00:58:59,578 --> 00:59:01,044
The ones we watched on tape.

1480
00:59:01,044 --> 00:59:02,778
Pay close attention to them.

1481
00:59:02,778 --> 00:59:04,344
(The players they'd studied
on tape countless times)

1482
00:59:04,578 --> 00:59:08,078
(Now seeing them on a concrete court)

1483
00:59:08,511 --> 00:59:10,578
They really are tall.

1484
00:59:11,644 --> 00:59:14,778
Where does Vietnam find players
with that kind of height?

1485
00:59:15,778 --> 00:59:19,844
(A pro team competing
in a local tournament)

1486
00:59:20,778 --> 00:59:24,644
(The atmosphere shifts.)

1487
00:59:27,244 --> 00:59:29,444
(Intrigued)

1488
00:59:30,978 --> 00:59:32,678
She's flashing a signal.

1489
00:59:33,344 --> 00:59:34,611
(Kieu Oanh's chance to swing)

1490
00:59:34,611 --> 00:59:35,611
Let's go!

1491
00:59:36,378 --> 00:59:37,444
(Stuffed)

1492
00:59:37,911 --> 00:59:40,811
(Thrilled)

1493
00:59:45,778 --> 00:59:47,011
They look completely gassed.

1494
00:59:47,011 --> 00:59:48,178
(Sweating buckets)

1495
00:59:48,178 --> 00:59:49,711
They won't go easy.

1496
00:59:51,311 --> 00:59:52,378
Set to the right.

1497
00:59:53,611 --> 00:59:54,944
(Refusing to be outdone)

1498
00:59:55,311 --> 00:59:56,311
(Heavy swings come and go.)

1499
00:59:56,311 --> 00:59:57,544
(Nodding)

1500
00:59:57,978 --> 00:59:59,044
Again!

1501
00:59:59,844 --> 01:00:01,811
(A full-power spike)

1502
01:00:02,078 --> 01:00:04,844
(Crowd going wild)

1503
01:00:07,644 --> 01:00:09,744
It's an unbelievably tight battle.

1504
01:00:14,811 --> 01:00:16,411
(With every point off the block,)

1505
01:00:16,411 --> 01:00:19,711
(the crowd cheers and groans along.)

1506
01:00:19,778 --> 01:00:21,411
No. 4 is playing great.

1507
01:00:21,411 --> 01:00:22,411
Yeah, she's pretty good.

1508
01:00:22,944 --> 01:00:24,878
And they're playing us after this.

1509
01:00:24,878 --> 01:00:25,878
I know.

1510
01:00:25,878 --> 01:00:27,611
(This is just the warm-up.)

1511
01:00:32,044 --> 01:00:34,078
(Volleyball grit forged on concrete)

1512
01:00:35,444 --> 01:00:39,478
We're witnessing something truly special.

1513
01:00:39,478 --> 01:00:40,844
(Whistle blows.)

1514
01:00:41,078 --> 01:00:44,144
(The match suddenly stops?)

1515
01:00:44,744 --> 01:00:47,678
(A player steps off the court.)

1516
01:00:47,978 --> 01:00:50,744
(A volleyball federation official
walks up to her.)

1517
01:00:53,044 --> 01:00:54,611
(Cash)

1518
01:00:55,511 --> 01:00:56,644
He just handed her cash.

1519
01:00:56,644 --> 01:01:00,078
They give players cash on the spot
when they make a great play.

1520
01:01:00,078 --> 01:01:02,211
- For a good play?
- Yes.

1521
01:01:02,611 --> 01:01:04,178
- That's awesome.
- I love that.

1522
01:01:04,178 --> 01:01:05,678
(A local tradition of handing out
cash bonuses)

1523
01:01:05,678 --> 01:01:07,144
Interesting.

1524
01:01:07,144 --> 01:01:09,811
(The cash bonus fires them up.)

1525
01:01:12,778 --> 01:01:15,078
(Intense)

1526
01:01:17,978 --> 01:01:20,378
(Everyone is locked in.)

1527
01:01:20,378 --> 01:01:22,878
Is this the Olympics? What is going on?

1528
01:01:23,111 --> 01:01:26,078
The players were so competitive.

1529
01:01:27,744 --> 01:01:29,078
They were swinging
with everything they had.

1530
01:01:29,478 --> 01:01:32,911
I was like,
"Are they really going all out?"

1531
01:01:32,911 --> 01:01:34,011
Still...

1532
01:01:34,478 --> 01:01:37,244
I was drawn into Vietnamese volleyball,

1533
01:01:37,244 --> 01:01:38,578
and how seriously they took the game.

1534
01:01:40,044 --> 01:01:41,878
There was something
really captivating about it.

1535
01:01:41,878 --> 01:01:42,878
(Fierce Vietnamese volleyball)

1536
01:01:42,878 --> 01:01:45,544
We definitely need to be sharp
for tomorrow's match.

1537
01:01:46,278 --> 01:01:48,344
(Match day)

1538
01:02:01,411 --> 01:02:04,044
(Tien Son Sports Center)

1539
01:02:08,844 --> 01:02:12,378
(Da Nang's premier international arena)

1540
01:02:12,878 --> 01:02:16,244
(For today's match,)

1541
01:02:18,511 --> 01:02:22,244
(the local Vietnamese crew is out
in full force.)

1542
01:02:22,878 --> 01:02:27,378
(The local PA announcer)

1543
01:02:27,544 --> 01:02:29,711
(Ready to call the game in both languages)

1544
01:02:33,944 --> 01:02:38,344
(From a massive jib camera...)

1545
01:02:40,911 --> 01:02:44,478
(to a full local broadcast setup)

1546
01:02:46,244 --> 01:02:50,044
(Only the scoreboard is manual.)

1547
01:02:53,811 --> 01:02:56,344
(There might be a few hiccups.)

1548
01:03:06,111 --> 01:03:09,978
(A blessing ceremony for a smooth event)

1549
01:03:10,778 --> 01:03:14,911
(Amid preparations
for the international match,)

1550
01:03:15,544 --> 01:03:18,311
(the players gather in the locker room.)

1551
01:03:19,244 --> 01:03:21,311
(Opening)

1552
01:03:23,544 --> 01:03:24,544
All right.

1553
01:03:26,111 --> 01:03:30,178
Our starting lineup today is...

1554
01:03:30,644 --> 01:03:31,778
Chae Rim.

1555
01:03:31,778 --> 01:03:35,311
Ho Bin and Ye Dam,
you're our two middle blockers.

1556
01:03:35,711 --> 01:03:38,011
Hyo Rim and Yeon Joo are starting.

1557
01:03:38,344 --> 01:03:41,144
Seon Ah and Yu Kyung,
handle serve receive and defense as usual.

1558
01:03:41,144 --> 01:03:42,144
Got it?

1559
01:03:42,544 --> 01:03:43,778
Next,

1560
01:03:43,778 --> 01:03:45,811
(Who will claim
the final outside hitter spot?)

1561
01:03:46,911 --> 01:03:48,711
Min Kyeong, you're in.

1562
01:03:49,311 --> 01:03:50,711
Min Kyeong, you're starting.

1563
01:03:51,211 --> 01:03:53,344
The rest of you, stay ready too, okay?

1564
01:03:53,344 --> 01:03:54,444
- Yes, Coach.
- Good.

1565
01:03:55,178 --> 01:03:56,478
I was really surprised.

1566
01:03:57,578 --> 01:04:01,078
It's actually my first time starting
for this team.

1567
01:04:02,478 --> 01:04:05,078
I'm excited to see Min Kyeong play.

1568
01:04:05,078 --> 01:04:08,278
We're counting on her offense.

1569
01:04:09,578 --> 01:04:10,778
(Yelling)

1570
01:04:10,778 --> 01:04:11,844
(A sharp cross-court shot)

1571
01:04:11,844 --> 01:04:12,844
That's it.

1572
01:04:13,244 --> 01:04:14,844
(A crisp line shot)

1573
01:04:16,011 --> 01:04:17,111
That's the spirit.

1574
01:04:17,878 --> 01:04:20,111
- Min Kyeong, nice. Good read.
- Nice set.

1575
01:04:20,578 --> 01:04:23,911
She looks to be in great form,

1576
01:04:24,478 --> 01:04:26,844
so I decided to give her
plenty of chances.

1577
01:04:27,844 --> 01:04:29,911
I felt confident, honestly.

1578
01:04:30,511 --> 01:04:33,044
Even I feel like I'm finding my groove.

1579
01:04:33,511 --> 01:04:34,944
I'll leave everything out on the court.

1580
01:04:37,744 --> 01:04:39,878
Can the undefeated Wonder Dogs...

1581
01:04:39,878 --> 01:04:43,544
ride this momentum
and secure their survival early?

1582
01:04:44,111 --> 01:04:46,911
Missing three key players,

1583
01:04:46,911 --> 01:04:49,244
the Wonder Dogs head
into their fourth match...

1584
01:04:49,244 --> 01:04:51,211
and their first overseas away game.

1585
01:04:51,211 --> 01:04:53,611
I'm joined by commentator Yang Hyo Jin
for today's showdown...

1586
01:04:53,611 --> 01:04:55,311
against Vietnam's Lao Cai.

1587
01:04:55,311 --> 01:04:57,011
- Hello.
- Hello.

1588
01:04:57,511 --> 01:05:00,844
Their first away match
takes place in Vietnam.

1589
01:05:01,478 --> 01:05:04,778
(Lao Cai, Vietnam's pro champions)

1590
01:05:05,078 --> 01:05:07,778
They even feature Ly Thi Luyen,

1591
01:05:07,778 --> 01:05:10,411
a 195-centimeter national team
middle blocker.

1592
01:05:11,078 --> 01:05:14,244
Hyo Jin, what do you see as this
Vietnamese team's biggest strength?

1593
01:05:14,244 --> 01:05:17,511
I'd say it's their middle blockers.

1594
01:05:18,011 --> 01:05:20,693
Ly Thi Luyen is the anchor
of their defense,

1595
01:05:20,694 --> 01:05:22,644
- standing 195 centimeters tall.
- Right.

1596
01:05:23,691 --> 01:05:25,825
(Ly Thi Luyen)

1597
01:05:26,396 --> 01:05:29,664
They were on another level physically.

1598
01:05:30,033 --> 01:05:31,700
A player who's 195 centimeters tall?
That's tough.

1599
01:05:32,735 --> 01:05:35,337
And Tichaya Boonlert is a setter.

1600
01:05:36,205 --> 01:05:38,173
At 180 centimeters,
she's as tall as a middle blocker.

1601
01:05:38,174 --> 01:05:39,507
(A towering 180-centimeter setter)

1602
01:05:39,775 --> 01:05:43,411
(Tichaya Boonlert, Thai import)

1603
01:05:45,781 --> 01:05:49,784
(A cannon-blast spike)

1604
01:05:49,785 --> 01:05:52,020
That's Tran Tu Linh.

1605
01:05:52,021 --> 01:05:54,689
Right.
She's solid on both offense and defense.

1606
01:05:54,690 --> 01:05:55,890
(Tran Tu Linh,
former Vietnam national team)

1607
01:05:56,258 --> 01:05:58,526
(A rising star hitter)

1608
01:05:58,962 --> 01:06:00,962
Against such a tough opponent,

1609
01:06:01,297 --> 01:06:03,765
can the Wonder Dogs hold their own?

1610
01:06:03,766 --> 01:06:05,634
We'll have to wait and see.

1611
01:06:06,036 --> 01:06:08,070
Coach Kim Yeon Koung
and Coach Nguyen Huu Ha...

1612
01:06:08,071 --> 01:06:10,939
have a lot in common.

1613
01:06:10,940 --> 01:06:12,240
That's right.

1614
01:06:12,241 --> 01:06:15,477
Both were legends in their playing days.

1615
01:06:15,655 --> 01:06:19,190
They even have similar coaching styles.

1616
01:06:19,191 --> 01:06:20,058
(Going over tactics until the last minute)

1617
01:06:20,593 --> 01:06:21,459
Hit it.

1618
01:06:21,661 --> 01:06:23,162
Hit it, hit it!

1619
01:06:23,296 --> 01:06:24,730
Switch. Switch!

1620
01:06:25,131 --> 01:06:26,272
Move. Move your feet!

1621
01:06:26,273 --> 01:06:28,162
(Even their way of repeating seems
familiar.)

1622
01:06:28,601 --> 01:06:30,635
I'm excited to see...

1623
01:06:30,636 --> 01:06:33,071
who comes out on top today.

1624
01:06:33,072 --> 01:06:34,839
(A Vietnamese volleyball legend)

1625
01:06:35,308 --> 01:06:37,509
Lao Cai is a formidable opponent,

1626
01:06:37,510 --> 01:06:40,144
and the Wonder Dogs can't field...

1627
01:06:40,145 --> 01:06:41,679
their full-strength lineup today.

1628
01:06:42,214 --> 01:06:43,515
What if the Wonder Dogs still
pull off the win?

1629
01:06:43,983 --> 01:06:46,585
If they win, we need to launch a pro team!

1630
01:06:47,887 --> 01:06:48,820
Well, first,

1631
01:06:49,455 --> 01:06:50,789
put up about three million dollars.

1632
01:06:52,392 --> 01:06:54,126
(Cut that part.)

1633
01:06:54,594 --> 01:06:56,895
(A crowd of fans in red pours in.)

1634
01:06:57,196 --> 01:06:58,663
(Staring)

1635
01:06:58,798 --> 01:07:00,098
Here come the drums.

1636
01:07:00,666 --> 01:07:01,666
That famous big drum.

1637
01:07:02,268 --> 01:07:03,935
Vietnam takes its sports seriously.

1638
01:07:03,936 --> 01:07:05,737
And their cheering section has arrived.

1639
01:07:06,339 --> 01:07:09,273
The crowd is what makes
away games so tough, isn't it?

1640
01:07:09,274 --> 01:07:10,174
Exactly.

1641
01:07:10,509 --> 01:07:15,613
Where are the Lao Cai supporters?

1642
01:07:18,951 --> 01:07:20,151
(Drum beats)

1643
01:07:20,386 --> 01:07:21,586
(Drum beats)

1644
01:07:21,954 --> 01:07:25,123
(Deafening cheers fill the arena.)

1645
01:07:25,725 --> 01:07:29,060
They came ready to cheer their hearts out.

1646
01:07:29,962 --> 01:07:34,699
That drum was kind of distracting.

1647
01:07:35,167 --> 01:07:39,270
Pilseung Wonder Dogs and your fans,

1648
01:07:39,271 --> 01:07:40,671
where are you?

1649
01:07:41,240 --> 01:07:42,907
(Cheers)

1650
01:07:43,209 --> 01:07:45,210
(Local Koreans saw the poster
and showed up.)

1651
01:07:47,546 --> 01:07:49,781
(A small but spirited cheering section)

1652
01:07:49,782 --> 01:07:51,449
Our players could really use...

1653
01:07:51,450 --> 01:07:53,351
some extra support today,

1654
01:07:53,352 --> 01:07:54,852
so Manager Boo flew in to cheer them on.

1655
01:07:55,087 --> 01:07:57,855
He took an early flight out here.

1656
01:07:58,491 --> 01:08:00,258
Now that's dedication.

1657
01:08:00,259 --> 01:08:01,426
(Cheering on zero sleep)

1658
01:08:02,728 --> 01:08:04,462
It's so hot in here.

1659
01:08:05,264 --> 01:08:08,566
(Sweating even with the AC on)

1660
01:08:08,968 --> 01:08:10,035
Even the air feels hot.

1661
01:08:10,036 --> 01:08:12,304
(The gym feels like a sauna.)

1662
01:08:12,672 --> 01:08:15,974
It was way hotter than in Korea.

1663
01:08:15,975 --> 01:08:19,177
I remember it feeling
over 40 degrees Celsius.

1664
01:08:19,178 --> 01:08:20,011
(It feels like 40 degrees Celsius.)

1665
01:08:20,012 --> 01:08:21,112
This heat is crazy.

1666
01:08:23,115 --> 01:08:24,582
It's tough adjusting to this heat.

1667
01:08:24,583 --> 01:08:25,983
(Meanwhile, Lao Cai looks unfazed.)

1668
01:08:26,285 --> 01:08:27,919
We'll just have to give it our all.

1669
01:08:27,920 --> 01:08:29,220
(And now they have to battle the heat.)

1670
01:08:29,989 --> 01:08:33,391
The Wonder Dogs are playing overseas...

1671
01:08:33,959 --> 01:08:37,462
for the first time, taking on Lao Cai.

1672
01:08:37,563 --> 01:08:41,032
(The Fourth Match: Overcome the Wall
of the Overseas Pro Champions)

1673
01:08:41,934 --> 01:08:44,402
Here's the Wonder Dogs' starting lineup.

1674
01:08:44,403 --> 01:08:46,604
Starting in Zone One, setter Hyo Rim,

1675
01:08:46,605 --> 01:08:48,573
outside hitter Min Kyeong,

1676
01:08:48,574 --> 01:08:50,241
middle blocker Ye Dam,

1677
01:08:50,510 --> 01:08:52,343
opposite hitter Yeon Joo,

1678
01:08:52,679 --> 01:08:54,546
outside hitter Chae Rim,

1679
01:08:54,714 --> 01:08:56,414
middle blocker Ho Bin,

1680
01:08:56,649 --> 01:08:58,783
and liberos Seon Ah and Yu Kyung.

1681
01:09:01,921 --> 01:09:05,056
Now let's look at Lao Cai's starters,

1682
01:09:05,057 --> 01:09:06,591
led by Coach Nguyen Huu Ha.

1683
01:09:06,726 --> 01:09:08,260
Setter Tichaya Boonlert,

1684
01:09:08,461 --> 01:09:10,362
outside hitter Bui Hong Nhung,

1685
01:09:10,763 --> 01:09:12,497
middle blocker Nong Thuy Anh,

1686
01:09:12,798 --> 01:09:15,299
opposite hitter Nguyen Thi Kieu Oanh,

1687
01:09:15,535 --> 01:09:17,502
outside hitter Hoang Hong Hanh,

1688
01:09:17,705 --> 01:09:19,337
middle blocker Trinh Thi Huyen,

1689
01:09:19,538 --> 01:09:21,305
and libero Pham Thi Khanh Lam.

1690
01:09:23,427 --> 01:09:25,261
They lined up just as we expected.

1691
01:09:25,262 --> 01:09:26,462
Only the setter is different.

1692
01:09:26,463 --> 01:09:27,396
- Yes.
- Okay.

1693
01:09:28,565 --> 01:09:31,533
With so many key players out,

1694
01:09:31,534 --> 01:09:34,036
Coach Kim named Min Kyeong
as her key player.

1695
01:09:34,037 --> 01:09:35,771
(Key player: Min Kyeong)

1696
01:09:35,772 --> 01:09:38,908
Can Min Kyeong live up to that trust?

1697
01:09:38,909 --> 01:09:41,110
Min Kyeong looked sharp...

1698
01:09:41,111 --> 01:09:42,644
in the last match too.

1699
01:09:43,013 --> 01:09:45,814
Will she have the game of her life today?

1700
01:09:45,815 --> 01:09:46,950
I can't wait to see.

1701
01:09:46,951 --> 01:09:48,617
She looks confident.

1702
01:09:49,152 --> 01:09:51,853
Min Kyeong! Right here!

1703
01:09:51,854 --> 01:09:53,421
(Message received)

1704
01:09:54,858 --> 01:09:57,122
- Toward the middle on your approach.
- Watch the net.

1705
01:09:57,728 --> 01:09:59,962
Tichaya opens with the serve.

1706
01:09:59,963 --> 01:10:00,963
And Set One is underway.

1707
01:10:00,964 --> 01:10:01,930
Right away.

1708
01:10:02,999 --> 01:10:04,133
Hyo Rim, set me C.

1709
01:10:04,134 --> 01:10:06,134
- There you go.
- Min Kyeong on the left!

1710
01:10:06,135 --> 01:10:07,536
Swing fast!

1711
01:10:07,537 --> 01:10:08,837
Single block!

1712
01:10:08,838 --> 01:10:10,672
Just one blocker on Min Kyeong!

1713
01:10:12,342 --> 01:10:13,276
And she gets stuffed.

1714
01:10:13,277 --> 01:10:14,643
- Sorry.
- It's okay.

1715
01:10:15,145 --> 01:10:17,646
- She couldn't get past Lao Cai's block.
- Next point!

1716
01:10:17,647 --> 01:10:19,548
Those blockers are tall.

1717
01:10:20,216 --> 01:10:22,984
(Lao Cai draws first blood
with a solo block.)

1718
01:10:23,553 --> 01:10:25,387
(Smiling)

1719
01:10:25,655 --> 01:10:27,055
(Cheers)

1720
01:10:27,791 --> 01:10:30,693
(Surrounded on all sides)

1721
01:10:31,595 --> 01:10:34,096
With the Vietnamese fans out
in full force,

1722
01:10:34,097 --> 01:10:35,965
I hope our players can block
out the noise...

1723
01:10:35,966 --> 01:10:38,067
- and just play their game.
- Right.

1724
01:10:38,068 --> 01:10:39,535
It's 0 to 1.

1725
01:10:39,536 --> 01:10:42,038
Lao Cai takes the opening point.

1726
01:10:42,772 --> 01:10:44,539
Sorry.

1727
01:10:44,540 --> 01:10:48,709
Min Kyeong may have overthought that one.

1728
01:10:48,710 --> 01:10:51,380
It was her first touch,
and she really wanted to put it away.

1729
01:10:51,381 --> 01:10:52,948
She can't let it shake her.

1730
01:10:53,783 --> 01:10:55,016
Min Kyeong!

1731
01:10:55,519 --> 01:10:57,052
Take a breath. You're fine.

1732
01:10:57,053 --> 01:10:58,253
Sorry.

1733
01:10:58,421 --> 01:11:00,021
Ready! Right away!

1734
01:11:00,223 --> 01:11:01,156
Let's get it up!

1735
01:11:01,291 --> 01:11:03,425
- Right away!
- Tichaya serves again.

1736
01:11:03,426 --> 01:11:04,426
One, two!

1737
01:11:04,928 --> 01:11:06,462
You have to get that!

1738
01:11:06,730 --> 01:11:07,563
Hey!

1739
01:11:08,732 --> 01:11:09,932
(Will it clear the net?)

1740
01:11:09,933 --> 01:11:10,866
Come on!

1741
01:11:11,134 --> 01:11:12,268
Here we go!

1742
01:11:12,502 --> 01:11:13,836
- Come on!
- Hey...

1743
01:11:14,037 --> 01:11:15,037
Swing!

1744
01:11:15,038 --> 01:11:16,572
- Out-of-system set!
- Take it!

1745
01:11:16,899 --> 01:11:18,867
It catches the net.

1746
01:11:18,875 --> 01:11:22,744
(First set, Lao Cai 2 : Wonder Dogs 0)

1747
01:11:23,980 --> 01:11:25,213
(A sidelong glance)

1748
01:11:25,515 --> 01:11:27,049
(Sharp stare)

1749
01:11:27,650 --> 01:11:28,717
Focus.

1750
01:11:29,052 --> 01:11:30,953
(Cool and collected)

1751
01:11:30,954 --> 01:11:31,987
Just a little more.

1752
01:11:32,555 --> 01:11:34,189
- Min Kyeong, just a little more!
- Sorry.

1753
01:11:34,190 --> 01:11:35,190
- Sorry.
- It's okay.

1754
01:11:35,191 --> 01:11:37,159
What's wrong with me?

1755
01:11:37,794 --> 01:11:39,194
- It's 0 to 2.
- It's okay. Stay calm.

1756
01:11:39,596 --> 01:11:41,464
Min Kyeong, settle down.

1757
01:11:41,465 --> 01:11:43,065
- What's there to be nervous about?
- Yes, Coach.

1758
01:11:44,434 --> 01:11:47,536
Min Kyeong got blocked
on her very first swing,

1759
01:11:47,837 --> 01:11:49,871
and it seems to have rattled her.

1760
01:11:49,872 --> 01:11:52,141
She looks a little flustered.

1761
01:11:52,142 --> 01:11:53,509
- It's okay.
- Sorry.

1762
01:11:54,177 --> 01:11:57,246
It was my first start,

1763
01:11:57,880 --> 01:12:00,549
and I think I was pressing too hard.

1764
01:12:01,651 --> 01:12:03,518
- Watch her coming in.
- Watch the middle.

1765
01:12:03,920 --> 01:12:06,655
She's coming fast. Time it. You're good.

1766
01:12:07,357 --> 01:12:08,357
- Go for it.
- Mine!

1767
01:12:08,625 --> 01:12:09,658
Clean pass.

1768
01:12:09,893 --> 01:12:10,759
Good.

1769
01:12:11,462 --> 01:12:12,394
Cover!

1770
01:12:12,395 --> 01:12:14,196
They keep it alive. Yeon Joo tips it,

1771
01:12:14,364 --> 01:12:15,464
and scores.

1772
01:12:15,465 --> 01:12:18,167
Once again,
Yeon Joo finds a way to score...

1773
01:12:18,168 --> 01:12:20,936
without swinging hard.

1774
01:12:22,005 --> 01:12:24,039
(Even the small cheering section erupts.)

1775
01:12:24,541 --> 01:12:26,242
It's okay.

1776
01:12:26,476 --> 01:12:27,576
Sorry.

1777
01:12:27,577 --> 01:12:29,378
Don't panic. It's okay. It happens.

1778
01:12:29,379 --> 01:12:30,946
- Sorry.
- Don't panic.

1779
01:12:30,947 --> 01:12:33,081
That's it. Good job.

1780
01:12:33,082 --> 01:12:35,184
Min Kyeong, you're fine.

1781
01:12:35,185 --> 01:12:37,319
- It's okay. Find your rhythm.
- Yes, Coach.

1782
01:12:40,757 --> 01:12:42,991
- The setter is in Zone One.
- Okay.

1783
01:12:43,593 --> 01:12:45,627
(Targeting Zone 1)

1784
01:12:47,097 --> 01:12:49,999
Serve to Zone One, Ye Dam.
That takes No. 22 out of the play.

1785
01:12:50,634 --> 01:12:52,167
It's a slide attack.

1786
01:12:58,775 --> 01:12:59,742
Just one.

1787
01:13:03,613 --> 01:13:04,680
Min Kyeong serves.

1788
01:13:05,849 --> 01:13:08,350
- Bui Hong Nhung struggles on the receive.
- Good.

1789
01:13:09,018 --> 01:13:10,118
Overpass!

1790
01:13:11,254 --> 01:13:13,288
And she puts it away.

1791
01:13:13,809 --> 01:13:15,877
(First set, Lao Cai 3 : Wonder Dogs 1)

1792
01:13:16,359 --> 01:13:17,960
Good job.

1793
01:13:18,027 --> 01:13:19,861
She put a little spin on that shot,

1794
01:13:19,862 --> 01:13:23,131
making it tough to dig.

1795
01:13:23,733 --> 01:13:24,900
One more!

1796
01:13:24,901 --> 01:13:27,235
They definitely have the height advantage,

1797
01:13:27,236 --> 01:13:30,172
and we let them dictate the pace early on.

1798
01:13:30,340 --> 01:13:31,340
It's okay.

1799
01:13:31,341 --> 01:13:33,475
- One more.
- Stay locked in.

1800
01:13:33,476 --> 01:13:35,177
(They can't let Lao Cai pull away.)

1801
01:13:36,112 --> 01:13:38,180
(The rookie coach's next move)

1802
01:13:38,414 --> 01:13:39,381
Yeon Joo, again.

1803
01:13:40,884 --> 01:13:42,184
(Got it.)

1804
01:13:42,653 --> 01:13:44,120
It's okay. Let's get a point back.

1805
01:13:44,121 --> 01:13:46,188
Be ready on serve receive right away.

1806
01:13:46,623 --> 01:13:47,456
It's 1 to 3.

1807
01:13:47,457 --> 01:13:48,190
(Everything starts with a good pass.)

1808
01:13:49,459 --> 01:13:50,526
One, two!

1809
01:13:51,361 --> 01:13:52,728
- Mine!
- Middle!

1810
01:13:52,729 --> 01:13:54,797
- Give her a good set.
- The set goes to Yeon Joo.

1811
01:13:54,798 --> 01:13:55,597
(The ball goes to Yeon Joo.)

1812
01:13:55,598 --> 01:13:56,398
Yeon Joo!

1813
01:13:56,599 --> 01:13:57,933
- Deep!
- Swing!

1814
01:13:58,035 --> 01:13:59,034
Push it out!

1815
01:13:59,703 --> 01:14:00,969
- She goes straight up.
- Nice play.

1816
01:14:00,970 --> 01:14:02,170
She tools the block for the point.

1817
01:14:02,372 --> 01:14:03,372
That's it.

1818
01:14:03,640 --> 01:14:05,641
- Okay.
- Great job.

1819
01:14:06,476 --> 01:14:07,710
Nice.

1820
01:14:07,711 --> 01:14:10,813
Yeon Joo has come a long way...

1821
01:14:10,814 --> 01:14:12,548
- since her first match.
- Without a doubt.

1822
01:14:12,549 --> 01:14:15,784
She's finding her contact point
and striking the ball cleanly.

1823
01:14:15,785 --> 01:14:17,820
Like we said earlier, at this rate,

1824
01:14:17,821 --> 01:14:20,022
- she's poised for a big comeback.
- Exactly.

1825
01:14:20,023 --> 01:14:21,457
Min Kyeong, stay calm.

1826
01:14:21,458 --> 01:14:22,458
Let's pick her up.

1827
01:14:22,459 --> 01:14:24,793
- I'll take my time on the serve.
- Sorry.

1828
01:14:25,128 --> 01:14:27,596
Min Kyeong, you're good. Take your time.

1829
01:14:27,602 --> 01:14:28,769
I'm sorry.

1830
01:14:32,769 --> 01:14:34,837
Their opposite hits cross-court a lot.

1831
01:14:34,838 --> 01:14:37,106
Get your hands up a little higher
on the block.

1832
01:14:37,908 --> 01:14:39,240
It's 3 to 4, down by just 1.

1833
01:14:39,241 --> 01:14:41,876
(First set, Lao Cai 4 : Wonder Dogs 3)

1834
01:14:43,012 --> 01:14:45,481
Serve to Zone One.

1835
01:14:45,482 --> 01:14:48,116
To the far side. A lot goes that way.

1836
01:14:48,117 --> 01:14:50,218
(Targeting Zone 1)

1837
01:14:51,988 --> 01:14:53,288
Yeon Joo steps up to serve.

1838
01:14:53,289 --> 01:14:54,289
(Yeon Joo serves.)

1839
01:14:55,758 --> 01:14:57,726
Good serve.

1840
01:14:57,894 --> 01:14:58,760
Nice serve.

1841
01:14:59,362 --> 01:15:01,730
(The serve drops into Zone 1.)

1842
01:15:04,167 --> 01:15:05,234
Ace!

1843
01:15:05,235 --> 01:15:06,835
(Service ace)

1844
01:15:06,836 --> 01:15:08,437
Nice.

1845
01:15:08,905 --> 01:15:10,739
(The Flame Deer delivers again.)

1846
01:15:10,740 --> 01:15:11,840
Oh, Yeon Joo!

1847
01:15:12,041 --> 01:15:13,545
And Yeon Joo goes wild
right from the start.

1848
01:15:13,763 --> 01:15:15,429
- The Flame Deer is charging ahead!
- Right.

1849
01:15:15,858 --> 01:15:19,290
This was what Coach Kim was going for.

1850
01:15:19,291 --> 01:15:22,157
Yeon Joo is doing a good job
meeting her expectations.

1851
01:15:22,158 --> 01:15:23,025
That's right.

1852
01:15:25,625 --> 01:15:26,891
They hit back...

1853
01:15:26,892 --> 01:15:28,092
when you target Zone Eight.

1854
01:15:28,558 --> 01:15:29,691
They're all gathered over here.

1855
01:15:30,391 --> 01:15:32,625
(The key strategy in the Lao Cai match)

1856
01:15:32,858 --> 01:15:35,090
Vietnamese players do
a lot of coordinated plays.

1857
01:15:35,091 --> 01:15:37,024
They move around here and there...

1858
01:15:37,025 --> 01:15:38,957
and do combination plays.

1859
01:15:38,958 --> 01:15:42,124
To block that...

1860
01:15:42,125 --> 01:15:44,324
serves are the key.

1861
01:15:44,325 --> 01:15:46,124
When you target Zone One,

1862
01:15:46,125 --> 01:15:49,024
the opponent's setter doesn't set
to the person who received the ball.

1863
01:15:49,025 --> 01:15:49,825
Got that?

1864
01:15:51,991 --> 01:15:55,291
(If you serve to the attacker...)

1865
01:15:58,258 --> 01:16:00,191
(the setter doesn't send the ball
in that direction.)

1866
01:16:02,191 --> 01:16:04,958
(All you have to do is
block the other side.)

1867
01:16:05,858 --> 01:16:08,758
(Operation: Shut Down Their Attacks)

1868
01:16:12,891 --> 01:16:13,958
Another serve.

1869
01:16:14,325 --> 01:16:16,025
Move along quickly!

1870
01:16:16,591 --> 01:16:17,791
Focus on C!

1871
01:16:18,291 --> 01:16:20,025
(The set goes opposite of the reception.)

1872
01:16:20,970 --> 01:16:22,170
A quick open from the left!

1873
01:16:22,191 --> 01:16:23,825
- It was blocked.
- There it is.

1874
01:16:25,658 --> 01:16:27,124
The opposite side is open.

1875
01:16:27,125 --> 01:16:28,025
It's up!

1876
01:16:30,491 --> 01:16:31,890
A push shot in for a point.

1877
01:16:31,891 --> 01:16:33,957
(Chae Rim's block scores.)

1878
01:16:33,958 --> 01:16:35,091
Nice.

1879
01:16:35,391 --> 01:16:36,158
That's it.

1880
01:16:37,258 --> 01:16:38,990
Scoring a point was nice,

1881
01:16:38,991 --> 01:16:40,925
but the block was even better.

1882
01:16:44,025 --> 01:16:46,957
Ultimately, it was Yeon Joo's serve
that opened the way.

1883
01:16:46,958 --> 01:16:47,791
Right.

1884
01:16:47,792 --> 01:16:49,824
That's why the serves are important.

1885
01:16:49,825 --> 01:16:53,325
(Making it easy to block the attacks)

1886
01:16:54,325 --> 01:16:57,490
Bo Been, just a bit more.

1887
01:16:57,491 --> 01:16:58,458
(Their strategy is successful.)

1888
01:16:59,225 --> 01:17:00,525
To the center.

1889
01:17:01,925 --> 01:17:03,358
They're stumbling over each other.
What a mess.

1890
01:17:04,425 --> 01:17:06,057
Boonlert, focus on setting.

1891
01:17:06,058 --> 01:17:09,091
Lam, if it's too close, let it go.

1892
01:17:09,092 --> 01:17:10,359
(Understood)

1893
01:17:11,825 --> 01:17:14,725
(Another serve from the Flame Deer)

1894
01:17:20,258 --> 01:17:21,258
Inside!

1895
01:17:21,259 --> 01:17:22,357
They're moving.

1896
01:17:22,358 --> 01:17:23,890
Coming down for a slide attack.

1897
01:17:23,891 --> 01:17:25,225
(Successful block)

1898
01:17:25,825 --> 01:17:26,791
A shaky reception.

1899
01:17:26,792 --> 01:17:28,325
(Min Kyeong's shaky defense)

1900
01:17:28,858 --> 01:17:31,291
To the right.

1901
01:17:33,112 --> 01:17:34,845
(Khanh Lam's dig)

1902
01:17:34,858 --> 01:17:36,058
Her dig saves the ball.

1903
01:17:37,184 --> 01:17:37,951
A tip.

1904
01:17:37,958 --> 01:17:39,291
An easy reception.

1905
01:17:39,625 --> 01:17:40,425
Send it to C!

1906
01:17:41,791 --> 01:17:43,324
Hyo Rim to the left.

1907
01:17:43,325 --> 01:17:44,158
Chae Rim!

1908
01:17:45,291 --> 01:17:46,991
Chae Rim scores off the block!

1909
01:17:47,691 --> 01:17:48,790
That was way too strong.

1910
01:17:48,791 --> 01:17:49,791
Sorry.

1911
01:17:50,891 --> 01:17:53,957
Despite two blockers right in her way,

1912
01:17:53,958 --> 01:17:57,825
Chae Rim looked deep
and made an accurate shot.

1913
01:17:59,058 --> 01:18:02,158
(The Flame Deer and Chae Rim...)

1914
01:18:02,825 --> 01:18:05,658
(help lead the first set.)

1915
01:18:07,458 --> 01:18:09,491
Don't be needlessly defensive.
Just hit it.

1916
01:18:13,391 --> 01:18:16,590
As the Wonder Dogs take early control,

1917
01:18:16,591 --> 01:18:17,458
they lead by two points.

1918
01:18:17,458 --> 01:18:18,291
The current score is 4 to 6.

1919
01:18:18,658 --> 01:18:19,625
To Zone 1.

1920
01:18:20,658 --> 01:18:22,691
Yeon Joo continues to serve.

1921
01:18:26,825 --> 01:18:27,591
That's it!

1922
01:18:28,791 --> 01:18:29,924
They're fighting for it.

1923
01:18:29,925 --> 01:18:31,325
(A very shaky reception)

1924
01:18:32,435 --> 01:18:33,524
They send the ball over.

1925
01:18:33,525 --> 01:18:35,490
- Mine!
- Take it easy.

1926
01:18:35,491 --> 01:18:36,557
(They pass it with ease.)

1927
01:18:36,558 --> 01:18:37,325
Smash it!

1928
01:18:37,325 --> 01:18:38,191
A tip!

1929
01:18:40,458 --> 01:18:41,458
(A dedicated defense)

1930
01:18:41,825 --> 01:18:43,725
We can still do this! Hit it!

1931
01:18:44,591 --> 01:18:46,124
The ball goes over.

1932
01:18:46,125 --> 01:18:47,757
(Another chance to attack)

1933
01:18:47,758 --> 01:18:50,191
To the left, and Chae Rim tips it.

1934
01:18:50,858 --> 01:18:51,658
That's it!

1935
01:18:54,525 --> 01:18:56,057
It's over again as a free ball.

1936
01:18:56,058 --> 01:18:57,557
Yeon Joo starting off calmly.

1937
01:18:57,558 --> 01:18:58,758
The ball passes to Hyo Rim.

1938
01:18:59,091 --> 01:18:59,991
Go deep.

1939
01:19:00,625 --> 01:19:01,525
Back Chae Rim!

1940
01:19:02,025 --> 01:19:03,358
The defense is quite solid.

1941
01:19:04,558 --> 01:19:06,325
Here's the counterattack.

1942
01:19:08,758 --> 01:19:10,658
And it falls on the Wonder Dogs' side.

1943
01:19:14,291 --> 01:19:15,857
(Lips pressed tight)

1944
01:19:15,858 --> 01:19:16,658
Oh, gosh!

1945
01:19:18,225 --> 01:19:20,791
Ho Bin, why did you jump just now?

1946
01:19:22,325 --> 01:19:24,058
This is so frustrating.

1947
01:19:25,151 --> 01:19:27,951
When Hong Hahn hits,

1948
01:19:27,958 --> 01:19:30,557
she hits it on her way down.

1949
01:19:30,558 --> 01:19:35,057
It's up to the Wonder Dogs blockers
to get the timing right.

1950
01:19:35,058 --> 01:19:36,825
It falls in on their side.

1951
01:19:37,358 --> 01:19:38,491
A point for Lao Cai.

1952
01:19:41,391 --> 01:19:42,825
(Staring)

1953
01:19:44,525 --> 01:19:45,558
Aim your serve at Number 17.

1954
01:19:46,225 --> 01:19:47,525
(Understood)

1955
01:19:48,091 --> 01:19:50,058
(Targeting Min Kyeong)

1956
01:19:50,059 --> 01:19:51,926
They also have short serves.

1957
01:19:52,191 --> 01:19:53,025
Got it!

1958
01:19:53,026 --> 01:19:54,624
Prepare for a short serve.

1959
01:19:54,625 --> 01:19:55,890
Kieu Oanh serves.

1960
01:19:55,891 --> 01:19:56,957
It's a short one!

1961
01:19:56,958 --> 01:19:57,725
It's short.

1962
01:19:59,025 --> 01:20:00,158
An ace.

1963
01:20:03,758 --> 01:20:05,391
Min Kyeong!

1964
01:20:06,025 --> 01:20:07,124
How could you miss that?

1965
01:20:07,125 --> 01:20:09,391
Why are you all over the place?

1966
01:20:12,091 --> 01:20:14,191
Actually, to be honest,

1967
01:20:16,325 --> 01:20:18,458
I couldn't be more nervous.

1968
01:20:19,691 --> 01:20:21,625
(Min Kyeong was extremely nervous)

1969
01:20:22,725 --> 01:20:26,258
I could see how furious the coach was,

1970
01:20:26,891 --> 01:20:28,225
so I couldn't even look at her.

1971
01:20:33,558 --> 01:20:34,491
Chae Rim serves.

1972
01:20:34,492 --> 01:20:36,591
(First set, Lao Cai 6 : Wonder Dogs 7)

1973
01:20:37,025 --> 01:20:38,291
(Thinking)

1974
01:20:38,491 --> 01:20:39,425
Huyen,

1975
01:20:39,426 --> 01:20:41,624
you have to attack to create chances.

1976
01:20:41,625 --> 01:20:43,658
(Directing a center attack)

1977
01:20:44,058 --> 01:20:45,658
(Again, the target is Zone 1.)

1978
01:20:48,591 --> 01:20:49,458
A good serve.

1979
01:20:49,725 --> 01:20:50,525
That's it!

1980
01:20:51,191 --> 01:20:52,624
On the left.

1981
01:20:52,625 --> 01:20:53,725
Jump up high and smash it down.

1982
01:20:55,725 --> 01:20:57,224
(Not left but center)

1983
01:20:57,225 --> 01:20:58,291
(Oops)

1984
01:20:59,991 --> 01:21:01,291
A quick attack to the middle!

1985
01:21:02,325 --> 01:21:03,158
That's it!

1986
01:21:05,591 --> 01:21:06,458
Nice.

1987
01:21:06,825 --> 01:21:09,524
Huyen jumps well in the middle,

1988
01:21:09,525 --> 01:21:11,058
and her attacks are becoming relentless.

1989
01:21:11,525 --> 01:21:12,857
They have to be wary of her attacks.

1990
01:21:12,858 --> 01:21:15,658
(First set, Lao Cai 7 : Wonder Dogs 8)

1991
01:21:16,158 --> 01:21:17,058
Ho Bin!

1992
01:21:18,325 --> 01:21:20,758
Watch Numbers 17 and 8.
They're working together.

1993
01:21:20,759 --> 01:21:21,859
Aim for Zone One.

1994
01:21:22,025 --> 01:21:23,458
(Targeting Zone 1)

1995
01:21:23,725 --> 01:21:24,858
Ho Bin serves.

1996
01:21:26,625 --> 01:21:27,957
The reception was shaky.

1997
01:21:27,958 --> 01:21:28,725
That's it!

1998
01:21:31,625 --> 01:21:33,291
They defend, and it goes to Yeon Joo!

1999
01:21:34,825 --> 01:21:35,725
Go!

2000
01:21:36,625 --> 01:21:38,290
Min Kyeong rushes in and spikes!

2001
01:21:38,291 --> 01:21:39,325
(Blocked)

2002
01:21:40,258 --> 01:21:41,258
Set it up!

2003
01:21:42,258 --> 01:21:43,891
(Nhung jumps)

2004
01:21:44,125 --> 01:21:46,425
It's a high ball! Watch the line!

2005
01:21:47,625 --> 01:21:48,491
She spikes.

2006
01:21:48,725 --> 01:21:50,324
(Blocks breached again)

2007
01:21:50,325 --> 01:21:51,291
A successful point.

2008
01:21:54,258 --> 01:21:56,790
When you watch closely, you can see...

2009
01:21:56,791 --> 01:21:59,124
that she hangs in the air
for a split second.

2010
01:21:59,125 --> 01:22:01,258
So the blockers have to wait a bit longer.

2011
01:22:01,758 --> 01:22:04,024
That was Nhung.

2012
01:22:04,025 --> 01:22:07,090
She is the team's hope for the future.

2013
01:22:07,091 --> 01:22:09,524
She's an all-rounder...

2014
01:22:09,525 --> 01:22:11,258
- who can both attack and defend.
- That's right.

2015
01:22:11,558 --> 01:22:13,091
(Smiling)

2016
01:22:13,491 --> 01:22:16,390
Ye Dam, you're jumping early,
so the ball hits you as you fall.

2017
01:22:16,391 --> 01:22:18,290
You're too fast, so the ball gets
you on your way down.

2018
01:22:18,291 --> 01:22:19,158
It's okay.

2019
01:22:19,658 --> 01:22:21,191
Delay your jumps before blocking.

2020
01:22:22,858 --> 01:22:23,891
The current score is 8 to 9.

2021
01:22:28,458 --> 01:22:29,458
A shaky reception.

2022
01:22:29,758 --> 01:22:30,791
A second contact.

2023
01:22:31,125 --> 01:22:31,991
Nhung goes up.

2024
01:22:32,225 --> 01:22:33,958
Mind the timing!

2025
01:22:34,158 --> 01:22:34,991
One...

2026
01:22:34,992 --> 01:22:36,358
(Jumping first...)

2027
01:22:38,958 --> 01:22:39,990
A touch out.

2028
01:22:39,991 --> 01:22:40,791
Hey!

2029
01:22:42,391 --> 01:22:43,991
That was too quick.

2030
01:22:45,158 --> 01:22:46,591
You have to jump with me.

2031
01:22:46,891 --> 01:22:47,691
Got it.

2032
01:22:47,925 --> 01:22:52,791
It looks like Nhung will be
the main attacker.

2033
01:22:53,291 --> 01:22:54,890
The Wonder Dogs will have
to figure out the rhythm.

2034
01:22:54,891 --> 01:22:56,958
When Nhung attacks,

2035
01:22:57,458 --> 01:22:59,590
you can see the blockers
aren't timing their blocks right.

2036
01:22:59,591 --> 01:23:01,990
- Are they moving too fast?
- Yes.

2037
01:23:01,991 --> 01:23:04,991
They also have to raise their arms
more properly during the jumps.

2038
01:23:05,725 --> 01:23:06,558
Hey!

2039
01:23:10,091 --> 01:23:11,691
I can't believe this.

2040
01:23:14,191 --> 01:23:15,357
What's the score?

2041
01:23:15,358 --> 01:23:16,525
The current score is 9 to 9.

2042
01:23:19,691 --> 01:23:22,525
(Lao Cai begins taking control again.)

2043
01:23:25,658 --> 01:23:26,425
Boonlert!

2044
01:23:26,891 --> 01:23:27,958
Send the ball to Number 17.

2045
01:23:30,325 --> 01:23:32,325
(Min Kyeong is the target again.)

2046
01:23:32,625 --> 01:23:34,058
Her serves are quick.

2047
01:23:34,658 --> 01:23:35,724
Prepare for a quick serve.

2048
01:23:35,725 --> 01:23:37,299
(They must lead the score again.)

2049
01:23:37,625 --> 01:23:38,825
Boonlert serves.

2050
01:23:43,425 --> 01:23:45,325
The ball lands inside.

2051
01:23:46,125 --> 01:23:48,324
(Lao Cai's ace)

2052
01:23:48,325 --> 01:23:49,158
An ace.

2053
01:23:49,591 --> 01:23:52,790
What's with the reception?
What did I say about the serves?

2054
01:23:52,791 --> 01:23:54,358
- Sorry.
- My bad.

2055
01:23:54,791 --> 01:23:55,725
Let's focus.

2056
01:23:56,825 --> 01:23:59,458
- They let them take the lead.
- Right.

2057
01:24:01,025 --> 01:24:03,190
The Wonder Dogs need to tighten up.

2058
01:24:03,191 --> 01:24:04,725
- This is the time to focus.
- Right.

2059
01:24:05,391 --> 01:24:07,791
Focus! Get it together!

2060
01:24:08,591 --> 01:24:10,258
(Glancing)

2061
01:24:11,391 --> 01:24:14,558
Boonlert, hit between Numbers 5 and 6!

2062
01:24:14,791 --> 01:24:16,258
(Nodding)

2063
01:24:19,058 --> 01:24:20,758
(The target is...)

2064
01:24:21,091 --> 01:24:22,958
(Min Kyeong again.)

2065
01:24:23,258 --> 01:24:24,625
One pass.

2066
01:24:24,925 --> 01:24:26,825
The serves are not that strong.
Many are shaky.

2067
01:24:27,258 --> 01:24:29,457
If you can't send it back,
send it to the center.

2068
01:24:29,458 --> 01:24:30,291
Got it.

2069
01:24:34,358 --> 01:24:36,258
(Boonlert serves.)

2070
01:24:37,558 --> 01:24:38,358
To the center!

2071
01:24:39,458 --> 01:24:40,591
(Will it go over?)

2072
01:24:40,858 --> 01:24:42,358
- Hey!
- Hey!

2073
01:24:44,925 --> 01:24:46,225
A direct shot!

2074
01:24:47,791 --> 01:24:51,491
(Lao Cai widens the gap.)

2075
01:24:53,458 --> 01:24:54,558
Sorry.

2076
01:24:55,225 --> 01:24:57,458
Min Kyeong isn't doing so well.

2077
01:24:57,891 --> 01:24:59,591
I don't know what's up with me today.

2078
01:25:00,658 --> 01:25:02,457
Min Kyeong, your turn to serve.

2079
01:25:02,458 --> 01:25:03,258
Oh...

2080
01:25:04,491 --> 01:25:05,957
The score is 11 to 10, a one-point lead.

2081
01:25:05,958 --> 01:25:07,225
(Pulling one back off a Lao Cai error)

2082
01:25:07,525 --> 01:25:08,791
Min Kyeong serves.

2083
01:25:10,391 --> 01:25:11,425
Target Zone One.

2084
01:25:13,248 --> 01:25:15,750
(The target is Zone 1.)

2085
01:25:15,751 --> 01:25:18,913
Be ready for the high balls.

2086
01:25:18,914 --> 01:25:20,588
Watch the timing
when they send a high ball.

2087
01:25:20,589 --> 01:25:22,623
- Okay.
- Watch how they set it up.

2088
01:25:23,725 --> 01:25:25,693
(Staring intently)

2089
01:25:27,596 --> 01:25:29,263
(The middle)

2090
01:25:29,764 --> 01:25:31,331
(Nodding)

2091
01:25:31,766 --> 01:25:33,066
I'll cover this side.

2092
01:25:33,201 --> 01:25:34,501
Move in slowly.

2093
01:25:34,502 --> 01:25:36,136
Take your time.

2094
01:25:40,842 --> 01:25:42,142
- Nice serve.
- That's it.

2095
01:25:43,211 --> 01:25:44,611
(With the right-side attack shut down,)

2096
01:25:44,612 --> 01:25:46,246
(they'll focus their attacks on the left.)

2097
01:25:46,855 --> 01:25:48,622
(Shifting toward the left)

2098
01:25:49,150 --> 01:25:50,217
The middle.

2099
01:25:51,853 --> 01:25:52,653
Block it.

2100
01:25:54,122 --> 01:25:55,656
Oh, no.

2101
01:25:56,124 --> 01:25:56,990
Slide.

2102
01:25:56,991 --> 01:25:57,858
(A surprise quick attack)

2103
01:25:59,127 --> 01:25:59,727
(Touch)

2104
01:26:00,195 --> 01:26:01,095
She kept it alive!

2105
01:26:03,064 --> 01:26:05,332
(They fail to defend.)

2106
01:26:05,333 --> 01:26:06,366
- Oh, no.
- Oh, no.

2107
01:26:06,568 --> 01:26:09,136
Oh, no!

2108
01:26:09,704 --> 01:26:12,272
(So close.)

2109
01:26:12,673 --> 01:26:15,642
That could have been an amazing play.

2110
01:26:16,111 --> 01:26:19,446
Their middle attack came
in incredibly fast just now.

2111
01:26:19,447 --> 01:26:20,848
(Lao Cai's surprise middle attack)

2112
01:26:20,949 --> 01:26:23,784
They let the opponents take the lead
and gave up consecutive points.

2113
01:26:23,785 --> 01:26:26,920
This is when it would be good
to put some pressure on them.

2114
01:26:27,422 --> 01:26:29,322
It's 10 to 12, two points apart.

2115
01:26:30,825 --> 01:26:33,427
Our blocking wasn't working well.

2116
01:26:33,428 --> 01:26:35,395
We've had the same issue the entire match.

2117
01:26:35,497 --> 01:26:36,464
One...

2118
01:26:36,831 --> 01:26:38,398
Take your time.

2119
01:26:38,967 --> 01:26:40,601
Watch the timing!

2120
01:26:40,602 --> 01:26:43,203
Watch the timing
when they send a high ball.

2121
01:26:43,204 --> 01:26:47,107
I kept shouting about timing,

2122
01:26:47,442 --> 01:26:51,345
but things didn't go the way I expected.

2123
01:26:51,813 --> 01:26:54,415
So, to stop their momentum...

2124
01:26:56,051 --> 01:26:57,985
Coach Kim calls a strategic timeout.

2125
01:26:59,087 --> 01:27:00,053
Get over here!

2126
01:27:01,223 --> 01:27:02,990
How many points are we giving away?

2127
01:27:02,991 --> 01:27:04,826
That's like 3 or 4 easy points already!

2128
01:27:04,827 --> 01:27:07,161
Don't give away ridiculous points
like that.

2129
01:27:07,162 --> 01:27:09,498
The timing of your blocks
on the left side is off.

2130
01:27:09,499 --> 01:27:11,999
You aren't in sync with each other.

2131
01:27:12,000 --> 01:27:14,335
- You need to get your timing together.
- Yes, Coach.

2132
01:27:14,336 --> 01:27:16,837
You're doing well
when the high balls come in.

2133
01:27:17,038 --> 01:27:20,273
Get your timing right
when the ball comes from the left.

2134
01:27:20,274 --> 01:27:22,642
And you need to handle the balls
that come in from there properly.

2135
01:27:22,643 --> 01:27:24,244
- Yes, Coach.
- Get your timing right.

2136
01:27:25,780 --> 01:27:27,447
- Got it.
- Chae Rim.

2137
01:27:27,682 --> 01:27:31,252
You need to be the one holding things
together on the court.

2138
01:27:31,253 --> 01:27:33,587
You can't get flustered or rush things.

2139
01:27:33,588 --> 01:27:34,321
- Okay?
- Got it.

2140
01:27:34,322 --> 01:27:35,722
You're rushing right now.

2141
01:27:37,125 --> 01:27:38,125
I got it.

2142
01:27:38,126 --> 01:27:39,860
- Let's go.
- Let's go.

2143
01:27:39,861 --> 01:27:41,428
- One, two, three, let's go!
- Let's go!

2144
01:27:41,429 --> 01:27:42,296
Let's go.

2145
01:27:44,466 --> 01:27:46,234
I'm not very tall.

2146
01:27:46,235 --> 01:27:49,703
So I'm at a disadvantage
when it comes to blocking height.

2147
01:27:50,205 --> 01:27:52,139
I've practiced a lot to make up for that.

2148
01:27:52,341 --> 01:27:54,575
I thought I should stay calm...

2149
01:27:54,576 --> 01:27:56,810
and follow Coach's instructions.

2150
01:27:58,379 --> 01:28:01,448
Get your timing right
when they send a high ball. Chae Rim!

2151
01:28:01,449 --> 01:28:03,183
Watch the high balls.

2152
01:28:03,184 --> 01:28:04,984
When one comes, get close,
and take your time with the jump.

2153
01:28:04,985 --> 01:28:05,985
- Okay.
- Okay.

2154
01:28:05,986 --> 01:28:08,254
Take your time with the high ball.

2155
01:28:09,958 --> 01:28:11,325
The server is Hong Nhung.

2156
01:28:16,231 --> 01:28:18,933
Push it toward Zone One.

2157
01:28:19,400 --> 01:28:21,701
(The target is...)

2158
01:28:21,702 --> 01:28:22,837
(They relentlessly target Min Kyeong.)

2159
01:28:22,838 --> 01:28:24,337
Let's keep it up.

2160
01:28:25,507 --> 01:28:27,074
Seon Ah, you take it.

2161
01:28:30,278 --> 01:28:31,178
Mine!

2162
01:28:32,647 --> 01:28:33,547
Seon Ah receives the ball.

2163
01:28:33,548 --> 01:28:35,015
Hyo Rim sends it to the left.

2164
01:28:35,584 --> 01:28:36,683
Chae Rim goes for a spike.

2165
01:28:37,118 --> 01:28:38,126
They dig it.

2166
01:28:38,127 --> 01:28:39,286
It's sent to the right.

2167
01:28:39,287 --> 01:28:40,187
It's a high ball!

2168
01:28:41,744 --> 01:28:43,790
Wait.

2169
01:28:43,791 --> 01:28:44,591
(Hesitating)

2170
01:28:45,994 --> 01:28:46,894
Now!

2171
01:28:51,332 --> 01:28:53,633
It's blocked by Chae Rim!

2172
01:28:53,802 --> 01:28:55,102
That's right.

2173
01:28:55,103 --> 01:28:56,871
Nice!

2174
01:28:57,272 --> 01:29:00,441
(Nice block, Chae Rim.)

2175
01:29:00,708 --> 01:29:03,209
Nice, Chae Rim.

2176
01:29:03,446 --> 01:29:06,413
Chae Rim isn't particularly tall.

2177
01:29:06,848 --> 01:29:11,084
But her hand position
on the block was excellent.

2178
01:29:12,020 --> 01:29:13,020
Nice job.

2179
01:29:13,021 --> 01:29:16,204
(Finally, the blocking timing is in sync.)

2180
01:29:16,891 --> 01:29:19,426
(Ye Dam serves.)

2181
01:29:19,661 --> 01:29:21,362
Aim for Zone Four.

2182
01:29:21,363 --> 01:29:22,196
Serve.

2183
01:29:25,033 --> 01:29:25,933
Nice serve.

2184
01:29:28,002 --> 01:29:29,369
They get it up.

2185
01:29:29,370 --> 01:29:30,737
(A shaky high-ball setup)

2186
01:29:30,738 --> 01:29:31,905
Watch the timing!

2187
01:29:32,240 --> 01:29:35,075
(Prep, then jump!)

2188
01:29:35,544 --> 01:29:38,112
Nice block from Ho Bin!

2189
01:29:38,113 --> 01:29:40,114
(Two consecutive blocks for points!)

2190
01:29:40,115 --> 01:29:41,215
That's right.

2191
01:29:41,784 --> 01:29:43,651
I want to scream.

2192
01:29:45,653 --> 01:29:46,874
You can't have volleyball without Ho Bin.

2193
01:29:46,955 --> 01:29:48,021
And for commentating, it's Ho Geun.

2194
01:29:48,389 --> 01:29:49,990
Ho Bin has been showing off...

2195
01:29:49,991 --> 01:29:51,859
some incredible blocks
from the very beginning.

2196
01:29:52,227 --> 01:29:54,562
A monster block!

2197
01:29:54,930 --> 01:29:56,196
That's what I'm talking about.

2198
01:29:56,197 --> 01:29:58,799
When you send a nice serve,
capitalize on the high ball.

2199
01:29:59,534 --> 01:30:02,903
(Finally, everything comes together.)

2200
01:30:03,205 --> 01:30:04,471
They're tied at 12.

2201
01:30:05,073 --> 01:30:06,374
Get the reception right, and...

2202
01:30:06,375 --> 01:30:09,377
(Let's take the lead now!)

2203
01:30:09,510 --> 01:30:11,811
We're attacking Zone Four,
so block the ball going that way.

2204
01:30:11,812 --> 01:30:12,612
Okay.

2205
01:30:13,115 --> 01:30:14,114
Serve.

2206
01:30:14,716 --> 01:30:15,849
Let's go.

2207
01:30:16,150 --> 01:30:17,984
- Short serve.
- That's it.

2208
01:30:19,554 --> 01:30:20,521
Quick attack.

2209
01:30:21,189 --> 01:30:22,456
Get it up.

2210
01:30:22,457 --> 01:30:24,424
They dig it. Ho Bin keeps the rally going.

2211
01:30:25,994 --> 01:30:28,162
(There's no opening.)

2212
01:30:28,456 --> 01:30:29,322
Damn it.

2213
01:30:31,065 --> 01:30:32,032
Yeon Joo.

2214
01:30:33,835 --> 01:30:34,802
Great job.

2215
01:30:34,827 --> 01:30:37,738
(A perfectly placed tip wins the point.)

2216
01:30:42,644 --> 01:30:43,945
- Nice!
- Nice!

2217
01:30:43,946 --> 01:30:45,646
They've taken the lead!

2218
01:30:46,180 --> 01:30:48,014
Well done.

2219
01:30:49,017 --> 01:30:51,987
Yeon Joo spotted an opening
in that split second.

2220
01:30:51,988 --> 01:30:54,888
Exactly. It was as if time had stopped,

2221
01:30:54,889 --> 01:30:55,989
and she tipped it so perfectly.

2222
01:30:55,990 --> 01:30:57,258
(Attacking through the tiniest opening)

2223
01:30:57,259 --> 01:30:59,226
- There was nobody there.
- Exactly.

2224
01:31:00,194 --> 01:31:02,262
(A sudden pang of regret)

2225
01:31:03,531 --> 01:31:04,965
Nice job.

2226
01:31:04,966 --> 01:31:07,767
(The open-space hunter is
always watchful.)

2227
01:31:07,969 --> 01:31:09,703
Yeon Joo is amazing.

2228
01:31:10,171 --> 01:31:11,504
Does she really see everything?

2229
01:31:11,806 --> 01:31:12,906
She's so experienced.

2230
01:31:13,474 --> 01:31:16,276
The Wonder Dogs have
taken the lead again, 14 to 13.

2231
01:31:16,277 --> 01:31:17,377
(First set, Lao Cai 13 : Wonder Dogs 14)

2232
01:31:19,547 --> 01:31:22,783
I've told you over and over
to bring your arms forward!

2233
01:31:25,787 --> 01:31:27,221
Why don't you ever listen?

2234
01:31:27,222 --> 01:31:29,990
Coach Nguyen seems
a little flustered now too.

2235
01:31:31,793 --> 01:31:33,594
Boonlert, come here.

2236
01:31:34,028 --> 01:31:36,062
Since they are crowding the sides,

2237
01:31:36,063 --> 01:31:38,698
if you get a good ball,
go through the middle.

2238
01:31:40,368 --> 01:31:45,372
(Attacking through the middle
to avoid the blockers)

2239
01:31:47,308 --> 01:31:49,042
Yeon Joo gets ready to serve.

2240
01:31:50,945 --> 01:31:53,479
Aim for Zone One. Watch the opposite side.

2241
01:31:55,517 --> 01:31:56,717
Good serve.

2242
01:31:57,285 --> 01:31:59,353
(As expected,
it's an attack from the left.)

2243
01:31:59,887 --> 01:32:01,121
Nice block.

2244
01:32:01,122 --> 01:32:02,589
Nice dig by Chae Rim.

2245
01:32:02,590 --> 01:32:04,023
Saved the direct hit!

2246
01:32:04,425 --> 01:32:06,126
(But now the opponent has a free ball.)

2247
01:32:07,395 --> 01:32:09,329
(The front-row attackers prepare
to attack.)

2248
01:32:09,430 --> 01:32:10,597
(Chaos)

2249
01:32:10,932 --> 01:32:11,698
The middle.

2250
01:32:12,700 --> 01:32:15,635
Kieu Oanh sends it down the middle.

2251
01:32:16,104 --> 01:32:18,539
(The strategy worked perfectly.)

2252
01:32:18,906 --> 01:32:21,608
The Wonder Dogs eventually let
the opponents tie the score.

2253
01:32:21,609 --> 01:32:24,444
(They let them catch up.)

2254
01:32:25,813 --> 01:32:26,713
Chae Rim.

2255
01:32:26,714 --> 01:32:27,781
Make it a touch-out.

2256
01:32:28,850 --> 01:32:30,017
I got it.

2257
01:32:31,352 --> 01:32:33,954
Keep using the middle.

2258
01:32:34,489 --> 01:32:36,857
Aim your serve short at Zone Four.

2259
01:32:38,159 --> 01:32:39,559
She might serve short.

2260
01:32:40,328 --> 01:32:41,261
You watch for the short serve.

2261
01:32:43,631 --> 01:32:44,864
Mine.

2262
01:32:45,133 --> 01:32:45,866
That's it.

2263
01:32:45,867 --> 01:32:46,700
Damn.

2264
01:32:46,701 --> 01:32:47,901
Oh, my goodness.

2265
01:32:47,902 --> 01:32:49,315
- They barely keep it alive.
- Hit it.

2266
01:32:49,510 --> 01:32:51,439
A roll shot.
The opponents have a free ball.

2267
01:32:51,839 --> 01:32:52,972
Move in.

2268
01:32:53,609 --> 01:32:55,642
The middle. Yeon Joo digs it.

2269
01:32:55,643 --> 01:32:56,543
Cover!

2270
01:32:56,811 --> 01:32:57,778
Chae Rim.

2271
01:32:58,312 --> 01:32:59,512
It's covered!

2272
01:33:00,014 --> 01:33:01,916
- It's yours.
- Yeon Joo attacks from the back row.

2273
01:33:02,350 --> 01:33:03,817
(Min Kyeong covers it again.)

2274
01:33:04,052 --> 01:33:04,985
They change directions.

2275
01:33:04,986 --> 01:33:05,919
Hit it.

2276
01:33:05,920 --> 01:33:06,787
Hit it.

2277
01:33:08,156 --> 01:33:10,524
Back to Chae Rim on the left.

2278
01:33:12,794 --> 01:33:14,394
It's called out!

2279
01:33:14,409 --> 01:33:15,229
(Out of bounds)

2280
01:33:16,198 --> 01:33:17,197
No, it's not.

2281
01:33:17,198 --> 01:33:19,566
- It definitely touched!
- She touched it.

2282
01:33:20,635 --> 01:33:21,835
No, it didn't touch.

2283
01:33:22,603 --> 01:33:25,438
(They're claiming
a touch off the blocker.)

2284
01:33:26,974 --> 01:33:28,541
She requests a VAR review.

2285
01:33:31,145 --> 01:33:32,445
(Ringing)

2286
01:33:33,047 --> 01:33:33,947
That sounds like a phone ringing.

2287
01:33:36,817 --> 01:33:39,353
Actually, Chae Rim finished
that play nicely.

2288
01:33:40,955 --> 01:33:42,388
It looks like her fingers moved.

2289
01:33:42,389 --> 01:33:43,256
(Shaking)

2290
01:33:44,792 --> 01:33:47,460
The call is overturned.
It was a touch-out off the blocker.

2291
01:33:47,461 --> 01:33:50,097
Chae Rim did a great job spotting
the fingertip touch.

2292
01:33:50,098 --> 01:33:52,866
Min Kyeong also did
a great job covering the ball.

2293
01:33:53,668 --> 01:33:56,937
The Wonder Dogs take
the lead again, 15 to 14.

2294
01:33:57,472 --> 01:33:59,506
Just hit it.

2295
01:33:59,507 --> 01:34:00,641
Aim for the corner.

2296
01:34:05,413 --> 01:34:06,780
Good reception.

2297
01:34:06,948 --> 01:34:08,248
Go for it.

2298
01:34:08,683 --> 01:34:09,516
Okay.

2299
01:34:11,285 --> 01:34:12,886
(As expected, they attack from the left.)

2300
01:34:13,489 --> 01:34:15,088
She charges in with a diagonal attack.

2301
01:34:15,756 --> 01:34:16,589
It's a touch-out.

2302
01:34:18,326 --> 01:34:21,495
Since the Vietnamese players
generally have great jumping ability,

2303
01:34:22,063 --> 01:34:24,631
it's a little difficult
to read their attack angles.

2304
01:34:24,632 --> 01:34:26,566
Right. They're tied again.

2305
01:34:26,567 --> 01:34:28,935
(A fierce battle for every single point)

2306
01:34:32,106 --> 01:34:34,675
(Min Kyeong moves to the front row.)

2307
01:34:35,309 --> 01:34:36,309
Min Kyeong.

2308
01:34:36,370 --> 01:34:37,970
Use the angle where you can hit it best.

2309
01:34:37,978 --> 01:34:40,446
Check whether it's a single block
or a double block before you attack.

2310
01:34:40,447 --> 01:34:41,381
I got it.

2311
01:34:41,382 --> 01:34:43,349
(We'll win with our angles too.)

2312
01:34:44,019 --> 01:34:45,218
They're tied at 15.

2313
01:34:47,221 --> 01:34:48,155
They barely get it.

2314
01:34:48,156 --> 01:34:49,455
- Set to C.
- Hit it.

2315
01:34:49,991 --> 01:34:50,857
Hit it.

2316
01:34:52,326 --> 01:34:54,193
Min Kyeong with a powerful spike!

2317
01:34:56,063 --> 01:34:59,766
It looks like Min Kyeong is
finally loosening up.

2318
01:35:00,901 --> 01:35:02,502
Seriously! That defense...

2319
01:35:04,872 --> 01:35:05,839
We're at 16 points.

2320
01:35:06,988 --> 01:35:08,822
The Wonder Dogs move one step ahead...

2321
01:35:08,843 --> 01:35:11,579
and head into the second technical timeout
of the first set.

2322
01:35:12,553 --> 01:35:14,101
It's the same as before.

2323
01:35:14,141 --> 01:35:17,074
When you pass, the ball comes
to the shakier side.

2324
01:35:17,075 --> 01:35:19,574
When it comes to the shakier side,
set it up around here.

2325
01:35:19,575 --> 01:35:21,141
Slightly over here.

2326
01:35:21,142 --> 01:35:22,809
- You understand?
- Yes, I'll signal that.

2327
01:35:23,475 --> 01:35:25,108
Why aren't you connecting well,
and why are you rushing?

2328
01:35:25,109 --> 01:35:27,657
Stay calm! There's no need to rush.

2329
01:35:28,142 --> 01:35:29,774
It's hot enough as it is,
so why are you in such a hurry?

2330
01:35:29,775 --> 01:35:30,909
Take your time!

2331
01:35:32,109 --> 01:35:32,975
Have some water.

2332
01:35:34,009 --> 01:35:36,942
(I don't need any water.)

2333
01:35:38,142 --> 01:35:41,675
(Completely focused on discussing tactics)

2334
01:35:42,642 --> 01:35:43,742
And...

2335
01:35:45,109 --> 01:35:47,574
Sub in Linh. Take her out now.

2336
01:35:47,575 --> 01:35:50,342
(Tu Linh, the captain, is brought in.)

2337
01:35:52,309 --> 01:35:53,809
(Glancing)

2338
01:35:55,775 --> 01:35:59,074
Coach Nguyen has subbed
Hoang Hong Hanh out...

2339
01:35:59,075 --> 01:36:00,574
and brought Tu Linh in.

2340
01:36:00,575 --> 01:36:02,925
It looks like Coach Nguyen wants
to shore up their defense,

2341
01:36:02,936 --> 01:36:04,538
especially their serves
and serve reception.

2342
01:36:04,575 --> 01:36:05,409
That's right.

2343
01:36:06,208 --> 01:36:08,008
Number 7 is slowing down a bit too.

2344
01:36:08,009 --> 01:36:09,975
- Take your time.
- You can relax a bit.

2345
01:36:14,342 --> 01:36:15,675
Tu Linh with a good pass!

2346
01:36:16,875 --> 01:36:17,842
A spike.

2347
01:36:18,575 --> 01:36:19,409
It worked.

2348
01:36:19,842 --> 01:36:23,008
(Quickly turning defense
into an offensive point)

2349
01:36:23,009 --> 01:36:24,375
There we go. No, that's not it.

2350
01:36:26,975 --> 01:36:28,108
She's definitely reliable.

2351
01:36:28,109 --> 01:36:30,541
Her serve reception has been solid,

2352
01:36:30,542 --> 01:36:32,508
which has allowed them
to run their offense smoothly.

2353
01:36:32,509 --> 01:36:34,041
Keep that up.

2354
01:36:34,042 --> 01:36:35,591
Stay active
and keep moving just like that.

2355
01:36:36,009 --> 01:36:38,041
(After the Wonder Dogs got one point back)

2356
01:36:38,042 --> 01:36:41,209
(First Set, Lao Cai 16 : Wonder Dogs 17)

2357
01:36:41,842 --> 01:36:42,875
Hyo Rim is serving.

2358
01:36:45,142 --> 01:36:46,075
She sends it in hard.

2359
01:36:47,735 --> 01:36:48,968
She goes for the spike off the high ball.

2360
01:36:48,975 --> 01:36:50,741
Chae Rim digs it from the back.

2361
01:36:50,742 --> 01:36:51,941
The Wonder Dogs are on the counterattack.

2362
01:36:51,942 --> 01:36:52,875
There it is!

2363
01:36:52,876 --> 01:36:53,909
Min Kyeong, go!

2364
01:36:54,275 --> 01:36:55,142
Stay put!

2365
01:36:55,143 --> 01:36:56,308
(They need a powerful attack here.)

2366
01:36:56,309 --> 01:36:57,242
Hit it!

2367
01:36:57,609 --> 01:36:59,041
(Homerun?)

2368
01:36:59,042 --> 01:37:00,175
Hey!

2369
01:37:01,509 --> 01:37:02,775
(Giving the opponents
an easy chance to attack)

2370
01:37:03,609 --> 01:37:04,409
(Sighing)

2371
01:37:05,275 --> 01:37:06,267
Back-row attack through the middle!

2372
01:37:06,488 --> 01:37:07,921
Send it up. To the middle!

2373
01:37:07,975 --> 01:37:08,809
Send it to C!

2374
01:37:09,875 --> 01:37:10,609
Hit it!

2375
01:37:10,610 --> 01:37:11,875
Min Kyeong again!

2376
01:37:11,881 --> 01:37:12,981
Smash it!

2377
01:37:15,675 --> 01:37:16,709
And she scores!

2378
01:37:17,942 --> 01:37:21,409
She seemed
to be overthinking the feint at first,

2379
01:37:21,809 --> 01:37:24,042
but she finished with a bold swing.

2380
01:37:25,275 --> 01:37:28,608
Min Kyeong, what was that tip?

2381
01:37:28,609 --> 01:37:30,274
When you have a chance to swing,
you need to swing!

2382
01:37:30,275 --> 01:37:32,009
Look at the score.
Now's the time to attack!

2383
01:37:34,342 --> 01:37:36,709
You keep playing well, then losing focus.

2384
01:37:37,975 --> 01:37:43,209
I like Min Kyeong's determination
and passion.

2385
01:37:43,909 --> 01:37:45,875
But she's inconsistent.

2386
01:37:46,242 --> 01:37:48,209
Sometimes she's really good,

2387
01:37:48,675 --> 01:37:50,208
then her performance suddenly drops.

2388
01:37:50,209 --> 01:37:51,975
(Min Kyeong losing momentum)

2389
01:37:53,501 --> 01:37:54,701
Then, she suddenly picks it back up,

2390
01:37:56,209 --> 01:37:57,042
only to drop off again.

2391
01:37:59,368 --> 01:38:00,602
(Ji Min Kyeong)

2392
01:38:00,609 --> 01:38:03,874
These ups and downs happen too often,

2393
01:38:03,875 --> 01:38:06,909
and that's a bit disappointing.

2394
01:38:07,675 --> 01:38:11,642
I think we should sub Min Kyeong out
when she rotates to the back row.

2395
01:38:13,575 --> 01:38:14,975
The score is 19 to 16.

2396
01:38:16,709 --> 01:38:18,709
(Right now!)

2397
01:38:20,295 --> 01:38:22,828
Coach Nguyen makes a double substitution.

2398
01:38:22,842 --> 01:38:24,109
(Boonlert out, Thu Thuy in)

2399
01:38:24,309 --> 01:38:26,542
(Kieu Oanh out, Hoa Tham in)

2400
01:38:27,609 --> 01:38:29,342
(Smirking)

2401
01:38:29,842 --> 01:38:33,242
He's now got three front-row attackers.

2402
01:38:34,709 --> 01:38:38,209
This is a double-substitution strategy
Coach Kim often uses.

2403
01:38:38,334 --> 01:38:40,508
(Her subbing strategy that worked
so well against Pohang)

2404
01:38:41,281 --> 01:38:43,297
(The double substitution strategy)

2405
01:38:43,709 --> 01:38:47,542
(A tactic that creates
varied attack options...)

2406
01:38:47,775 --> 01:38:51,342
(with three front-row hitters)

2407
01:38:51,842 --> 01:38:53,942
(A mirror-image double substitution)

2408
01:38:55,281 --> 01:38:56,348
I thought it was getting interesting.

2409
01:38:57,448 --> 01:38:59,348
Setter Hoa Tham comes in.

2410
01:38:59,809 --> 01:39:02,874
Coach Nguyen scouted her himself...

2411
01:39:02,875 --> 01:39:05,641
when she was twelve.

2412
01:39:05,642 --> 01:39:06,575
Right.

2413
01:39:06,576 --> 01:39:08,542
She's definitely one to watch.

2414
01:39:09,002 --> 01:39:09,968
Focus on serve reception!

2415
01:39:11,509 --> 01:39:12,909
They have three attackers.

2416
01:39:13,409 --> 01:39:14,509
Three attackers!

2417
01:39:15,909 --> 01:39:16,809
Hyo Rim is serving.

2418
01:39:20,575 --> 01:39:22,175
Go!

2419
01:39:22,575 --> 01:39:23,642
(Right)

2420
01:39:23,942 --> 01:39:25,109
(Left)

2421
01:39:25,115 --> 01:39:26,181
(Center)

2422
01:39:26,575 --> 01:39:27,975
(Scrambling)

2423
01:39:30,942 --> 01:39:32,508
The spike!

2424
01:39:32,509 --> 01:39:33,809
(Blasting it through the block)

2425
01:39:34,975 --> 01:39:37,908
Lao Cai can close the gap in no time
if the Wonder Dogs lose focus.

2426
01:39:37,909 --> 01:39:39,075
They need to stay focused.

2427
01:39:40,675 --> 01:39:42,842
(First Set, Lao Cai 17 : Wonder Dogs 21)

2428
01:39:43,642 --> 01:39:46,009
(Min Kyeong rotated to the back row.)

2429
01:39:46,409 --> 01:39:47,149
Let's sub.

2430
01:39:51,909 --> 01:39:54,209
Coach Kim subs Ye Eun in.

2431
01:39:56,109 --> 01:39:58,074
Why did you tip it like that?

2432
01:39:58,075 --> 01:39:59,474
You should've hit it with that timing.

2433
01:39:59,475 --> 01:40:00,609
That was a good ball too.

2434
01:40:01,942 --> 01:40:04,208
Why are you so nervous? It's embarrassing.

2435
01:40:04,209 --> 01:40:05,342
Just sit on the bench the whole time.

2436
01:40:05,942 --> 01:40:06,775
I really can't understand it.

2437
01:40:10,209 --> 01:40:12,209
I was really mad at myself.

2438
01:40:13,342 --> 01:40:17,209
I wanted to do well so badly...

2439
01:40:17,509 --> 01:40:21,309
that I ended up tensing up.

2440
01:40:23,609 --> 01:40:24,609
Ye Eun is serving.

2441
01:40:25,242 --> 01:40:26,854
When the pass comes up,
run the combo play with Hong Nhung.

2442
01:40:27,642 --> 01:40:28,575
Pass it to me.

2443
01:40:29,875 --> 01:40:30,775
Ye Eun serves.

2444
01:40:31,775 --> 01:40:32,675
They passed it well.

2445
01:40:32,675 --> 01:40:33,475
Good.

2446
01:40:34,609 --> 01:40:35,442
She sets it to the left.

2447
01:40:38,442 --> 01:40:39,309
(Touched)

2448
01:40:39,310 --> 01:40:41,041
And the quick open attack is good.

2449
01:40:41,042 --> 01:40:42,842
(Hong Nhung again!)

2450
01:40:43,542 --> 01:40:48,242
(Lao Cai is chasing.)

2451
01:40:50,042 --> 01:40:51,309
(Ringing)

2452
01:40:53,775 --> 01:40:56,009
The Wonder Dogs called a timeout.

2453
01:40:57,042 --> 01:40:58,641
It's the same thing I told you earlier.

2454
01:40:58,642 --> 01:41:01,408
They're giving you high balls,
but you're not scoring any points.

2455
01:41:01,409 --> 01:41:02,674
Because your block timing is too early,

2456
01:41:02,675 --> 01:41:04,760
the ball comes over
right as you're coming down,

2457
01:41:04,784 --> 01:41:07,351
so it keeps deflecting off your hands
and going out.

2458
01:41:07,375 --> 01:41:09,909
Wait a little longer before you jump.
Got it?

2459
01:41:10,742 --> 01:41:14,742
We can win this match
if we just cut down on our errors.

2460
01:41:15,075 --> 01:41:20,208
Let's fight to keep
every playable ball alive.

2461
01:41:20,209 --> 01:41:21,309
Come on, focus!

2462
01:41:23,875 --> 01:41:25,275
- In 1, 2, 3.
- Let's go!

2463
01:41:26,209 --> 01:41:27,442
Let's get one right away.

2464
01:41:33,142 --> 01:41:35,475
Target Zone Five with your serves.

2465
01:41:38,642 --> 01:41:40,409
(Targeted serves to Chae Rim)

2466
01:41:41,242 --> 01:41:42,175
Hong Nhung serves.

2467
01:41:44,509 --> 01:41:45,342
Good.

2468
01:41:45,342 --> 01:41:46,309
Defense, take your time!

2469
01:41:46,309 --> 01:41:47,209
(Getting ready)

2470
01:41:48,142 --> 01:41:49,675
Back set! And Yeon Joo crushes it!

2471
01:41:50,075 --> 01:41:51,209
(Not a chance!)

2472
01:41:51,442 --> 01:41:52,242
Keep going!

2473
01:41:53,609 --> 01:41:54,442
(The ball goes to the left.)

2474
01:41:55,875 --> 01:41:56,742
Ye Dam!

2475
01:41:58,242 --> 01:41:59,742
(Waiting before jumping)

2476
01:42:00,942 --> 01:42:04,008
She spikes, and Ye Dam blocks it!

2477
01:42:04,009 --> 01:42:05,009
That's it!

2478
01:42:06,009 --> 01:42:07,409
Unbelievable! That was great!

2479
01:42:07,775 --> 01:42:11,041
Tu Linh went for a decisive swing,

2480
01:42:11,042 --> 01:42:14,141
and Ye Dam was right there
to shut it right down.

2481
01:42:14,142 --> 01:42:17,608
Ye Dam has started
building a wall here in Vietnam too.

2482
01:42:17,609 --> 01:42:20,308
She put up four of them in the last match.

2483
01:42:20,309 --> 01:42:22,209
She's practically a bricklayer
at this point.

2484
01:42:22,842 --> 01:42:23,675
Hey!

2485
01:42:24,042 --> 01:42:26,309
Because you're not using the middle,
you're facing a double block on the pins.

2486
01:42:27,609 --> 01:42:30,709
(Now is the chance.)

2487
01:42:31,775 --> 01:42:32,709
Nice block!

2488
01:42:32,709 --> 01:42:33,675
(Low five)

2489
01:42:33,942 --> 01:42:36,709
Ye Dam comes out, and Yun Ha comes in.

2490
01:42:37,575 --> 01:42:38,342
Zone Four.

2491
01:42:40,275 --> 01:42:43,409
(Shutting down
the left-side attack this time)

2492
01:42:45,342 --> 01:42:47,409
- I'll serve.
- Yun Ha is serving.

2493
01:42:50,175 --> 01:42:51,641
- The reception is shaky.
- Good.

2494
01:42:51,642 --> 01:42:52,409
Get in there.

2495
01:42:53,742 --> 01:42:55,775
(To the right, as expected)

2496
01:42:56,075 --> 01:42:56,942
(Chae Rim steps up.)

2497
01:42:56,943 --> 01:42:58,042
Watch your timing!

2498
01:42:58,342 --> 01:42:59,309
(Waiting)

2499
01:43:00,775 --> 01:43:01,775
Spike!

2500
01:43:02,609 --> 01:43:04,575
It's blocked!

2501
01:43:04,875 --> 01:43:06,409
(Exclaiming)

2502
01:43:06,542 --> 01:43:07,942
Nice job!

2503
01:43:09,175 --> 01:43:10,242
Nice play!

2504
01:43:10,675 --> 01:43:13,075
(Thumbs up!)

2505
01:43:13,309 --> 01:43:16,874
The Wonder Dogs' serves are
landing really well.

2506
01:43:16,875 --> 01:43:18,174
The hitter tracked the ball all the way...

2507
01:43:18,175 --> 01:43:21,008
and even twisted her wrist to angle it in,

2508
01:43:21,009 --> 01:43:23,409
but Chae Rim shut that down cleanly.

2509
01:43:24,575 --> 01:43:27,142
The Wonder Dogs are
completely on a roll here.

2510
01:43:28,109 --> 01:43:29,875
Yun Ha continues to serve.

2511
01:43:33,342 --> 01:43:34,175
Finish it!

2512
01:43:34,409 --> 01:43:35,409
Back-row attack from the middle!

2513
01:43:35,842 --> 01:43:36,675
They dug it!

2514
01:43:37,775 --> 01:43:38,609
Good!

2515
01:43:38,975 --> 01:43:40,341
They need to stay calm
and take it one touch at a time.

2516
01:43:40,342 --> 01:43:42,109
- Yun Ha sets it over.
- Send it over!

2517
01:43:44,309 --> 01:43:45,609
The ball goes over!

2518
01:43:48,497 --> 01:43:49,075
(Jumping)

2519
01:43:49,709 --> 01:43:51,209
And she pushes it in!

2520
01:43:52,075 --> 01:43:53,708
(Chae Rim, the invincible wall)

2521
01:43:53,709 --> 01:43:54,509
Good.

2522
01:43:55,542 --> 01:44:00,042
(Cheers erupt.)

2523
01:44:02,909 --> 01:44:03,742
Hong Nhung!

2524
01:44:04,742 --> 01:44:06,909
What on earth is wrong with you?

2525
01:44:08,642 --> 01:44:11,675
(Even the usually calm coach is
losing his cool.)

2526
01:44:12,609 --> 01:44:14,775
Chae Rim has been phenomenal
in the first set.

2527
01:44:15,942 --> 01:44:18,275
It's set point for the Wonder Dogs.

2528
01:44:18,675 --> 01:44:21,042
(First Set, Lao Cai 19 : Wonder Dogs 24)

2529
01:44:21,342 --> 01:44:23,008
Let's end it right here.

2530
01:44:23,009 --> 01:44:25,894
They can take the first set
if they just grab one more point.

2531
01:44:27,209 --> 01:44:28,009
Hyo Rim!

2532
01:44:29,009 --> 01:44:29,975
I'll go with this.

2533
01:44:30,509 --> 01:44:31,309
I'll run a B-back C.

2534
01:44:31,310 --> 01:44:33,975
(Decoy for the blockers.)

2535
01:44:35,042 --> 01:44:36,142
Luan Thi Loan serves.

2536
01:44:37,709 --> 01:44:38,942
Ye Eun passes it cleanly.

2537
01:44:39,942 --> 01:44:41,109
(Throwing the bait)

2538
01:44:41,442 --> 01:44:43,008
(Scrambling around)

2539
01:44:43,009 --> 01:44:44,309
You do it!

2540
01:44:45,009 --> 01:44:46,209
(The real option is Yeon Joo.)

2541
01:44:47,342 --> 01:44:51,009
There's the spike!

2542
01:44:56,775 --> 01:44:59,209
(The oldest player closes it out.)

2543
01:45:00,242 --> 01:45:03,142
The Wonder Dogs take the first set.

2544
01:45:03,609 --> 01:45:05,708
(First Set, Lao Cai 19 : Wonder Dogs 25)

2545
01:45:05,709 --> 01:45:06,667
Nice job!

2546
01:45:06,668 --> 01:45:07,636
(Against a pro team)

2547
01:45:08,642 --> 01:45:11,075
(Taking the first set)

2548
01:45:11,909 --> 01:45:13,974
(Set Two timeout)

2549
01:45:15,677 --> 01:45:17,978
I'm sweating all of a sudden.
I was fine a minute ago.

2550
01:45:19,380 --> 01:45:20,780
It's insanely hot.

2551
01:45:21,917 --> 01:45:23,551
Our serves are giving them trouble,

2552
01:45:23,552 --> 01:45:25,586
- so they can't run their offense.
- They keep setting high balls, right?

2553
01:45:26,554 --> 01:45:28,602
We're covering that side like we planned,
so they're not setting over there.

2554
01:45:28,825 --> 01:45:31,358
Their right-side attack is
pretty much shut down now.

2555
01:45:31,526 --> 01:45:32,659
They're playing with half the court.

2556
01:45:32,660 --> 01:45:34,327
Exactly. Just half the court.

2557
01:45:35,096 --> 01:45:36,863
(Meanwhile, on Lao Cai's side)

2558
01:45:41,169 --> 01:45:44,271
(A somber mood after losing Set One)

2559
01:45:46,007 --> 01:45:48,342
How can you mess up a free ball
when you're standing right there?

2560
01:45:48,343 --> 01:45:51,845
I don't know where your head is.

2561
01:45:53,181 --> 01:45:55,916
They barely attack through the middle.

2562
01:45:55,917 --> 01:45:58,786
We've hardly seen them go down the middle.

2563
01:46:02,190 --> 01:46:04,958
Get into that gap and cover it.

2564
01:46:07,395 --> 01:46:10,664
(Ready for attacks from the wings)

2565
01:46:10,898 --> 01:46:12,932
Yeon Joo has 6 points, 1 block,
and a 45 percent attack success rate.

2566
01:46:13,268 --> 01:46:15,135
Chae Rim has three blocks.

2567
01:46:15,136 --> 01:46:16,069
Seven points.

2568
01:46:16,604 --> 01:46:18,438
Min Kyeong has three points.

2569
01:46:18,639 --> 01:46:20,540
Min Kyeong's attack percentage needs
to go up.

2570
01:46:20,842 --> 01:46:23,276
Right. She needs to get into the mid-40s.

2571
01:46:23,277 --> 01:46:24,277
Look at the reception stats.

2572
01:46:24,846 --> 01:46:26,346
Min Kyeong's numbers aren't even there.

2573
01:46:27,648 --> 01:46:28,581
Zero percent.

2574
01:46:30,351 --> 01:46:31,318
I can do this.

2575
01:46:32,120 --> 01:46:33,320
I just need to loosen up.

2576
01:46:35,523 --> 01:46:36,623
Why is she so nervous?

2577
01:46:38,026 --> 01:46:39,493
She's over 30.

2578
01:46:39,660 --> 01:46:40,527
What is wrong with me?

2579
01:46:40,528 --> 01:46:43,296
I've had you practice reception
so many times.

2580
01:46:43,731 --> 01:46:45,432
Can you try to calm her down?

2581
01:46:46,567 --> 01:46:48,968
I have. I've told her over and over
to settle down.

2582
01:46:49,170 --> 01:46:51,204
But I think we're past that point now.

2583
01:46:52,073 --> 01:46:53,407
She's over 30, for crying out loud.

2584
01:46:54,709 --> 01:46:56,176
- You need to stay composed.
- Yes.

2585
01:46:56,177 --> 01:46:57,543
You're in too much of a hurry.

2586
01:46:57,544 --> 01:46:59,546
You're rushing, and you're all stiff.

2587
01:46:59,881 --> 01:47:02,082
Stay loose, but move quickly.

2588
01:47:02,583 --> 01:47:03,483
Are you nervous?

2589
01:47:03,484 --> 01:47:04,884
(Nodding)

2590
01:47:06,154 --> 01:47:07,788
It was my first time starting too.

2591
01:47:09,791 --> 01:47:10,624
Yes.

2592
01:47:12,593 --> 01:47:14,727
I know how much that chance means.

2593
01:47:18,032 --> 01:47:19,833
A blue-chip rookie prospect.

2594
01:47:20,668 --> 01:47:23,637
If she were still young and fully healthy,
she'd be an automatic draft pick.

2595
01:47:24,005 --> 01:47:26,873
At this point, though,
she's just a reminder of past potential.

2596
01:47:27,675 --> 01:47:31,511
I've always wished I could go back
to when I was healthy.

2597
01:47:33,614 --> 01:47:35,348
It hurt to think about.

2598
01:47:37,051 --> 01:47:37,984
Stretch it out.

2599
01:47:37,985 --> 01:47:40,286
(She kept pushing through rehab.)

2600
01:47:40,855 --> 01:47:44,657
Even when I was with Hyundai,
I barely got to play.

2601
01:47:46,194 --> 01:47:48,562
(It was the same with the Wonder Dogs.)

2602
01:47:49,964 --> 01:47:52,666
A player needs to be on the court,

2603
01:47:53,234 --> 01:47:55,202
but I hardly ever got to play.

2604
01:47:55,203 --> 01:47:56,837
(All she wanted was a chance to play.)

2605
01:47:56,838 --> 01:48:00,273
For today's starting lineup,

2606
01:48:00,274 --> 01:48:01,875
Min Kyeong is in.

2607
01:48:03,778 --> 01:48:05,112
(The moment she had waited so long for)

2608
01:48:05,113 --> 01:48:07,014
I'd wanted this chance so badly.

2609
01:48:10,151 --> 01:48:11,818
My bad.

2610
01:48:11,819 --> 01:48:13,520
I felt I had to prove myself.

2611
01:48:16,457 --> 01:48:17,390
(Her body won't cooperate.)

2612
01:48:17,391 --> 01:48:19,092
What's wrong with me? I'm losing it.

2613
01:48:19,293 --> 01:48:20,126
It's short!

2614
01:48:21,429 --> 01:48:23,997
(A chance she'd worked so hard for)

2615
01:48:23,998 --> 01:48:26,667
That was tough.

2616
01:48:44,585 --> 01:48:45,285
(Back on the bench)

2617
01:48:45,286 --> 01:48:46,986
Come on, why are you so nervous?

2618
01:48:46,987 --> 01:48:48,087
You stay on that bench.

2619
01:48:49,591 --> 01:48:53,527
I was just so frustrated with myself.

2620
01:48:53,528 --> 01:48:55,262
(In the end, she missed her chance.)

2621
01:48:56,531 --> 01:48:57,931
Why do you keep backing off?

2622
01:48:57,932 --> 01:48:59,500
- Why do you keep backing off?
- Because I'm scared.

2623
01:49:02,136 --> 01:49:05,205
(Min Kyeong returns to the warm-up zone.)

2624
01:49:05,772 --> 01:49:08,074
Relax. Just do what you always do.

2625
01:49:08,276 --> 01:49:10,777
(The Set Two timeout nears its end.)

2626
01:49:13,447 --> 01:49:14,280
Min Kyeong.

2627
01:49:14,982 --> 01:49:16,916
Get in there.

2628
01:49:19,220 --> 01:49:20,954
Wait, what?

2629
01:49:21,656 --> 01:49:23,257
- I think now's a good time.
- I think so too.

2630
01:49:23,258 --> 01:49:24,391
- Let's just do it now.
- Okay.

2631
01:49:24,959 --> 01:49:26,226
Let Min Kyeong get some rest.

2632
01:49:26,327 --> 01:49:29,195
She'll be going back in.

2633
01:49:30,064 --> 01:49:33,232
(They planned to put her back in.)

2634
01:49:33,233 --> 01:49:35,135
I guess I had faith in her.

2635
01:49:36,470 --> 01:49:37,370
I just have to do my part.

2636
01:49:38,573 --> 01:49:42,142
I loved her drive and how genuine she was.

2637
01:49:42,443 --> 01:49:43,877
I can't wait!

2638
01:49:44,078 --> 01:49:44,878
Cover!

2639
01:49:44,879 --> 01:49:47,747
(Her determination stood out at tryouts.)

2640
01:49:47,949 --> 01:49:51,818
If you hit as hard as you yell,
you'd be something else, Min Kyeong.

2641
01:49:51,886 --> 01:49:52,819
Yes, Coach.

2642
01:49:52,820 --> 01:49:55,422
I love how proactive she is.

2643
01:49:56,090 --> 01:49:57,724
(Min Kyeong, the Squawking Songbird)

2644
01:49:57,725 --> 01:49:59,059
There are plenty of talented players...

2645
01:49:59,060 --> 01:50:01,194
who just haven't had a chance.

2646
01:50:01,696 --> 01:50:02,863
Min Kyeong, it starts now.

2647
01:50:02,864 --> 01:50:04,464
It's okay. The rough start is
in the past now.

2648
01:50:05,199 --> 01:50:07,667
You're back. Feeling better now?

2649
01:50:08,202 --> 01:50:09,969
You got this.

2650
01:50:10,472 --> 01:50:13,907
- You got this!
- I went in like it was my last chance.

2651
01:50:14,075 --> 01:50:16,877
I want us to dig deeper and pull through.

2652
01:50:17,545 --> 01:50:18,612
Let's go!

2653
01:50:18,646 --> 01:50:21,948
(Like the cheer-loving squawker she is)

2654
01:50:21,949 --> 01:50:23,249
- Stay focused.
- Yes, Coach.

2655
01:50:23,250 --> 01:50:24,851
- Let's go!
- I've got to step up.

2656
01:50:24,852 --> 01:50:26,586
- Let's go!
- Let's go!

2657
01:50:26,587 --> 01:50:28,555
- Let's go again!
- Let's do it!

2658
01:50:28,556 --> 01:50:29,489
You got this.

2659
01:50:29,490 --> 01:50:30,490
Let's go for it.

2660
01:50:30,491 --> 01:50:31,658
(Back on court, fired up)

2661
01:50:31,659 --> 01:50:32,861
- Let's go!
- We need to serve.

2662
01:50:32,862 --> 01:50:34,261
It's our serve.

2663
01:50:37,199 --> 01:50:38,699
Serve to Zone One.

2664
01:50:38,700 --> 01:50:40,100
Hold your position.

2665
01:50:40,101 --> 01:50:41,101
- Serve to Zone One.
- Hold your position.

2666
01:50:41,369 --> 01:50:42,703
(Oops)

2667
01:50:44,805 --> 01:50:46,606
- Focus on yourself. Stop coaching.
- Yes, Coach.

2668
01:50:46,774 --> 01:50:47,807
Serve to Zone One.

2669
01:50:47,808 --> 01:50:49,108
(Stifled laughter)

2670
01:50:49,710 --> 01:50:52,512
(Embarrassed)

2671
01:50:53,914 --> 01:50:57,083
I have a real soft spot for Min Kyeong.

2672
01:50:57,918 --> 01:51:00,353
(Lao Cai prepares for attacks
from the wings.)

2673
01:51:00,620 --> 01:51:02,921
They give to Number 8 and Number 66 a lot.

2674
01:51:03,190 --> 01:51:04,590
- Wait a bit before you jump.
- Okay.

2675
01:51:07,295 --> 01:51:09,062
(Second set, Lao Cai 0 : Wonder Dogs 0)

2676
01:51:09,563 --> 01:51:10,997
(Hyo Rim serves.)

2677
01:51:11,599 --> 01:51:12,765
Set Two is underway.

2678
01:51:13,968 --> 01:51:16,536
- Wait on the block!
- One, two.

2679
01:51:17,338 --> 01:51:18,338
It's blocked!

2680
01:51:18,339 --> 01:51:19,739
- Okay!
- Good.

2681
01:51:19,806 --> 01:51:20,606
(Tsk tsk)

2682
01:51:20,842 --> 01:51:21,775
Free ball!

2683
01:51:23,311 --> 01:51:24,144
Kieu Oanh.

2684
01:51:24,145 --> 01:51:25,212
(Chae Rim digs it.)

2685
01:51:25,213 --> 01:51:26,680
Great diving dig by Chae Rim!

2686
01:51:26,681 --> 01:51:28,148
Hey, send it to C!

2687
01:51:31,452 --> 01:51:33,019
Good! Stay patient on the block.

2688
01:51:34,021 --> 01:51:35,288
- Swing!
- Hit it!

2689
01:51:35,289 --> 01:51:36,656
(A wall at the net)

2690
01:51:36,824 --> 01:51:37,857
Hit it!

2691
01:51:38,493 --> 01:51:40,827
Here comes Min Kyeong!

2692
01:51:40,828 --> 01:51:42,195
She scores!

2693
01:51:43,264 --> 01:51:45,332
- Nice!
- That's it!

2694
01:51:45,333 --> 01:51:47,534
- Good job!
- Nice set.

2695
01:51:49,503 --> 01:51:50,336
Hey!

2696
01:51:51,038 --> 01:51:55,408
They almost always hit cross-court.
Why are you blocking the other way?

2697
01:51:56,411 --> 01:51:59,879
That was a great attack by Min Kyeong.

2698
01:51:59,880 --> 01:52:04,184
She made contact high and placed it deep.

2699
01:52:04,985 --> 01:52:07,253
That's it, Min Kyeong!

2700
01:52:08,289 --> 01:52:09,356
Looking good, Min Kyeong!

2701
01:52:09,757 --> 01:52:11,257
- Good job!
- Thank you.

2702
01:52:11,258 --> 01:52:13,560
(Min Kyeong's confidence is up.)

2703
01:52:17,998 --> 01:52:19,265
(Serve target: Zone 4)

2704
01:52:19,266 --> 01:52:21,848
Number eight struggles with reception.

2705
01:52:21,849 --> 01:52:22,768
(Zone 4: Targeting Number 8)

2706
01:52:23,938 --> 01:52:26,106
(The server has her target in sight.)

2707
01:52:28,809 --> 01:52:29,909
It's 1 to 0.

2708
01:52:30,478 --> 01:52:31,845
(Hyo Rim's second serve)

2709
01:52:32,680 --> 01:52:33,813
It clips the net!

2710
01:52:38,018 --> 01:52:40,052
And it falls in!

2711
01:52:40,053 --> 01:52:41,787
(A service ace, right on target)

2712
01:52:42,056 --> 01:52:43,456
What was that?

2713
01:52:43,457 --> 01:52:44,457
An ace!

2714
01:52:44,458 --> 01:52:45,992
(Fidgeting nervously)

2715
01:52:46,127 --> 01:52:48,028
It's okay. Shake it off. Move on.

2716
01:52:48,196 --> 01:52:50,163
In their opener against Shujitsu,

2717
01:52:50,164 --> 01:52:52,265
they didn't get a single ace,

2718
01:52:52,266 --> 01:52:54,568
but against the Pink Spiders
and Pohang Sports Council,

2719
01:52:54,569 --> 01:52:56,870
- their serves helped them win.
- That's right.

2720
01:52:58,005 --> 01:52:59,138
It's 2 to 0.

2721
01:52:59,240 --> 01:53:01,041
Ye Dam, aim for Number eight.

2722
01:53:01,042 --> 01:53:02,676
Watch right in front of Number 22.

2723
01:53:04,111 --> 01:53:05,244
I've got to do this.

2724
01:53:06,914 --> 01:53:08,448
(Hyo Rim's third serve)

2725
01:53:10,217 --> 01:53:11,417
Their reception is shaky again.

2726
01:53:13,254 --> 01:53:14,321
(Kieu Oanh fires a powerful spike.)

2727
01:53:14,322 --> 01:53:15,188
The spike!

2728
01:53:15,323 --> 01:53:16,856
Yu Kyung with the dig!

2729
01:53:16,857 --> 01:53:17,757
Min Kyeong!

2730
01:53:19,894 --> 01:53:20,961
(The opponent braces...)

2731
01:53:20,962 --> 01:53:23,764
(for a cross-court attack.)

2732
01:53:24,231 --> 01:53:25,164
Min Kyeong!

2733
01:53:25,165 --> 01:53:27,099
Min Kyeong, one more!

2734
01:53:27,468 --> 01:53:30,804
I really thought this was my last chance.

2735
01:53:31,839 --> 01:53:33,506
(Squealing)

2736
01:53:33,507 --> 01:53:34,669
- You've got to make it happen.
- Finish it.

2737
01:53:34,670 --> 01:53:35,897
She goes for a tip...

2738
01:53:35,969 --> 01:53:36,869
and that's a point!

2739
01:53:37,111 --> 01:53:38,478
(Groaning)

2740
01:53:39,013 --> 01:53:40,146
(Squealing)

2741
01:53:40,414 --> 01:53:42,081
(Shouting)

2742
01:53:43,151 --> 01:53:45,185
- There you go!
- That's it!

2743
01:53:46,454 --> 01:53:47,354
Ji-Star!

2744
01:53:47,721 --> 01:53:49,255
- Let's go!
- That's it!

2745
01:53:49,256 --> 01:53:50,589
(Another point, with no sign of nerves)

2746
01:53:51,759 --> 01:53:53,393
- Nice!
- Good one.

2747
01:53:53,627 --> 01:53:56,195
Min Kyeong, that's it!

2748
01:53:56,730 --> 01:53:57,663
Got it!

2749
01:53:58,666 --> 01:54:00,233
(A slight smile)

2750
01:54:03,638 --> 01:54:06,672
I want to be a player
my team can count on.

2751
01:54:07,047 --> 01:54:10,911
I couldn't start
because I have shortcomings.

2752
01:54:11,364 --> 01:54:13,632
I'll work even harder.

2753
01:54:15,843 --> 01:54:18,945
(Working hard to rehabilitate her knee)

2754
01:54:19,119 --> 01:54:20,086
Mine!

2755
01:54:20,688 --> 01:54:22,822
- Sorry.
- If you call "Mine!" that loud,

2756
01:54:22,823 --> 01:54:23,823
you'd better make a good pass.

2757
01:54:23,824 --> 01:54:24,624
Yes, Coach.

2758
01:54:24,625 --> 01:54:26,359
If I were still healthy...

2759
01:54:26,360 --> 01:54:28,728
If I were still young...

2760
01:54:29,530 --> 01:54:32,532
(All she can do now is keep working.)

2761
01:54:32,766 --> 01:54:33,833
What were my reception stats?

2762
01:54:34,969 --> 01:54:37,037
(Reviewing the game afterward)

2763
01:54:37,338 --> 01:54:39,105
(Squawking Songbird mode on)

2764
01:54:39,240 --> 01:54:40,006
Again.

2765
01:54:40,007 --> 01:54:40,941
Can I give it one more try?

2766
01:54:40,942 --> 01:54:42,008
(Until she gets it right)

2767
01:54:42,810 --> 01:54:44,511
My foot is bleeding.

2768
01:54:46,748 --> 01:54:48,181
Take it slow.

2769
01:54:49,717 --> 01:54:53,320
I don't want to be a player who says
I can't play because of an injury.

2770
01:54:53,587 --> 01:54:57,323
I want to show I can still play,
even with an injury.

2771
01:55:01,128 --> 01:55:02,328
- There you go.
- A tempo attack.

2772
01:55:03,230 --> 01:55:04,764
They kept that one alive together.

2773
01:55:05,332 --> 01:55:06,198
Send it to C!

2774
01:55:06,534 --> 01:55:07,367
Mine!

2775
01:55:07,654 --> 01:55:08,721
We need to finish it!

2776
01:55:09,042 --> 01:55:10,843
- Good.
- You've got to get that!

2777
01:55:13,774 --> 01:55:14,906
(She gets another chance.)

2778
01:55:16,723 --> 01:55:20,893
I used to worry
about how my knee would hold up that day.

2779
01:55:21,127 --> 01:55:24,463
Now I love being able to play
without worrying about it.

2780
01:55:25,866 --> 01:55:28,400
(Looking back on her return to the court)

2781
01:55:28,401 --> 01:55:30,002
I feel like I'm finding my form again.

2782
01:55:31,123 --> 01:55:33,257
Min Kyeong times that hit perfectly!

2783
01:55:33,272 --> 01:55:34,740
She spikes it down the line.

2784
01:55:34,934 --> 01:55:36,201
(Cheering)

2785
01:55:36,342 --> 01:55:37,442
Nice!

2786
01:55:37,443 --> 01:55:39,411
- There you go!
- Way to go!

2787
01:55:40,146 --> 01:55:41,780
(Rediscovering the thrill of scoring)

2788
01:55:41,781 --> 01:55:43,382
- All right!
- Way to go!

2789
01:55:44,150 --> 01:55:46,752
Min Kyeong is finally coming alive!

2790
01:55:47,453 --> 01:55:50,121
(She can soar again.)

2791
01:55:50,122 --> 01:55:51,656
Min Kyeong!

2792
01:55:52,458 --> 01:55:53,658
Nice one!

2793
01:55:54,026 --> 01:55:54,959
That's it!

2794
01:55:55,928 --> 01:55:57,462
Nice, Min Kyeong!

2795
01:55:57,463 --> 01:55:59,364
Good job, Min Kyeong!

2796
01:55:59,365 --> 01:56:00,365
- Nice one.
- Good job!

2797
01:56:00,366 --> 01:56:04,469
I was so grateful they trusted me
and waited for me.

2798
01:56:05,472 --> 01:56:08,372
Min Kyeong was a standout prospect.

2799
01:56:08,373 --> 01:56:09,541
She sure was.

2800
01:56:10,676 --> 01:56:13,578
She's finally gotten past the injury
that held her back,

2801
01:56:13,813 --> 01:56:14,446
(Roaring)

2802
01:56:15,448 --> 01:56:16,748
and she's giving it her all.

2803
01:56:16,749 --> 01:56:17,949
(The Wonder Dogs bought...)

2804
01:56:20,453 --> 01:56:21,720
Nice, Min Kyeong!

2805
01:56:21,721 --> 01:56:23,288
(a blue-chip volleyball prospect
on the dips.)

2806
01:56:24,123 --> 01:56:25,990
(Second set, Lao Cai 1 : Wonder Dogs 5)

2807
01:56:26,959 --> 01:56:28,426
It's a slow one.

2808
01:56:29,495 --> 01:56:30,495
Watch for the short serve.

2809
01:56:30,696 --> 01:56:32,563
- Let's go!
- Okay!

2810
01:56:32,798 --> 01:56:34,398
- Min Kyeong, just tap it.
- Okay.

2811
01:56:34,400 --> 01:56:36,335
(Time to pull ahead)

2812
01:56:40,373 --> 01:56:41,206
- Good.
- That's it.

2813
01:56:41,207 --> 01:56:42,140
Middle!

2814
01:56:42,141 --> 01:56:43,642
- Send it to C!
- C!

2815
01:56:43,643 --> 01:56:44,409
(Left side)

2816
01:56:44,410 --> 01:56:45,844
(The defenders hesitate.)

2817
01:56:45,845 --> 01:56:46,378
(Whoosh)

2818
01:56:47,246 --> 01:56:48,846
- A back set.
- Good.

2819
01:56:48,847 --> 01:56:49,747
One more!

2820
01:56:50,483 --> 01:56:52,284
(They fell for it!)

2821
01:56:52,418 --> 01:56:53,651
- Yeon Joo!
- Yeon Joo!

2822
01:56:53,652 --> 01:56:55,053
(A solo-block chance for Yeon Joo)

2823
01:56:56,989 --> 01:56:58,323
Yeon Joo!

2824
01:56:58,324 --> 01:56:59,257
(She hammers it down.)

2825
01:56:59,258 --> 01:57:00,224
Okay!

2826
01:57:00,326 --> 01:57:01,459
- That's it!
- All right!

2827
01:57:02,596 --> 01:57:03,862
Nice!

2828
01:57:04,397 --> 01:57:05,665
Man...

2829
01:57:05,666 --> 01:57:07,065
The Wonder Dogs are on a roll!

2830
01:57:07,200 --> 01:57:08,233
What's gotten into them?

2831
01:57:09,268 --> 01:57:11,970
Their attacks are leaving us speechless.

2832
01:57:11,971 --> 01:57:12,871
That's right.

2833
01:57:12,872 --> 01:57:15,240
At this rate, Lao Cai's defenders...

2834
01:57:15,241 --> 01:57:18,176
won't know where to position themselves.

2835
01:57:18,177 --> 01:57:19,244
(The Deer covers the right side.)

2836
01:57:19,579 --> 01:57:20,579
Darn it.

2837
01:57:20,900 --> 01:57:22,534
It's 6 to 1, a 5-point lead.

2838
01:57:22,548 --> 01:57:23,682
(Second set, Lao Cai 1 : Wonder Dogs 6)

2839
01:57:24,651 --> 01:57:26,984
Lao Cai has no choice...

2840
01:57:26,985 --> 01:57:30,388
but to keep going with high balls
for offense.

2841
01:57:30,389 --> 01:57:33,825
The Wonder Dogs are serving so well,

2842
01:57:33,826 --> 01:57:36,629
and Lao Cai is struggling to receive.

2843
01:57:36,630 --> 01:57:39,831
Even Coach Nguyen looks thrown off.

2844
01:57:39,832 --> 01:57:41,766
And who can blame him?

2845
01:57:42,201 --> 01:57:45,403
Now let's see how he adjusts.

2846
01:57:45,939 --> 01:57:50,542
Coach Kim's strategy worked really well.

2847
01:57:50,543 --> 01:57:55,413
They played fast, and their serves were
especially tough.

2848
01:57:55,414 --> 01:57:58,784
So when our middle blocker couldn't
do her job...

2849
01:57:59,118 --> 01:58:02,387
Warm up.

2850
01:58:02,841 --> 01:58:05,309
We'd make it tough for the other team.

2851
01:58:06,158 --> 01:58:07,158
(Here she comes.)

2852
01:58:14,300 --> 01:58:16,034
We're just getting started.

2853
01:58:21,273 --> 01:58:23,341
I subbed in Ly Thi Luyen.

2854
01:58:23,342 --> 01:58:26,244
Coach Nguyen has brought in...

2855
01:58:26,245 --> 01:58:29,213
Luyen, who stands 195 cm tall.

2856
01:58:29,214 --> 01:58:31,115
- Is she finally coming in?
- Yes.

2857
01:58:31,684 --> 01:58:33,385
Now they have to take her on.

2858
01:58:33,386 --> 01:58:35,187
- Exactly.
- Come on, let's go!

2859
01:58:37,156 --> 01:58:40,592
Oh, right. This is bad.

2860
01:58:41,160 --> 01:58:42,560
Luyen, watch carefully.

2861
01:58:42,561 --> 01:58:45,130
Once they serve, move out
and get ready to block.

2862
01:58:48,934 --> 01:58:52,103
I thought, "Wait, she's really tall."

2863
01:58:52,471 --> 01:58:53,738
It caught me a little off guard.

2864
01:58:55,141 --> 01:58:58,510
I thought she'd finally come in.

2865
01:58:59,418 --> 01:59:01,620
This could become a tough match.

2866
01:59:02,181 --> 01:59:05,316
It actually motivated me.

2867
01:59:06,672 --> 01:59:10,582
(The Wall vs. Ye Dam)

2868
01:59:10,590 --> 01:59:12,457
I'll give it a shot.

2869
01:59:16,770 --> 01:59:19,505
(The aerial assault begins.)

2870
01:59:20,868 --> 01:59:24,404
(An impenetrable wall at 195 cm tall)

2871
01:59:24,412 --> 01:59:27,247
At 195 cm, Luyen is a real threat.

2872
01:59:30,784 --> 01:59:33,886
Why are you so scared?
Swing hard when you have the chance!

2873
01:59:33,887 --> 01:59:36,055
A spike and she scores!

2874
01:59:37,591 --> 01:59:40,226
You can hit that harder.
Why are you holding back?

2875
01:59:40,227 --> 01:59:42,662
Get a good set up!
What do you mean, a mistake?

2876
01:59:42,963 --> 01:59:44,897
What do you mean, a mistake?

2877
01:59:45,366 --> 01:59:48,407
(Two legends, alike but different)

2878
01:59:49,737 --> 01:59:52,105
(The two coaches go head-to-head.)

2879
01:59:52,973 --> 01:59:54,087
(The Wonder Coach 2)

2880
01:59:54,088 --> 01:59:55,542
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
